articles.body:
3zPz led Historical [UEZ], one of only two [[concordia|Concordia]] member guilds known by name.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L133, L200–201}}

He took Historical out of Concordia and into [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], and on 8 November 2015 posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded"; it drew 27 replies and 4,049 views, was locked, and was last posted in by Ferne on 10 November 2015.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|Alliance-prefix thread index}} [[ezura|Ezura]] of [[validus|Validus]] contested the disbandment in the thread, without changing how it was read.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L203–204}}

A month later he founded [[vesta|Vesta]] out of what Concordia left behind, opening its alliance thread on 10 December 2015.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}} Vesta was the larger alliance at the time it formed — fourteen guilds against Ordo's dozen — and is remembered chiefly for having done nothing.

Aequitas [Aeq] is a Wynncraft guild created on 24 Nov 2019.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## Leadership and structure

The guild's forum recruitment thread was opened on 3 Jan 2021 by [[frozengalaxy|FrozenGalaxy]] and has been maintained by him since. Aequitas runs a courtroom-themed rank ladder - Justices, Judges, Attorneys, Advocates, Jury, Witnesses - at the top of which the thread lists 'Justice Frozenman [OWNER]' and 'Justice Lalatera [CHIEF]'; Lalatera also drew the guild's artwork, and recruitment ran through peter3536.{{cite:thread-280525|post #1, opened 3 Jan 2021}} Two weeks after opening the thread, on 17 Jan 2021, FrozenGalaxy added the guild to [[the-forum-megalist|the forum megalist]] as a level 48 community and war guild.{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #66, 17 Jan 2021}}

The bar for entry rose as the guild did. In January 2021 the form asked players above level 70 whether they would help war, and within two days put the same question to players above 95{{cite:thread-280525-p02|#21, 24 Jan 2021, and #24, 26 Jan 2021, reproducing the application form}}. By December 2022 it carried a formal combat-level minimum of 80 and addressed warring to players above 100{{cite:thread-280525-p20|#381, 19 Dec 2022, reproducing the form}}. The minimum moved three times after that: 75 from May 2023{{cite:thread-280525-p22|#421, 24 May 2023, reproducing the form}}, 90 from August 2024{{cite:thread-280525-p24|#472, 30 Aug 2024, reproducing the form}}, and 100 by March 2025{{cite:thread-280525-p25|#491, 9 Mar 2025, reproducing the form. Applicants sometimes copied a superseded version, so each date is a requirement's first appearance rather than the day it was set}}.

The thread's header reads 'Est. November 24th 2019',{{cite:thread-280525|post #1, opened 3 Jan 2021}} matching the API's creation date:{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Aequitas was a year old before it began recruiting publicly.

## History

### Goose and Khaos (2021-2022)

Aequitas belonged to [[Goose]] among the coalition's later additions by 30 Mar 2021, when [[drasalia|Drasalia]]'s Goose fanart thread drew it as a blindfolded Greek figure - 'their name is the Latin concept of justice, equality' - and both Lalatera and FrozenGalaxy replied.{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}} Aequitas also had a brief [[Artemis]] stint in the war's final week (early May 2021) while still with Goose; the overlap was never explained.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} At [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021 Aequitas co-founded [[Khaos]] with the Goose bloc's core, fighting the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war against Valhalla and Vanir]] that peaked in January 2022;{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Khaos was defunct by 26 Jun 2022 and its guilds were absorbed into [[Cucumber Company]].{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}

### The super-alliance years (2022-2023)

Aequitas appears in Cucumber Company's 14-guild megalist roster of 26 Jun 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} and carried through into [[smtn elf]] until the alliance's quiet end in mid-2023.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In September 2023 'TNL and AEQ were allied and warring together'{{cite:thread-280525-p22|p22 #427, 1 Sep 2023}} - the only named guild relationship of its era.

### The Long Raid and the great wars (2024-2026)

In late July 2024 Aequitas's claim in the Sky province endured [[the-long-raid|a roughly week-long siege]], recounted in the video 'Wynncraft Warring - The Long Raid' (premiered 4 Aug 2024).{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-rlrh14ns6ok|premiered 4 Aug 2024}}{{cite:thread-318070|post #1, 9 Aug 2024}} The attackers were never named. From 3 Nov to 21 Dec 2025 Aequitas fought [[Avicia]] in [[aequitas-avicia-war|the largest war ever recorded]] (15,710 territory exchanges).{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} After a one-week clash in August 2025 and spring 2026 skirmishes, [[aequitas-sequoia-war|full war with Sequoia]] erupted in the week of 24 Aug 2026 - 7,488 territory exchanges in its first week,{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-aequitas|territory count, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} That war is ongoing.

![The in-game guild leaderboard for Season 23, which ended 13 April 2025: Aequitas second on 11,082,978 Season Rating behind Sequoia, ahead of Empire of TKW, TruthSworD, Avicia and Titans Valor. Published in Titan Times vol. 19, 2 August 2025.](/images/chronicles/media/aequitas-b0ea886d.webp){{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol19|vol. 19, 2 Aug 2025}}

## Alliances

- [[Goose]] - by 30 Mar 2021 - 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}}
- [[Artemis]] - early May 2021 - 11 May 2021 (brief overlapping stint, never explained)
- [[Khaos]] - 11 May 2021 - defunct by 26 Jun 2022 (co-founder)
- [[Cucumber Company]] - spring 2022 - Sep 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}
- [[smtn elf]] - Sep 2022 - Jun 2023

## History

### Formation
The pact was created on 25 March 2018 by [[Fantasy]], Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team as a bond of sister guilds within the map-dominant Federation.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} [[DiamondDeities]] was accepted into the pact on 18 July 2018.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} The pact's thread, posted by the Sins of Seedia leader lotuss on 5 June 2018, described Aesir as "an alliance, or if you will sister-ship pact, between 4 warring and growing community guilds". Fantasy and Sins of Seedia became friends during the War Syndicate era, were separated when Fantasy entered the [[Coalition]] and Sins of Seedia warred against it, and were reunited inside [[the-federation|the Federation]], where IceBlue Team and then DiamondDeities were added.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

### Leadership
Each member guild was represented by two leaders.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

| Guild | Tag | Leaders |
|---|---|---|
| [[Fantasy]] | Fux | [[viaire|Viaire]], SpaseCow |
| Sins of Seedia | SDU | [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]], Shy_Phoenix |
| IceBlue Team | IBT | [[vmark03|Vmark03]], Mpr100 |
| [[DiamondDeities]] | DDT | [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], Icey_Diamond |

New guilds were admitted by a vote of these leaders; the thread advised applicants to form friendships with them first "(for voting process)".{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} Several of the same names recur in the Federation's leadership: [[Drew1011]] credited simplyinfinity_ as the first to accept the merger proposal that created the Federation, called Viaire "perhaps the best mapmaker the alliance had", and counted Nitrogen2Oxygen and Icey_Diamond among its most trusted friends.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

### The Fantasy anomaly
Fantasy was an Aesir founder, yet waged war on the Federation itself from May to October 2018, a conflict in which more than 220 territories were exchanged.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The pact survived Fantasy's exit from the Federation: Fantasy's Aesir membership ran unbroken from the founding to the end.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} How the pact reconciled the two was never recorded.

### The last defence
When the Federation began to cascade apart on 10 Nov 2018, the Aesir guilds — Sins of Seedia, DiamondDeities and IceBlue Team — were its last defenders, quitting only after 14 hours of constant warring{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}} as [[the-federation-dies|the Federation fell]] on 10–11 November 2018. The community timeline records: "At this point Aesir died too."{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Aesir Pact}}

## Legacy
The pact never existed apart from the Federation: it formed inside the bloc and ended at the hour of its fall. Its guilds scattered into the post-Federation world — DiamondDeities into [[SOL]] within weeks, while IceBlue Team and Fantasy resurfaced in [[Terra]] during the wars of 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Angry_will was Emperator of the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] when the alliance fell on 17 October 2017, the date its thread's opening post was last rewritten to name him.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}} He held the office the day after [[drew1011|Drew1011]] held it for a single day; the sequence was never explained.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's forum profile title chain, 2016–2019}}

At the fall, Drew1011 was Shadow Advisor and [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] was among the alliance's four remaining member guilds.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}

He had stood for the Shadow Advisor post earlier that year. On 31 August 2017 [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] asked the alliance to choose between Shy_Phoenix, Angry_will, Drew1011 and Whimsicality; the tallies were 4, 5, 19 and 4.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|Shadow Advisor poll screenshot dated 08/31/2017, part 12}}

## History

### Founding
Artemis was formed on 30 October 2019, in the aftermath of the [[Terra]] bloc's fall, by [[Imperial]], [[Paladins United]] and Caeruleum Order.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} On 10 November 2019 fragments of the collapsed Terra launched a final raid on the newborn alliance. Nightingales and Phantom Hearts joined within days of the founding.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

No founding announcement was ever posted, and the founder guilds' own leadership at that moment is known only in fragments. Caeruleum Order — founded on 10 September 2018 and self-described as "a democratic, fully parliamentary guild" — was run by a four-member Caeruleum Parliament of MultiSmith, 1917Lenin1917, StormPh0enix and StarlyNight.{{cite:thread-254001|post #1, MultiSmith}} The guild passed from [[Luna]] to Artemis; its recruitment thread still read "We are a part of the Luna Alliance" while listing "Artemis Alliance" as the current bloc.{{cite:thread-254001|post #1, MultiSmith}} Carrie spoke for Paladins United in the same period.{{cite:thread-263975-p03|p3 #41, 9 Mar 2020}}

### The 2020 transformation
No Artemis membership list was published between November 2019 and December 2020, and the alliance that emerged from that gap looked very different from the one that entered it. By 9 March 2020 [[Kingdom Foxes]] was a member{{cite:thread-263975|9 Mar 2020}}, and [[ShadowFall]] held a leadership seat: on that day [[goulartjj|GoulartJJ]] posted "as the Shadow Fall leader and one of Artemis leaders", defending the alliance against the charge that it froze small guilds out.{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} ShadowFall, he wrote, had grown to "level 20ish by August of last year" through free-for-all territory grinding after "we tried joining Luna when we were leveling but got denied", and he set out the alliance's two working rules: "Guilds who are with big claims are the guilds who have contributed the most to the alliance", and "Guilds may also apply to Artemis by contacting one of the guild leaders, and possibly be accepted."{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} By 2 December 2020 the [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] described Artemis as "(war alliance) made up of all the current massive land holding guilds on the map", naming [[Titans Valor]] as a member.{{cite:thread-278112|post #10, 2 Dec 2020}}

The founders, meanwhile, had drifted out: by 18 December 2020 both Paladins United and Imperial stood with the unnamed anti-Artemis coalition that would take the name [[Goose]].{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} When and why they left was never recorded; their departures appear to have come near the start of December 2020, when that coalition's war on the Artemis core ignited.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### The Goose war and collapse
From December 2020 Artemis defended its map dominance in the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]]. The bleed of members continued into the new year — "BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now", a megalist post recorded on 1 February 2021, marking ShadowFall's switch to the enemy.{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} On 25 January 2021 the two blocs jointly granted [[Profession Heaven]] neutral status as a public profession-XP guild.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Artemis guilds were still warring the Rymek area held by Rays in February 2021{{cite:thread-286375|post #2, 20 Feb 2021}}, and took late reinforcements — Sins of Seedia in March 2021, [[Aequitas]] and Wheres The Finish in early May — but on 11 May 2021 Artemis and Goose collapsed on the same day.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

## Membership
Several membership dates are "by" dates rather than exact joins. The roster between November 2019 and December 2020 was never published.

{{alliance:Artemis}}

## Legacy
Artemis gave its name to the [[artemis-goose-era|Artemis-Goose era]]. Its final membership fed both successor blocs of [[the-great-collapse|The Great Collapse]]: Titans Valor went into [[Valhalla]], while the late joiners Aequitas and Wheres The Finish co-founded [[Khaos]] the same day.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The joint protection of Profession Heaven outlived both blocs, maintained by their successors until 2026.

Avicia [AVO] is a Wynncraft guild created on 1 Aug 2018.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-avicia|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Its tag is an acronym of the Latin phrase "amor vincit omnia", "love conquers all".{{cite:thread-233859|post #1}}

## History

### Founding and leadership

Avicia was founded by birdiefly209, who led it as "Grand Avis" over a High Council of a High Archon and about a dozen Archons.{{cite:thread-233859|post #1}} On 1 Dec 2018 birdiefly209 posted on the guild's thread: "I have stepped down from my role as Guild Master and passed the position on to Norgari."{{cite:thread-233859|post #16, 1 Dec 2018}} The succession of later leaders was never published: [[urbymine]] was a former Chief by February 2021,{{cite:thread-286375|post #5, 20 Feb 2021}} and FlamingoBike held the Chief title in April 2020.{{cite:thread-265297-p02|p2 #30, 12 Apr 2020}} Which of them held the office during the guild's August 2019 revolt against [[Luna]] is not recorded.

### The Luna era (2019)

During [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the alliance wars of 2019]], when [[Luna]] wiped every other guild from the map, Avicia was the last power standing; by joining Luna on 17 Jul 2019 it completed Luna's full map control.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Six weeks later, on 29 Aug 2019, Avicia and [[Emorians]] left after a leadership dispute and declared war on [[Imperial]], spiralling into a large war over Gavel out of which [[Terra]] emerged.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Goose, Valhalla and Vanir (2020-2021)

Avicia belonged to the anti-[[Artemis]] coalition of 18 Dec 2020{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} that became [[Goose]] — 'BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now', Avicia's own urbymine wrote on 1 Feb 2021{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} — and stayed until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, when it co-founded [[Valhalla]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It also belonged to the community alliance [[Niflheim]] by July 2021.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} On 28 Nov 2021 it followed Valhalla into [[Vanir]] — and on 18 Dec 2021 it was one of the four guilds whose departure collapsed it, the same day Niflheim dissolved.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Super-alliances and the Avocado split (2022-2024)

Avicia joined [[Cucumber Company]] for Season 5 of 2022 and carried through into [[smtn elf]],{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} while also joining the community alliance [[Adonis]] by 12 Jun 2022.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol3|vol. 3, 12 Jun 2022}} In June 2023 it quit smtn elf with [[The Aquarium]] over claim-shrinking pressure;{{cite:thread-308780|Avicia guild season post, 10 Jun 2023}} the pair fought on as the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact into early 2024.{{cite:thread-310286|Avicia guild season post, 19 Aug 2023}} From 30 Oct 2023 Avicia waged [[avicia-sequoia-war|war on the young Sequoia]], with a second round in January 2024.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### The Aequitas war (2025)

From 3 Nov to 21 Dec 2025 Avicia fought [[Aequitas]] in [[aequitas-avicia-war|the largest war in the entire territory record]] — 15,710 territory exchanges, with a weekly peak of 4,736.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} It was over by Christmas.

## Alliances

- [[Luna]] — 17 Jul 2019 – 29 Aug 2019
- [[Goose]] — by 18 Dec 2020 – 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}
- [[Niflheim]] — by 7 Jul 2021 – 18 Dec 2021 (community alliance){{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}}
- [[Valhalla]] — 11 May 2021 – 28 Nov 2021 (founding member)
- [[Vanir]] — 28 Nov 2021 – 18 Dec 2021
- [[Cucumber Company]] — spring 2022 – Sep 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}
- [[Adonis]] — by 12 Jun 2022 – Mar 2024 (last recorded; community alliance){{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol3|vol. 3, 12 Jun 2022}}
- [[smtn elf]] — Sep 2022 – Jun 2023
- [[Avocado Aquarium]] — Jun 2023 – Feb 2024

## History
The name was never written down while the pact existed.{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony of Cameron, a TAq veteran}} After [[the-avocado-split|the Avocado split]] of June 2023, in which the two guilds rejected pressure to shrink their territorial claims and walked out of [[smtn elf]], they ran a joint campaign against their ex-allies; [[Avicia]]'s Season 13 post of 19 August 2023 calls [[The Aquarium]] “our unwavering ally and neighbour”.{{cite:thread-310286|Avicia Season 13 post, 19 Aug 2023}}

The pact ran shared infrastructure. The joint subguild Avoquarium [HQs] was created on 9 August 2023{{cite:wynncraft-api|official Wynncraft API guild record for Avoquarium (HQs)}} — Avicia's June season post already thanks its allies “for the hqs”{{cite:thread-308780|Avicia Season 12 post, 10 Jun 2023}} — alongside the subguilds [[ShadowFall]] (The Aquarium's) and the Avos (Avicia's), across which the pair ran mega-claims. During the pact Avicia also fought the rising [[Sequoia]] in the [[avicia-sequoia-war|Avicia-Sequoia war]] (October–November 2023, with a second round in January 2024).{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

No formal end was ever recorded. The joint campaign ran into early 2024{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony of Cameron, a TAq veteran}}, fading out around February 2024.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The first friction between the two guilds themselves came in June 2024, after the pact had lapsed.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Avocado Aquarium}}

## Legacy
Avocado Aquarium is emblematic of the [[private-diplomacy-era|private-diplomacy era]]: a consequential alliance whose very name was never written down while it existed. Within months of its fade its members stood at the center of the era's biggest wars — The Aquarium against [[Idiot Co]] in the [[idiot-co-aquarium-war|Idiot Co-Aquarium war]] from April 2024.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

[[neonrider|NeonRider]] and [[naraka00|Naraka00]] founded the guild on 19 January 2016{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-blacklisted|creation date 19 Jan 2016, retrieved 3 Sep 2026}}{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}}, and it spent 2016 and 2017 as the third partner of the unnamed bloc that held most of the territory map with [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[libertas|Libertas]].

## History

### The pirate guild and the Hax bloc

The 2016 thread is pirate-themed from its first line — "Yo-ho-ho. We are Blacklisted, a guild of friends who aim to claim ultimate victory!" — and locates the guild geographically: "The Capital is Selchar and our territory is composed by the great ocean islands, where plenty of booty is to be found!"{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} It recruited at level 80 and above and ran a weekly war night, "Treasure Thursday", with "a special prize (5 unidentified legendaries) for the person who gets more territories".{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}}

Under a heading "ALLIANCES AND ALLIES" the same post declared: "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} No other member guild ever wrote the arrangement down. Outsiders described the same bloc: "They work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories", a poster objected in August 2016{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, 9 Aug 2016}}, and a Hax veteran wrote four years later, "didnt yall work with BLA and Lir for a lot of it".{{cite:thread-263975-p02|post #31, 9 Mar 2020}} The bloc had no name at the time; the label "Hax & Co" was attached to it later, in 2019.{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}} On 23 September 2016 Blacklisted held 22 of the map's roughly 332 territories at guild level 51 with 56 members — fourth behind Hax's 146, [[libertas|Libertas]]' 60 and [[ultimatexeons|UltimateXeons]]' 53.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}

The terms of its membership were argued in public in October 2016. Love_You_Buddy, who identified himself as a Beasts co-leader and a former Libertas co-leader, wrote that "Blacklisted is a funny joke. Hax only uses you for Ocean territories... BLA may have power now, but they won't for long", the ocean being worth "no xp".{{cite:thread-153722-p03|posts #49 and #52, 16 Oct 2016}} Tomix answered for the bloc: "We are not allied with Blacklisted to use them... they said that they want only ocean and they are ok with having only ocean … we 'gave' it to them to control it. And the thing with ocean giving 'no xp' isn't true."{{cite:thread-153722-p04|post #62, 20 Oct 2016}}

In March 2017 a defender of Hax still counted the guild among the map's holders, asking critics "are Lir, BLA, UXs somehow exempt?"{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}} [[neonrider|NeonRider]] replied in the same thread with a deflation: "It's cute that you guys think that my guild is super op but in reality it's only me doing wars and we're down to 1.7mil emeralds."{{cite:thread-179383|post #18, 2 Mar 2017}}

### After the bloc

A second recruitment thread was opened on 21 February 2018, the week [[hackforums|HackForums]] lost the last of its territories.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-54-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Blacklisted, milo890, 21 Feb 2018}} It names a third leader — "the leaders are @NeonRider, @Naraka00, and I", written by milo890 — and drops the alliance section entirely, describing a guild fighting on its own account: "Currently, we are an actively warring guild. Our wars mostly take place in Ragni and Dernal Jungle areas."{{cite:thread-219617|post #1, as last revised 29 Aug 2019}}

Blacklisted was a member of [[luna|Luna]] from 14 February to 19 September 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It was among the first guilds to change sides in that year's wars: after a failed raid, "two significant allies, Blacklisted and BuildCraftia, defected to [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]]'s side", joining the counter-offensive before their own territories were attacked in turn.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” to “THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} Where it stood in 2020 was unclear even to contemporaries: asked to lay out the alliance map that April, one poster could only offer "then there's Sentinels who has Lxt and BLA I guess?"{{cite:thread-266020|post #2, 12 Apr 2020}} It joined [[cucumber-company|Cucumber Company]] from 1 April to 25 September 2022{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, then [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]] until 30 June 2023.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} As of September 2026 the guild stands at level 78 with 30 members, no territories and 11,354 lifetime wars under the owner _Catastrophic_; when the war counter began counting was never documented.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-blacklisted|level, members, territories, war count and owner, retrieved 3 Sep 2026}}

## Alliances

- Unnamed bloc with [[hackforums|HackForums]] and [[libertas|Libertas]] — active 2016 – Mar 2017{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}}{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, 9 Aug 2016}}{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}}
- [[luna|Luna]] — 14 Feb 2019 – 19 Sep 2019{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}
- [[cucumber-company|Cucumber Company]] — 1 Apr 2022 – 25 Sep 2022{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}
- [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]] — 25 Sep 2022 – 30 Jun 2023{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Chownick founded TheNoLifes [TNL] on 27 December 2014, days after the guild system was introduced, making it one of the oldest guilds in the game.{{cite:thread-306694|post #1 (OP)}}

He was still the guild's owner in 2017, when TheNoLifes joined the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]: the alliance thread's roster lists "The No Lifes (TNL) - Owner: chownick" among its twelve member guilds, beside [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] under [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] and [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] under simplyinfinity_{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster, 7 May 2017}}.

He also belonged to the Ordo Malleus circle of the mid-2010s. Replying to the Federation Tribute on 13 November 2018 with "ordo buddies"{{cite:thread-237070|post #5, 13 Nov 2018}}, he drew from [[drew1011|Drew1011]] the answer "Once an Ordo brother always an Ordo brother."{{cite:thread-237070|post #6, 13 Nov 2018}}

TheNoLifes long outlasted his tenure — recorded switching to [[goose|Goose]] in February 2021{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} and inside [[niflheim|Niflheim]] that July{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} — but no source records when or how Chownick left its leadership.

## History

### Formation
The Council formed on 15 Sep 2019, a week after [[Terra]] took the map from [[Luna]], by seven guilds: [[Kingdom Foxes]], [[DiamondDeities]], [[Titans Valor]], [[The Simple Ones]], [[Fantasy]], Phantom Hearts and Empire of Sindria.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|15 Sep 2019 entry}} Five had fought with Terra. Kingdom Foxes had co-founded Luna in February and did not leave it until 18 September, three days after the Council was founded, so the alliance spanned both sides of the war it followed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|14 Feb, 15 Sep and 18 Sep 2019 entries}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Course
Phantom Hearts left the Council around 1 October 2019{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}, and went on to join [[Artemis]] on 4 Nov. TheNoLifes joined on 29 Sep, BlueStoneGroup on 11 Oct and Vindicator on 15 Oct, bringing the Council to its peak of nine concurrent members.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Kingdom Foxes departed on 2 Nov, the day Terra formally fell.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2 Nov 2019 entry}}

### Collapse
The Council collapsed on 23 Nov 2019 after The Ascendancy bloc departed, two days after Titans Valor and DiamondDeities left.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The Ascendancy — created 27 Apr 2019{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} — never published a roster. A week later, on 1 Dec, DiamondDeities, Titans Valor and The Simple Ones regrouped as [[Horologium]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

