## Legacy
The Council was the first of the short-lived successor blocs that followed the [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|Alliance Wars of 2019]] — none of Terra's heirs held together for more than a few months, and the map stabilized only with [[Artemis]]'s rise from 30 Oct 2019. Its own direct successor, Horologium, lasted five weeks.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

{{map:2018-01-07|The earliest weeks of the recorded territory map, days after the era's close}}

The early guild era is the least documented period of Wynncraft guild warfare: the continuous territory-exchange log begins only on 3 January 2018, no exchange-level war data was ever published for the years before it{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}, and the era is documented mainly by forum threads, a community-maintained timeline{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Wynncraft guild history timeline, community document}}, a first-person memoir written between 2018 and 2021 by [[drew1011|Drew1011]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|composed 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}}, and two captures of the guild leaderboard{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 16 Apr 2018}}.

## The first guilds (December 2014 – 2015)

Guilds and guild wars arrived together in [[the-guild-update|the Guild Update]] — version 1.13, the "Wynnter Update" of 22 December 2014{{cite:https://wynncraft.fandom.com/wiki/Version_1.13|Version 1.13 — Wynncraft Wiki}}. The first foundings came that same week: Holders Of LE [HoL] by PillowPet and Nethers Ascent [TNA] by Francis12qwasyx on 21 December, Kingdom Foxes [Fox] registered in-game by [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]] on 22 December, Kangronomicon [Fuq] on 23 December, and [[HackForums]] [Hax] by [[thedarksoul|TheDarkSoul]] on 24 December.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2014 entries}} Kingdom Foxes had existed as "the first 'guild'" since 2 June 2014, six months before the mechanic{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jun 2014 entry}}. Holders of LE described itself as "Founded upon the advent of the official release of guilds"{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}, and PillowPet was still a chief of it in 2018{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}. [[Imperial]] followed on 14 January 2015 under darkbio99 and KnightOfValor [KnV] on 16 January under Nozomi.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jan 2015 entries}}

The first alliance was **Legio Praetoria**, founded in early March 2015 by KnightOfValor, Imperial, Nethers Ascent and Kangronomicon; Imperial and KnightOfValor left it on 5 June 2015, and the alliance collapsed a month later "due to internal strife".{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2015 entries}} Contemporaries gave the same diagnosis in 2016 — "Legio fell because of internal affairs"{{cite:thread-133666|post #15, 28 Jun 2016}} — and Drew1011 treated the split as the origin of [[Valkyrie]]: "much like Imp leaving Legio to create Valkyrie with Fox".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L499 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

By mid-2015 two guilds held the map between them. "Kangronomicon [Fuq] and Nether's Ascent [TNA] were essentially the Hax of mid 2015," Drew1011 wrote{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L32, composed 22 Feb 2018}}, and a June 2016 forum post named "the ancient guilds of 'The Nether's Ascent' and 'Kangronomicon'"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}. Kangronomicon, led by Spham and then by Dar_Krusos, ran a system of subguilds. Holders of LE became one in August 2015 and, during a period when "a major war glitch" prevented Kangronomicon itself from attacking{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, took and held about fifty territories on its behalf.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L34–41, L100–101, composed 22 Feb 2018}}

Within six months of the Guild Update the era's most durable institution appeared: [[Valkyrie]], founded on 2 June 2015 by Kingdom of Foxes and [[Imperial]] "not established for the purpose of war" and governed by an Electorate of guild masters{{cite:thread-89529|post #1}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Jun 2015 entry}}. It outlived every war alliance around it, lasting into 2022{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. It also set the constitutional template the period reused: internal affairs left to each guild, foreign policy pooled in a unanimous council of guild masters{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, 15 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1}}.

!['Visualized History of the Kingdom Foxes', an infographic timeline running January 2014 to December 2015: nine government sessions and their leaders plotted against the guild's founding, the merger and detachment of Nether's Ascension, the Wynnter War, the founding of Imperial in January 2015 and the incorporation of Valkyrie. Posted by LoveLusting in the Kingdom of Foxes thread.](/images/chronicles/media/early-guild-era-c45cf1a5.webp){{cite:thread-89227|post #1, timeline graphic}}

## Concordia and Ordo Malleus (autumn 2015 – March 2016)

The first bloc assembled against the Kangronomicon–Nether's Ascent duopoly was **Concordia**, founded by the guild Validus under Ezura, with a chief named tangler as its recruiter. It grew through the autumn of 2015 by absorbing guilds that resented the duopoly, destroyed "the remnants of Legio", and peaked in October 2015.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L119–147, composed 22 Feb 2018}} The Concordia Wars began in late 2015.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Contemporary opponents accused the Validus leadership of hostile conduct in game and on the forums; Drew1011, who was among the accusers, later wrote that he had campaigned to persuade another guild's leader that Ezura "was a bad person", and that he considered Ezura's conduct to have cost Validus allies.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L138–143, L194, composed 22 Feb 2018}} Nothing else about Ezura was recorded.

![A territory map dated to late September or early October 2015, showing Concordia at its peak: Validus and Travellers hold most of the province, Holders of LE are reduced to a Detlas pocket, Nether's Ascent keeps its eastern block, and Kangronomicon appears nowhere on the map. From Drew1011's account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/06-image.webp)

The counter-bloc was [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], the Order of the Hammer, created on 6 November 2015 by seven guilds — Kangronomicon, Holders of LE, Ha Ha United, End of Everything, HackForums, ToastedPandas and Sinners — and, in Drew1011's words, "created for the sole purpose of defeating Concordia".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–179, composed 22 Feb 2018}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "-= Ordo Malleus =-", Paladin A'renos, Nov 6, 2015}} It won by assigning each member guild a block of territories to hold, and Concordia was effectively finished within days: on 8 November 2015 the leader of Historical [UEZ], 3zPz, posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded", which Ezura contested in the thread itself.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "Concordia Disbanded", 3zPz, Nov 8, 2015, 27 replies, locked}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L197–204, composed 22 Feb 2018}} By February 2016 Ordo Malleus counted twelve guilds, bound by a single rule — "Don't attack the territories that ally guilds own" — and coordinating over Skype{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}. It fell "from the inside because of guilds fighting"{{cite:thread-143392|post #10, 9 Aug 2016}} on 9 March 2016 — 11 March by the community timeline, which traces the collapse to "a chain of leaves started by Holders Of LE [HoL] approximately 2 days before"{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}} — with Holders of LE withdrawing on 9 March{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L454, composed 26 Feb 2018}}.

### Vesta

The last alliance of the period was **Vesta**, built by 3zPz out of what remained of Concordia. It counted fourteen member guilds — Historical [UEZ], Validus [Val], Travellers [TVL], TheNoLifes [TNL], Super Crafters [SPC], Wynn Try Hards [WTH], Da Classy Goats [CLG], NightStriders [CGO], BOOM [BOO], Frosted Pants [FPS], Omegamine [OMM], Silver of Anarchy [SOA], IceBlue Team [IBT] and Artifact [UPZ] — and was larger than Ordo Malleus at the time, but, in Drew1011's words, "Aside from a few small skirmishes, Vesta barely even existed." It was declared dead one month after its creation, on 10 January 2016.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L289–311, composed 26 Feb 2018}} A Holders of LE member recalled that the guild "we were at war with Vesta" before Gavel was released.{{cite:thread-217600|post #17, PikaLegend}}

Both the community timeline and Drew1011 date Vesta's creation to **December 2016**{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L289, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, a year late: 3zPz opened the Vesta alliance thread on 10 December 2015{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "-*-vesta Alliance-*-", 3zPz, Dec 10, 2015}}, and Drew1011's own chronology agrees — an alliance built from the remnants of a bloc that died in November 2015, dead by January 2016, with Gavel's release following.

Gavel's release closed the period with a territory lock. Drew1011 dates the release to 21 December 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L315–325, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, the community timeline to 14 December{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}. The whole map was frozen for roughly two weeks afterwards, so that guilds holding good territory when it landed kept it; ToastedPandas, which had captured the entire jungle days earlier, rose to guild level 51 during the freeze.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L315–325, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

## The alliance scatter (2016)

What followed Ordo's collapse was not another war bloc but a scatter of small community alliances, formed while one guild held most of the map and open warring paid poorly. The **Astrafteri Affinity** is the exception that mattered: founded around January 2016, apparently by coralialia, a former Holders of LE officer{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L352–358, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, it appears from 11 February 2016, when HackForums' recruitment thread listed "Astrafterí-affinity" as its alliance{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}, and it only acquired a forum thread of its own on 3 April 2016, posted by LordMuttonChops rather than by coralialia{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "✯ Astrafterí Affinity ✯", LordMuttonChops, Apr 3, 2016}}. The rest were social: [[halcyon|Halcyon]] (June 2016) paired ToastedPandas and Holders of LE in an "agreement for whenever help is needed"{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; [[seraphim|Seraphim]] (August 2016) declared itself "100% community based" with "no intention of actively providing support for guild wars"{{cite:thread-143392|post #1}}; [[lux-imperius|Lux Imperius]] (September 2016) was invite-only and refused applicants to stay small{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016}}; and [[aurelion|Aurelion]] (February 2017) gathered House of Sentinels, Hippies of Snuggles, The Dark Phoenix and Dragons Arise{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}}. Membership overlapped freely — Seraphim's rules expressly allowed guilds to belong to several at once{{cite:thread-143392|post #1}} — and Holders of LE was in three of them within five months.

## The HackForums dominance

By 2016 the map belonged to [[HackForums]]. In June 2016 an anti-Hax alliance thread put the guild at 94 territories{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; by September 2016 Hax held 146 of roughly 332 territories, ahead of [[Libertas]] with 60 and UltimateXeons with 53{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}. Hax was not acting alone. A June 2016 thread described a "rule of two" with Libertas — "The two guilds crushed all opposition and still rule with an iron fist"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} — and a member of UltimateXeons named his own guild as a third party: "our alliance with Hax and Lir (we are UXs)"{{cite:thread-133666|post #13, 27 Jun 2016}}. "Hax has not been a one man army in ages," a poster objected in August 2016. "They work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories."{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, 9 Aug 2016}} With Libertas' 60 and Blacklisted's 22 beside Hax's 146, the bloc held 228 of the map's 332 territories in September 2016{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}, and Blacklisted's own thread stated the arrangement plainly: "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}}

The bloc was never named at the time. A contemporary called it "a mutual land agreement" rather than an alliance{{cite:thread-133666|post #16, 28 Jun 2016}}; a Libertas member who asked his guild owner for "the name of our alliance" in August 2016 got no reply{{cite:thread-119596-p08|post #152, 9 Aug 2016}}; and no Alliance-prefixed thread was ever opened for it{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}. The name "Hax & Co" was coined only in retrospect: Drew1011 used it in a chapter written on 30 August 2018{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1086, L1097, composed 30 Aug 2018}}, and its earliest public use is a July 2019 post listing "Federation, Hax & Co, Coalition" among Wynn's mega-alliances{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}}.

Resentment was public and futile, and in June 2016 it produced two named alliances in three weeks. The Banhammer, opened by Mr_Robin_Hood on 8 June, argued that Hax "are too strong for a single guild to fight / and the only way for us to be able to beat them / is if all of the guilds unite!" and listed World of Crafters [WoC], The Wynn Guard [TwG] and MythicZodiac [MZS]{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}; a Hax-side poster replied that "I will not stop till every inch of wynncraft is mine or my allies"{{cite:thread-130386|post #5, 8 Jun 2016}}. The Separatists, founded by Tapu_Fini on 26 June around the guild The Anarchy under supermariowifi, took open enrolment — "You could pledge your guild to The Separatists, and you way withdraw that allegiance whenever you feel the need"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}. "Right now there is 2 anti hax alliances," a Hax chief noted at the end of the month{{cite:thread-134638|post #13, 30 Jun 2016}}; both failed, as an UltimateXeons member had already predicted from the earlier attempts — "It didn't work, all those guilds no longer have any territory."{{cite:thread-133666|post #10, 27 Jun 2016}}

In March 2017 a thread demanding that "Haxforums Should Be Limited On Territory Influence" charged that Hax held "100+ territories" by "taking advantage of the broken guild system"{{cite:thread-179383|post #1, 1 Mar 2017}} and "cheat the game with there control"{{cite:thread-179383|post #5, 1 Mar 2017}}; the thread's respondents, including Drew1011, uniformly rejected the idea of a cap — "Their success should not be limited just because other people are upset"{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} — and one asked pointedly "are Lir, BLA, UXs somehow exempt?"{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}}. Drew1011's diagnosis was that Hax's position was an artefact of the era rather than of strength: "The reason that Hax is able to hold so much is because, to put it simply, nobody is trying to challenge them."{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} By May 2017 a forum thread title was asking why Hax had "MORE THAN 300 TERRITORIES"{{cite:thread-189768|post #1, thread title, Hide007, 22 May 2017}}, and a 2020 recollection put the peak "closer to 350", "when they owned the whole map"{{cite:thread-265297|post #18, 4 Apr 2020}}.

## 2017: Emperium, War Syndicate and the Coalition

The [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]], founded on 21 April 2017 under Emperator [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], was the era's most elaborate institution: twelve member guilds with named leaders, a High Council of guild representatives, portfolio leaders for war, community and economy, judges whose word could not be over-ruled, and an oath for incoming members{{cite:thread-188024|post #1}}. It fell on 17 October 2017, with Angry_will as its last Emperator{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, as last edited 17 Oct 2017}}, the day after [[drew1011|Drew1011]] held the title of Emperator for a single day{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011's forum profile title chain, 2016–2019}}; the sequence was never explained.

[[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] was created on 17 July 2017{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}; its roster and leadership were never published, and it had no thread of its own{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}. In October 2017 Kingdom Foxes, KingdomPhoenixes, Gilded Sparrows and House of Sentinels founded the [[Coalition]]{{cite:community-guild-timeline|2017 entries}}. It took control of the Wynn province on 23 November 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Nov 2017 entry}} and ended War Syndicate that December — "They wiped ws off the map on Christmas day", a veteran recalled in 2020{{cite:thread-265297-p02|post #34, 14 Apr 2020}}, while another insisted the two blocs instead merged{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}} — entering 2018 with full map dominance.

## The state of the record

Nothing like a war log exists for these years. Archived 2015-era guild pages on wynncraft.com carry no territory counts, and 2016–2017 war events survive only as forum-thread imagery and written accounts. The two leaderboard captures — September 2016 and April 2018 — bracket the era{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 16 Apr 2018}}; everything between them is narrative. How HackForums fell from roughly 350 territories to the 111 it held in February 2018 is recorded in no contemporaneous source: no thread names the attackers, the dates or the sequence. The end itself, however, is dated. A 2020 participant called the fall of Hax "probably the biggest event that happened in 2017"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}}, but a contemporaneous thread of 22 February 2018 records that "HaxForums has lost all its territories" and that the largest guild on the map then held only 43{{cite:thread-219744|post #1, 22 Feb 2018}} — placing the fall about two months later than the recollection, in the week after [[the-federation|the Federation]] was founded. The era closed in mid-February 2018, when five guilds split from the Coalition over map disputes and opened the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]], beginning the [[federation-era|Federation era]]{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}.

The single largest addition to the record for these years is a memoir rather than an archive: a serialised chat history posted by Drew1011 between February 2018 and February 2021, covering January 2015 to June 2018, written by a participant in most of what it describes.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|composed 22 Feb 2018 – 1 Feb 2021}} He set out his own standard for it — "I strive to tell a factually accurate story, with no lies or complete falsities. Along with this factually accurate story, I interweave my own perspective and opinions… If you ask others who were here, they might give a completely different perspective"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L393–397, composed 26 Feb 2018}} — and his own limits, writing of the rise of HackForums that "even my timelines and knowledge of guild history has its limits, and I know no exact dates for any of this."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L518, composed 26 Feb 2018}} Where his dates for late 2015 and early 2016 can be checked against the forum-thread census, several of them are correct to the day; his 2017 and 2018 dates are from memory, and he says so.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L695, L1153}}

Eden's own recruitment thread describes it as having 'a deep history, both in guild politics and community relations' and states an aim 'to be a strong, independent force in Wynncraft politics'.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}} In the winter of 2020-21 it was one of the guilds that broke [[Artemis]]'s hold on the map,{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} and in May 2021 it was a founding member of [[Khaos]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Government

Eden governs itself as an 'Empire' with an unusually formal constitution for a Wynncraft guild, set out in its recruitment thread. Three institutions sit under the Emperor, the guild's leader, whose principal power is a veto: the Agora, of which every member is part and where non-binding votes are taken; the Legion, the guild's military, open to any member who applies for an army rank; and the Senate, which votes on decisions affecting the whole guild. Senate ranks run Consul (two, one permanent and one elected monthly, handling foreign relations), Dux (senior officers below the Consuls), and Senate; below them come Legate, Legionnaire and Citizen. An Emperor can only be replaced when the incumbent steps down and hands over.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

In 2020-21 [[yugito|Yugito]] led Eden - he opened the guild's forum thread on 1 January 2020 and answered on it throughout that year - with Lev98bug, Asthae and Rothboy among its chiefs and senators. By the time the thread was last revised, in January 2025, the Senate had turned over completely: it listed FadeDave as Emperor, Asthae as a Consul and Yugito as one of six Duxes, in a body of fourteen.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

## History

### Against Artemis (2020-21)

In March 2020 Asthae, an Eden chief, posted as an involved party in the thread attacking the Artemis alliance, replying to a critic that 'clearly I am the chief who messaged you'.{{cite:thread-263975|post #15, 9 Mar 2020}} Nine months later Eden was on the other side of the map from Artemis. The 'Guild Moderators' thread of 18 December 2020 - the flashpoint of the Dec 2020 moderation crisis - names Eden among the then-unnamed anti-Artemis coalition,{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} and Asthae posted in support of it within three minutes of publication.{{cite:thread-279337|post #2, 18 Dec 2020}}

That coalition acquired a name the following month: on 19 January 2021 Eden's chief Lev98bug wrote to [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]], 'Eden is in Goose if you could add that.'{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #72, 19 Jan 2021}} Eden's standing inside [[Goose]] was substantial. In February 2021, arguing about the 1.20 war rework, Rothboy and Lev98bug spoke for the Goose side against a critic,{{cite:thread-286375|posts #8, #9, #13 and #16, 20 Feb 2021}} and a third poster cited 'EDN who had to literally try crawl through ERN terrs' as an example of what warring against fortified [[Emorians]] territory cost.{{cite:thread-286375|post #10, 20 Feb 2021}} When [[drasalia|Drasalia]] of ChinaNumberOne drew the Goose alliance in April 2021, Eden led the second thread: 'Eden, the big bois who own a whole lotta territory. Really cool guys but I get a military vibe from them since I see them helping out other guilds during wars a lot.'{{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}}

### Khaos (2021-22)

At [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, Eden was one of the nine guilds that founded [[Khaos]] rather than [[Valhalla]], alongside [[Aequitas]], Wheres The Finish, Nerfuria, Tartarus Wrath, Ultra Violet, Fuzzy Spiders, ChinaNumberOne and Cyphrus Code. It fought the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war against the ex-Valhalla guilds]] that peaked in January 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Khaos was defunct by 26 June 2022; Eden does not appear in [[Cucumber Company]]'s roster of that date,{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} and no later alliance membership is recorded for it.

### The coup

At some point before April 2023, Eden was overthrown from within. The only account is by xK6TA, a former member describing his own past in an April 2023 guild application to [[Titans Valor]]: 'I was a part of Eden when it was #1 and slightly after it got couped.' The application repeats the claim once - 'Eden when it was #1, it got couped when I was a player lol'.{{cite:thread-206094-p97|p97 #1922, 16 Apr 2023}}

The coup's actors and date were never recorded, and what '#1' meant is not known: Eden never won a [[guild-seasons|guild season]],{{cite:wynncraft-wiki-gg-wiki-guild-seasons|season winners table}} and no other ranking of the period placed Eden first. The guild survived the coup: its recruitment thread was still being maintained in 2025, with a full Senate and an Emperor who was not Yugito.{{cite:thread-260434|post #1, opened 1 Jan 2020, revised to 19 Jan 2025}}

## Alliances

- [[Goose]] - by 18 Dec 2020 - 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}
- [[Khaos]] - 11 May 2021 - defunct by 26 Jun 2022 (founding member)

ElegantDeath stood in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]'s Emperator election of 2017 under the name Josh. When [[arenos|Paladin A'renos]] announced he no longer had time to run the alliance, three candidates came forward — [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]], Josh and [[drew1011|Drew1011]] — and Josh withdrew to act as Drew1011's campaign manager in exchange for the promise of the Community Leader post.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The vote ran a week and ended 31–30 in Nitrogen2Oxygen's favour.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

In early October 2017 [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]] handed [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] to him and briefly rejoined [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] before taking the guild back.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L853–863}} A message from the guild's parliament channel is signed "King ElegantDeath".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|KingdomPhoenixes parliament channel screenshot}}

His forum account was registered on 10 August 2016 and shows the guild Hall of Fame.{{cite:wynncraft-forum-profiles|ElegantDeath, member 69528}}

Emorians [ERN] was created on 17 Dec 2017{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} and was in the thick of alliance politics within weeks. Its recruitment thread records: "The Emorians started their journey on December 17th, 2017, under command of AzanderK and Hazeful, with Kanafarmari as second in command."{{cite:thread-248101|post #1, opened 21 Apr 2019, revised in place}}

## History

### Coalition to Federation (2017-2018)

By the turn of 2018 Emorians was in the [[Coalition]]. On 17 Feb 2018 it left with four other guilds to co-found [[Alliance Alliance]], fighting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]; when the war ended it was absorbed into [[the-federation|the Federation]], where it stayed until [[the-federation-dies|the collapse of 10 Nov 2018]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It also joined the [[Valkyrie]] community alliance on 23 May 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Drew1011's Federation tribute thanked OliviaLime — whose forum title read "Retired Lady of Emoria" — "for slapping the sense in to people when nobody else wanted to".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

### Luna and the revolt (2019)

Emorians was a founder of [[Luna]] on 14 Feb 2019.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} In March 2019 it was the map's second-largest holder at 61 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 3 Mar 2019}} On 29 Aug 2019, after a leadership dispute, Emorians and [[Avicia]] left Luna and declared war on [[Imperial]] — the revolt that spiralled into a large war over Gavel, out of which [[Terra]] formed and Luna ultimately fell.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

[[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]], writing from the opposing side on 14 September 2019 while the war was still running, stated that the Emorians left "supposedly frustrated with the actions of other prominent guilds", that in response "Luna seized all of its lands", and that this was "a large mistake", because "the Emorians became more sympathetic to our efforts against Luna".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} The seizure is recorded nowhere else.

GrandpaLee later led the guild as Lord of the Emorians, over a council styled "The Parly" — DerpyEmerald24, KittySenpai_, BurntPancakes, Splintered and IzzSt; when that leadership took over is not recorded.{{cite:thread-248101|post #1, opened 21 Apr 2019, revised in place}} DerpyEmerald24 later became Chief of Emorians and, in April 2020, compiled the community guild timeline.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, DerpyEmerald24}}

### The blocs of the 2020s

Emorians appears in the 18 Dec 2020 anti-[[Artemis]] coalition list that became [[Goose]],{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} staying until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, then joined [[Valhalla]] at its founding and followed it into [[Vanir]]. On 18 Dec 2021 it was one of the four guilds whose departure collapsed Vanir after twenty days.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It had also joined the community alliance [[Hestia]] by 6 Jun 2021,{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #140, 6 Jun 2021}} and was still a member when Hestia was last recorded in September 2022.

