An alliance of the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]], it was governed under a written constitution of offices, and its membership — twelve guilds at its August 2017 peak — turned over almost completely between May and October.

## History

The first alliance thread (Wynncraft forums thread 188024) was opened on 7 May 2017 by Paladin A'renos: "The Emperium of Wynn (TEoW) is a Dynamic alliance that was formed on the 21st of April with the goal of uniting guilds of all levels and experience to create a more user-friendly experience."{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}} Its stated order of business put community ahead of war — "As a fairly new alliance, our first goal is to get connected with our community. Events, giveaways, dungeon runs... After that, we plan on bringing in the war aspect of any alliance" — though the rules also provided for "aggressive extermination" of guilds found to be bullying members, and asked members to "refrain from taking lands from small guilds".{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}}

The May 2017 roster listed ten guilds — [[libertas|Libertas]], UltimateXeons, NeoPancakes, Sinners, The Mage Legacy, Wynn Theory, Boom, BuildCraftia, Shadow Kittens and LE Flowers — with Beasts and Jaguars pending, and only one filled leadership portfolio (War Leader DownDeeper).{{cite:thread-188024|post #4, Yuno F Gasai, 7 May 2017}} By the time the opening post was last revised in August 2017 the roster had turned over almost completely and every office was staffed; the War Leader by mid-June was TnTdestroyd, who was also named the alliance's member of the month for his warring.{{cite:thread-188024-p05|p5 #82, 16 Jun 2017, quoting the opening post}}

A second thread (202724) was opened on 4 September 2017 by Nitrogen2Oxygen, posting as "Cloud Man", after A'renos left the alliance.{{cite:thread-202724|post #2, Drew1011, 4 Sep 2017}} By 5 September 2017 the alliance had a ten-guild roster, Nitrogen2Oxygen as Emperator and Drew1011 already installed as Shadow Advisor;{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya quoting the opening post, 5 Sep 2017}} by 17 October 2017 it was much reduced.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

## Government

The Emperator was "the main figure head and the leader of the Emperium of Wynn... Their word is law within the alliance". Beneath the Emperator sat a Shadow Advisor — "the co-leader of the alliance", bound by an "Oath of the Shadow Advisor" — a War Leader (territory allocation, guild banks, war games), a Community Leader chosen by community poll, and an Economy Leader. A High Council of one to three representatives per guild voted on rule changes, leadership changes and admissions; Judges ruled on rule-breaking, and their word could not be over-ruled. A Buddy System let member guilds sponsor sub-guilds and lend them territory, and the constitution capped any single alliance at 10–15 guilds, requiring an overflow of five or more to be spun off as a "Brother Alliance" under its own Emperator.{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}}{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

Applications were processed in the thread itself: Tranquility [PaT], led by DemoGhost and self-described as "War", applied on 12 September 2017 and was answered by Drew1011 as Shadow Advisor.{{cite:thread-202724-p02|p2 #26 and #27, 12 Sep 2017}}

