## The Emperator election

The alliance held two contested elections in 2017; neither was recorded on the forums.

![A Discord announcement by Paladin A'renos calling the vote for Emperator between Nitrogen2Oxygen and Drew1011, with the reaction tallies showing D = 30 and N = 31. From Drew1011's storytime account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/37-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|Emperator election screenshot, part 12}}

By Drew1011's narrative the contest opened when A'renos announced he no longer had time to run the alliance; three candidates stood — Nitrogen2Oxygen, joshaftel (ElegantDeath) and Drew1011 — and joshaftel withdrew to act as Drew1011's campaign manager in exchange for the promise of the Community Leader post. The vote ran a week and ended 30–31 in Nitrogen2Oxygen's favour.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} Drew1011's application was an essay setting out his guild and alliance offices from 2015 onward.{{cite:the-emperial-truth|Drew1011's Emperator application essay}} The alliance's constitutional document, which he says was titled "The Emperial Truth", does not survive.

No forum record dates the election. Nitrogen2Oxygen was already Emperator by August 2017, which places the contest before then rather than in the autumn where the sequence of Drew1011's narrative would otherwise put it.{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, opened 7 May 2017, last revised Aug 2017}}

A second, better-dated poll followed. On 31 August 2017 Nitrogen2Oxygen asked the alliance to choose a Shadow Advisor between Shy_Phoenix, Angry_will, Drew1011 and Whimsicality; the tallies were 4, 5, 19 and 4.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|Shadow Advisor poll screenshot dated 08/31/2017, part 12}} Drew1011 held the post by 5 September 2017.{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya quoting the opening post, 5 Sep 2017}}

![The Shadow Advisor poll of 31 August 2017, in which Drew1011 was elected 19 votes to 5, 4 and 4. From Drew1011's storytime account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/38-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|Shadow Advisor poll screenshot dated 08/31/2017, part 12}}

### An unresolved question

Three sources describe the top of the alliance in October 2017 and no two agree.

- **Drew1011's forum profile** records the title "Emperator of the Emperium of Wynn (15 October 2017 — 16 October 2017)", a reign of a single day.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011 forum profile title chain}}
- **Drew1011's own narrative** says he ran for Emperator and **lost**, 30–31, and that he afterwards won a by-election for Shadow Advisor. He never claims to have been Emperator.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}}
- **The second thread**, the only contemporaneous source, names Nitrogen2Oxygen as Emperator on 5 September 2017{{cite:thread-202724|post #7, Aya quoting the opening post, 5 Sep 2017}} and **Angry_will** as Emperator in the opening post as last revised at 3:59 PM on 17 October 2017, with Drew1011 as Shadow Advisor in both.{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

The three cannot be reconciled. A one-day Emperatorship between Nitrogen2Oxygen's departure and Angry_will's installation would fit every recorded date, since the Shadow Advisor was constitutionally the co-leader — but no source states that such a succession occurred. Angry_will, who was also the alliance's Economy Leader, appears in no other source.

## Decline and fall

The leadership thinned through the late summer. On 4 September 2017 Nitrogen2Oxygen wrote in the first thread: "Such a sad time. Arenos leaves, Josh leaves and now my bot gets hecked"{{cite:thread-188024-p08|p8 #149, 4 Sep 2017}} — the alliance's thread-keeper and its Community Leader gone within weeks, alongside a compromised Discord bot that had mass-banned visitors.{{cite:thread-188024-p08|p8 #148, 4 Sep 2017}} The replacement thread he promised was posted the same day.{{cite:thread-202724|post #2, Drew1011, 4 Sep 2017}}

The community guild-timeline image records "10/17/17 Emperium Falls".{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Drew1011, then its Shadow Advisor, wrote that by mid-October "the Emperium was completely dead at that point", and dates his own move to found the [[coalition|Coalition]] to the same weeks.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}} The first thread's own last two posts are dated 17 October 2017: Paladin A'renos writing "bumity bump bump lets get this back up", and the reply "necro!!! alert alert!!".{{cite:thread-188024-p08|p8 #154 and #155, 17 Oct 2017}}

## Legacy

The Emperium's people outlasted it, and several of them reassembled elsewhere. Nitrogen2Oxygen resurfaced as DiamondDeities' representative in [[aesir-pact|the Aesir Pact]] in 2018 alongside [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]] of Sins of Seedia;{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} IceResistance's [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] became one of the longest-running guilds in the record; and IceBlueTeam, TheNoLifes and Sins of Seedia all reappear in later alliance rosters. Four guilds named in Drew1011's roster of [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] at the December 2017 declaration of war — BuildCraftia, Sins of Seedia, Titans Valor and Beasts — were Emperium members during 2017, Tranquility applied that September, and the Emperium's War Leader in mid-2017 was TnTdestroyd, whom the same account names as War Syndicate's unofficial leader. The possible continuity between the two blocs is set out on the War Syndicate page. As an institution the Emperium left less: no successor claimed the name, and its constitution of Emperators, Judges and Brother Alliances was not imitated by the war blocs that followed.

The Empire of Nemract ran community events through 2021, and its guild thread carried the Empire branding until July 2023.

## History
The union was formed on 17 August 2020 by [[The Simple Ones]] [ILQ] and Mystic Woods.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} From 30 November 2020 it was branded “The Empire of Nemract … | ILQ + Aeu”{{cite:thread-278123|the thread title carrying the ILQ + Aeu branding}}; the “Aeu” tag belonged to **Admiralia**.{{cite:thread-278123|post #1 (OP as last edited 18 Apr 2023)}} Admiralia was a member from that rebrand; whether Mystic Woods was renamed or replaced at that point was never recorded. Its empress held court titles (“Empress of Nemract, Queen of Aphelion”), and the Empire hosted community events through 2021.

On 30 November 2020 the union ran to five guilds. Beside The Simple Ones and Admiralia it named Mystic Woods [MYC], Nefarious Ravens [NFR] and a guild tagged [Apa], and it was aligned with, though not a member of, the [[Artemis]] alliance.{{cite:thread-278123|post #7, 30 Nov 2020, quoting the opening post}} Nefarious Ravens signed the Treaty of Damask with The Simple Ones on 21 May 2021 and declared independence.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|21 May 2021}}

By November 2021 the Empire described itself as “a group of guilds under one foreign policy, united to stand and fight together” and was a member of [[Valhalla]]. Only The Simple Ones and Admiralia were named as member guilds by then, and recruits had to hold a class of at least combat level 40.{{cite:thread-278123-p15|p15 #283, 22 Nov 2021, quoting the opening post}} The alliances named in the last state of the thread, in April 2023, were Kanzeon, the Concorde and [[smtn elf]].{{cite:thread-278123|post #1 (OP as last edited 18 Apr 2023); Kanzeon and the Concorde appear in no other archived source}}

### The court

The Empire was governed through a court of titled officers. Its thread names twelve of them under noble titles — the empress **XeraAndromeda** as owner, Crown Prince GrandAdmiralAce_ and Chancellor Count MightyShaper as chiefs, and nine more ranked count, viscount, viscountex, baroness or baron — each carrying post-nominal letters for the Empire's own orders, awarded in up to three grades{{cite:thread-278123|post #1 (OP as last edited 18 Apr 2023)}}.

The court grew as the Empire aged. In November 2020 it ran to six — the empress, the crown prince, two barons and two viscounts — none of them yet carrying post-nominals.{{cite:thread-278123|post #7, 30 Nov 2020, quoting the opening post}} A year later there were eleven, the orders were in use, and a second prince and a chancellor had been added.{{cite:thread-278123-p15|p15 #283, 22 Nov 2021, quoting the opening post}}

Recruits were asked to be "somewhat active in our community" and told that "participation in guild wars are completely optional though preferred", and those accepted were invited to [[The Simple Ones]], named as "our main guild"{{cite:thread-278123|post #1 (OP as last edited 18 Apr 2023)}}. The wars clause and the main-guild clause were both in the thread by November 2020.{{cite:thread-278123|post #7, 30 Nov 2020, quoting the opening post}}

The thread was locked between March 2022 and January 2023, and reopened on 8 January 2023 at its owner’s request; her first post back read “We are back gamers”.{{cite:thread-278123-p17|p17 #332–333, 8 Jan 2023}} It ran on under the Empire branding to a last post dated 18 July 2023.{{cite:thread-278123-p19|p19 #367, 18 Jul 2023}} No dissolution was ever announced. The Simple Ones and Mystic Woods exchanged only about thirty territories across six years — they never fought.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

