Ezura led the guild [[validus|Validus]], and under him it founded [[concordia|Concordia]] — the first bloc assembled against the [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]]–[[nethers-ascent|Nether's Ascent]] control of the territory map — with a chief named [[tangler]] as its recruiter.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L119–126}}

Concordia peaked in October 2015, when around four of its guilds attacked Kangronomicon and Nether's Ascent simultaneously.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L119–126}} It was answered on 6 November by the creation of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], and two days later 3zPz of Historical [UEZ] posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded". Ezura contested the disbandment in the thread itself, "that was when most people began to consider the alliance dead".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L203–204}}

Opponents accused the Validus leadership of hostile conduct in game and on the forums. Drew1011, who was among the accusers, later wrote that he had campaigned to persuade another guild's leader that Ezura "was a bad person", and considered Ezura's conduct to have cost Validus its allies.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L138–143, L194, composed 22 Feb 2018}} Nothing else about him was recorded.

Goden rose from recruit to guild leader inside [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] across [[federation-era|the Federation era]].{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

Answering [[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s tribute on 13 November 2018, [[lego-dw|Lego_DW]] named "the absolute gods of war this alliance created" — himself, 21(n), Goden, _Antho74_, InnerJoker, 0x7cf and snowy — as the players who "really held the alliance together in terms of war power".{{cite:thread-237070|post #18, Lego_DW, 13 Nov 2018}} Of the seven, Goden is the only one recorded elsewhere.

He appears in the warring arguments of the period on both sides of the map's balance. In June 2016 he credited a guild outside the anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] bloc with breaking its hold: "Nether's Ascent took over Hax recently... and they've been able to hold the map decently well."{{cite:thread-130386-p05|post #94, 21 Jun 2016}} Defending the Federation's dominance in April 2018, he cited [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]] as proof that a small guild could still reach the top of the leaderboard — "that case of more members = #1 isn't always the case, as shown by how IBT took #1 with like four active warring members in total".{{cite:thread-224905|post #7 (Goden)}}

## History

### An unnamed coalition
By 18 December 2020 an unnamed group of anti-[[Artemis]] guilds had formed - among them [[Avicia]], [[Emorians]], [[Eden]], Ultra Violet, Bovemists, Diablo and The Dark Phoenix - together with [[Paladins United]] and [[Imperial]], the two surviving founders of Artemis itself.{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} The coalition's coordinated war on the Artemis core began that same December, when territory exchanges jumped to 913 for the month after months of skirmishing.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]] would run for the rest of the coalition's life.

### Named by January 2021
The name Goose first appeared on the morning of 19 January 2021, in two [[the-forum-megalist|megalist]] posts made within half an hour of each other: 99loulou999 of The Dark Phoenix noting that 'TNR (TNI and TNA) are part of Goose', and Lev98bug of Eden asking 'Eden is in Goose if you could add that'.{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #71 and #72, 19 Jan 2021}} The megalist's maintainer added both and replied, 'Just want to drop in and say that I'm a huge fan of the name.'{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #73, 19 Jan 2021}} Who coined it, and when the coalition formally adopted it, was never written down.

Growth continued through the spring.{{cite:thread-278112-p06|p6 #112 and #113, 4 Mar 2021}} On 1 February 2021 [[urbymine]], a former Chief of Avicia, noted that 'BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now' - [[ShadowFall]]'s defection from an Artemis leadership seat, alongside IceBlue Team and TheNoLifes.{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} By late March the future [[Khaos]] core ([[Aequitas]], Wheres The Finish, ChinaNumberOne, Eden, joined in April by Fuzzy Spiders) was aboard.{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}}{{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}}

### The fanart roster
Goose was the only alliance whose membership was ever drawn. On 30 March and 6 April 2021 [[drasalia|Drasalia]], a member of ChinaNumberOne, posted two illustration threads personifying twelve member guilds: The Mage Legacy, Aequitas, ChinaNumberOne, Wheres The Finish, TheNoLifes and IceBlue Team in the first,{{cite:thread-289196|post #1, 30 Mar 2021}} Eden, Guardian of Wynn, Fuzzy Spiders, ShadowFall, The Dark Phoenix and Avicia in the second.{{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}} The threads were explicitly partial and unofficial - 'this is just my doodles of what I think the Guilds would look like if they were people', with the second noting 'the GOOSE alliance still has more I need to finish'.{{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}} Members of the drawn guilds replied approvingly, among them Lalatera and FrozenGalaxy of Aequitas, ZrBence of IceBlue Team, DeathLucifer of TheNoLifes and Eden's Lev98bug.{{cite:thread-289196|posts #8, #10, #12 and #17, 30 Mar – 7 Apr 2021}}

![Character art of six Goose member guilds from the second of Drasalia's illustration threads, 6 April 2021, each figure captioned with its guild tag: EDN, GsW, Cxz, SHY, TNI and AVO.](/images/chronicles/media/goose-902f9e79.webp){{cite:thread-289556|post #1, 6 Apr 2021}}

On 25 January 2021 Goose and Artemis jointly granted [[Profession Heaven]] neutral status as a public profession-XP guild.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Goose took map control from Artemis and held it until 11 May 2021, when both alliances collapsed on the same day - [[the-great-collapse|The Great Collapse]] - splitting into [[Valhalla]] and Khaos.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

### What remains unknown
Goose's formation date, internal leadership and full roster were never recorded. Every recorded membership join is a 'by' date.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Two guilds named in the December 2020 coalition list - 'Lily Pad' and 'HICH' - cannot be identified with any known guild.{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}

