## Legacy
Goose's split seeded the next era: Valhalla drew on its broad membership while Khaos formed from its core, and the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war between them]] began the day both were founded. The joint protection of Profession Heaven that Goose co-established persisted under successor alliances until 2026.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

On 9 March 2020, in VeeeKoooN's thread "The Artemis Alliance And Why It's Problematic To Me", GoulartJJ replied: "Hello, as the Shadow Fall leader and one of Artemis leaders I'd like to say that small guilds can grow very easily, alliance or not"{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}}. No other first-person claim to an [[artemis|Artemis]] leadership seat was ever recorded.

The rest of the post set out how Artemis explained itself. On growth: ShadowFall "grew with FFA's, we were level 20ish by August of last year, we tried joining [[luna|Luna]] when we were leveling but got denied, that didn't stop us"{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}}. On the map: "If you're not in a map controlling alliance, nothing stops you from attacking any territories in the map, some may reclaim it instantly, others would rather use a diplomatic approach"{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}}. On the distribution of land: "Guilds who are with big claims are the guilds who have contributed the most to the alliance." On entry: "Guilds may also apply to Artemis by contacting one of the guild leaders, and possibly be accepted."{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}}

Within a year ShadowFall had changed sides — [[urbymine]] reported on 1 February 2021 that "BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now"{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}}. GoulartJJ was later a member of [[imperial|Imperial]]{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, author guild badge as captured (badge markup, not post text)}}.

The dominant territorial power of [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]], HackForums kept the same owner in every recovered revision of its recruitment thread from 2016 to 2023: "HackForums [Hax] Lvl. 92 - Created 12/24/2014 / Guild Owner: [[thedarksoul|TheDarkSoul]]"{{cite:thread-109319|post #1}}.

## History

### Ordo Malleus, expulsion and readmission (1015–2016)

HackForums was one of the seven founding guilds of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] on 6 November 2015, TheDarkSoul sitting in its leader chat{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178, composed 22 Feb 2018}}, and it was assigned the desert after End of Everything was expelled from the alliance on 1 December 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L238–239, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. It was later expelled and then readmitted. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] wrote in 2016 that "Hax was actually kicked out of Ordo"{{cite:thread-143392|post #7, Drew1011, 9 Aug 2016}}, and that "Hax was one of the original guilds, although we kicked them out, and then for some reason, let them back in"{{cite:thread-133666|post #6, Drew1011, 27 Jun 2016}}, giving no date or reason.

The expulsion came in early January 2016, immediately after TheDarkSoul was banned from the forums: Drew1011 raised the ban in the alliance's senior chat, Yamipanda of ToastedPandas moved a vote, and the vote was unanimous or nearly so. The grievances were repeated accidental attacks on allied guilds, and defending recaptured allied territory with full mob defences instead of the light defences the alliance's recapture tactic required.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L333–342, composed 26 Feb 2018}} HackForums is absent from Ordo Malleus' 20 February 2016 roster{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}, and on 11 February 2016 its own opening post listed a different alliance entirely — "Alliances: Astrafterí-affinity"{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}. In late February 2016 Paladin A'renos re-invited the guild.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L435–436, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

### The rise to dominance (1016–2017)

Drew1011, writing in February 2018, gave no dates for the guild's rise: "even my timelines and knowledge of guild history has its limits, and I know no exact dates for any of this. All I know is that Hax began their reign sometime around the summer of 2016."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L517–518, composed 26 Feb 2018}} By his account the guild's freedom of action grew when it moved into the Astrafteri Affinity, because "they no longer had a massive list of allies that they could not attack, and had much more freedom in wars"; when Astrafteri's guilds went inactive and the alliance died, "they stayed in an alliance with [[Libertas]], and divided all of Wynn amongst themselves and a few others such as Blacklisted"; and when those partners in turn went inactive, "Hax was left as the one truly active war guild. With nobody to challenge them, they expanded their horizons and engulfed all of Wynn and Gavel."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L508–516, composed 26 Feb 2018}} He adds that the guild "would occasionally give territories to other guilds such as [[paladins-united|Paladins United]]"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L517, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, and offers a judgement: that HackForums "intended to share the glory with a few allies such as Libertas" and expanded into the vacuum its allies left{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L519–523, composed 26 Feb 2018}}.

One element of his sequence is dated earlier than he places it: he puts the move to the Astrafteri Affinity after Ordo Malleus' collapse of 9 March 2016, but the guild's own thread listed Astrafteri as its alliance on 11 February 2016, a month before{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}. The Hax–Libertas–Blacklisted bloc was described repeatedly at the time. A June 2016 post described a "rule of two" with [[Libertas]]: "This enemy, known only has 'Hack Forums' quickly established their rule through military might... Soon after, another guild, Libertas, joined the surge. The two guilds crushed all opposition and still rule with an iron fist."{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} A member of UltimateXeons wrote the next day that "our alliance with Hax and Lir (we are UXs) is gonna let the three guilds keep their territory... without anybody really taking it unless one of the guilds leaves or breaks the alliance"{{cite:thread-133666|post #13, 27 Jun 2016}}. "You do realize Hax has not been a one many army in ages?", a poster objected in August 2016. "They work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories."{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, 9 Aug 2016}} Blacklisted [BLA] — founded 19 Jan 2016 under NeonRider and Naraka00 — stated the arrangement from the other side in its own recruitment thread, under a heading reading "ALLIANCES AND ALLIES": "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} In March 2017 a defender of Hax asked its critics "are Lir, BLA, UXs somehow exempt?"{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}}.

On 8 June 2016 Hax held 94 territories{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}. By 23 September 2016 HackForums held 146 of the map's ~332 territories, nearly two and a half times the next guild (Libertas, at 60), with Hax, Libertas and Blacklisted together on 228{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}. Its peak ran higher still: a May 2017 forum thread title asked why Hax had "MORE THAN 300 TERRITORIES"{{cite:thread-189768|post #1, thread title, Hide007, 22 May 2017}}, and in 2020 a player put the maximum "closer to 350", "when they owned the whole map"{{cite:thread-265297|post #18, 4 Apr 2020}}.

The bloc appears to have had no name while it existed. A contemporary corrected the UltimateXeons member by calling it "a mutual land agreement" rather than an alliance{{cite:thread-133666|post #16, 28 Jun 2016}}; a Libertas member who asked his own guild owner "the name of our alliance" in August 2016 received no answer anywhere in the thread{{cite:thread-119596-p08|post #152, 9 Aug 2016}}; and no alliance thread was ever posted for the bloc{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-page-2-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-directi|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 2}}. The label "Hax & Co" is retrospective: Drew1011 used it in August 2018{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1086, L1097, composed 30 Aug 2018}}, and the earliest public use is a July 2019 post listing "Federation, Hax & Co, Coalition" among Wynn's mega-alliances{{cite:thread-252647|post #5, 21 Jul 2019}}.

The dominance was resented in public and never checked. Two anti-Hax alliances were posted within three weeks of each other in June 2016. The Banhammer, opened by Mr_Robin_Hood on 8 June, proposed a universal non-aggression bloc on the ground that "Hax currently owns 94 territories / They are too strong for a single guild to fight / and the only way for us to be able to beat them / is if all of the guilds unite!", and listed World of Crafters [WoC], The Wynn Guard [TwG] and MythicZodiac [MZS] as members{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}. A Hax-side poster answered it the same day: "I will not stop till every inch of wynncraft is mine or my allies, my allies will attack you or be attacked if they revolt."{{cite:thread-130386|post #5, 8 Jun 2016}} The Separatists, a Star Wars-themed open-enrolment alliance founded by Tapu_Fini on 26 June around the guild The Anarchy, followed{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}; its founder conceded that "even if we don't beat them, at least we can be an annoyance"{{cite:thread-133666|post #11, 27 Jun 2016}}. At the end of the month a Hax chief noted in passing that "right now there is 2 anti hax alliances"{{cite:thread-134638|post #13, 30 Jun 2016}}. Neither worked; an UltimateXeons member's verdict on the earlier attempts was "It didn't work, all those guilds no longer have any territory."{{cite:thread-133666|post #10, 27 Jun 2016}}

In March 2017 a thread titled "Haxforums Should Be Limited On Territory Influence" argued that Hax's "taking advantage of the broken guild system has clearly killed the guild system for everyone else"{{cite:thread-179383|post #1, 1 Mar 2017}} and that "they cheat the game with there control and need to be broken up"{{cite:thread-179383|post #5, 1 Mar 2017}}. The thread's respondents rejected a cap almost unanimously, Drew1011 among them: "Although I dislike a single guild or alliance having such a monopoly over the territories, I have never, and will never support the limiting of guild territories... Their success should not be limited just because other people are upset."{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} His explanation of the position was that it was an artefact of a broken and unloved system rather than of force: "The reason that Hax is able to hold so much is because, to put it simply, nobody is trying to challenge them... When people begin trying again... it will become very difficult for Hax to maintain control of the 100+ territories they currently own."{{cite:thread-179383|post #6, 1 Mar 2017}} A 2020 retrospective listed the mechanics that had made it possible: "subguilds were heavily abused / there was no cd timer after you took a territory, you could instantly snipe it back / alt warring was legal / wars hardly worked at all so no one was motivated whatsoever"{{cite:thread-263975-p02|post #31, 9 Mar 2020}}

### The Coalition and the wipe (2017-2018)

By the end of 2017 HackForums was a member of the [[Coalition]], the alliance holding full map dominance that winter{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. Drew1011, who recruited it, records that he approached TheDarkSoul personally in the autumn of 2017 and that the guild was revived for the purpose: TheDarkSoul "said that he was busy and did not know when he would have the time to revive Hax, but that when he did have the time, he would most certainly help us deal with War Syndicate."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L878, composed 22 Mar 2018}} The guild reappeared on the map that winter.

On 17 Feb 2018 HackForums left the Coalition with four other guilds to form [[Alliance Alliance]], starting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}; the community timeline gives the same five departures on the same date{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Feb 2018 entry}}, and Drew1011 dates the split to 16 February, within an hour of the announcement of a proposed division of the province of Wynn{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1057–1059, composed 11 Jul 2018}}. Two days later, on 19 Feb 2018, the newly formed [[the-federation|Federation]] attacked HackForums' 111 territories and [[the-wipe-of-hackforums|wiped them to zero]]{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}; the guild held none by 22 Feb 2018{{cite:thread-219744|post #1, 22 Feb 2018}}.

The attack came at the end of a four-day campaign that had already taken Llevigar, the swamp and the forests; the decision was Snowythewolf's, of Hall of Fame. Drew1011 wrote: "At the very latest hours of the 19th, Snowy announced it was time to attack Hax. At the time they held 111 territoires. Less than 10 hours later, they had none."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1091, composed 30 Aug 2018}} His figure of under ten hours is shorter than the "under 12 hours" of the community timeline image{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, and both are estimates. The thread of 22 February reporting the fall noted that "the guilds with the most territories have only 43"{{cite:thread-219744|post #1, 22 Feb 2018}}: guilds nobody was fighting had drifted to the top of the leaderboard in the confusion — Blacklisted among them, which "sat at #1 on the leaderboards for roughly a day"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1092, composed 30 Aug 2018}}. It was the end of Hax as a territorial power, and the agent was the Federation rather than the Coalition. A moderator closed the 22 February thread four minutes after it opened, as not relevant{{cite:thread-219744|post #3, 22 Feb 2018}}.

The fall is often placed in 2017 — a participant wrote in 2020 that it was "probably the biggest event that happened in 2017"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}} — but it came in February 2018. What belongs to 2017 is the decline, from a reported peak near 350 to the 111 territories Hax still held on 19 Feb 2018{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}.

### After the fall

The guild endured. By 3 March 2019 it was back at 33 territories, at guild level 82 with the largest roster on the leaderboard (84 members){{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 3 Mar 2019}}. In 2021 it joined [[Valhalla]] at its founding{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, and it was a member of the community alliance [[Hestia]] by 6 Jun 2021, in a six-guild roster posted to the guild megalist{{cite:thread-278112-p07-wb20211128|post #140, 6 Jun 2021}}, remaining through September 2022{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}. Its thread today describes a guild that has given up the thing it was known for: "This is a community guild, we do not war."{{cite:thread-109319|post #1}} The guild still exists{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}.

## Alliances

- [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] — founder guild, 6 Nov 2015; expelled early Jan 2016 and readmitted late Feb 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178, L333–342, L435–436}}{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}{{cite:thread-143392|post #7, 9 Aug 2016}}
- Astrafteri Affinity — listed by the guild from 11 Feb 2016{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}
