- [[Coalition]] — by late 2017 – 16/17 Feb 2018{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L878, L1057–1059}}
- [[Alliance Alliance]] — 17 Feb 2018 – 20 Mar 2018 (co-founder){{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}
- [[Valhalla]] — 11 May 2021 – 28 Nov 2021{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}
- [[Hestia]] — 6 Jun 2021 – 19 Sep 2022 (community alliance){{cite:thread-278112-p07-wb20211128|post #140, 6 Jun 2021}}

Halcyon belongs to a cluster of non-war alliances that appeared in the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]] alongside [[seraphim|Seraphim]] and [[aurelion|Aurelion]], at a point when a single guild — [[hackforums|HackForums]] — held close to half the territory map and open warring had become unrewarding for most guilds.

## History

Yamipanda, leader of ToastedPandas, posted the announcement thread on 8 June 2016: "On June 5th, 2016, the Halcyon Alliance was born. The Halcyon Alliance was founded upon the vision to create solutions of preparing for success, improving community ideals and player relations."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}} The terms were mutual aid and joint deliberation rather than a war compact: "This is an agreement for whenever help is needed, each member shall aid each other in whatever task it may be. Each guild shall work together to discuss any issues that may arise and compromise to reach agreement."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}

Its governance mirrored the pattern [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] used in the same period, splitting internal from external affairs: "Internal affairs are to be handled by individual guild leaders, while matters concerning foreign entities as well as within the whole alliance are to be dealt with by every guild leader and any other representatives."{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}} The stated aim was social — "to provide an environment where members can feel comfortable socializing and gaming" — with events and challenges promised.{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, 8 Jun 2016}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]], owner of Holders of LE, signed on in the thread the same evening: "Glad to create an alliance with a guild as amazing as TnP. Long live Halcyon / To clarify, it's pronounce Hal-see-on."{{cite:thread-130444|post #4, 8 Jun 2016}} [[killerfish|Killerfish]] was credited by Yamipanda with "helping with most of the diction" and replied as an insider — "Now, let us all within the alliance see an age of Halcyon"{{cite:thread-130444|post #2, 8 Jun 2016}} — placing him inside the Halcyon circle a month before he became a founding council member of House of Sentinels, and eighteen months before he founded a [[coalition|Coalition]] guild.{{cite:thread-135191|post #1, as last revised 29 Apr 2017}}

## Membership

Halcyon was founded between exactly two guilds, ToastedPandas and Holders of LE, and no third guild is recorded as joining, though a reader in the thread wished aloud that "this alliance includes increased amounts of guilds".{{cite:thread-130444|post #12, 10 Jun 2016}} Both members had appeared in the [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] roster of February 2016;{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016}} Holders of LE went on to join [[seraphim|Seraphim]] that August and [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] that October.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No dissolution was recorded, and Halcyon was never mentioned again after June 2016; a reply in the founding thread asking "how long will this last?" went unanswered.{{cite:thread-130444|post #14, 11 Jun 2016}} A social layer persisted underneath the territorial situation: the two guilds' leaderships stayed closely tied, and Drew1011 went on to lead [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] from October 2016 and to found [[the-federation|the Federation]] in 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## History
Hestia first appears on 2 December 2020: “ANO is apart of the alliances Hestia (a community alliance between ANO, ESI, LXA, and PUN) and [[Artemis]] (war alliance)”.{{cite:thread-278112|post #10, 2 Dec 2020}} Its founding was never documented; a June 2021 description put it at “about a year now”, placing its formation around mid-2020, and listed six members: [[Titans Valor]], [[Emorians]], Lux Nova, Empire of Sindria, [[Paladins United]] and [[HackForums]].{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #140, 6 Jun 2021}}

Hestia's membership cut across the war-alliance lines of its era: in December 2020 Titans Valor was fighting inside Artemis while Paladins United stood with the opposing coalition that became [[Goose]] — yet both belonged to Hestia.{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} As a community alliance it took no recorded part in the wars themselves.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

By May 2022 [[titan-times|Titan Times]], Titans Valor's newsletter, described Hestia as declining but “still around”, and recorded [[Adonis]] being founded as a community successor.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} Paladins United's recruitment thread continued to list Hestia — alongside [[Valkyrie]], “both community alliances”{{cite:thread-246617|opening post, Wayback capture 28 Nov 2021}} — until 19 September 2022, the alliance's last mention anywhere.{{cite:thread-246617-wb20220919|Paladins United recruitment thread opening post, Wayback Machine capture of 19 Sep 2022}} No dissolution was ever recorded.

