## Legacy
Hestia is one of the clearest examples of its era's split between war and community alliances: its members fought one another under war banners while remaining social allies in Hestia. Its role passed to Adonis, founded around May 2022 by the leaders of Titans Valor and Empire of Sindria, which outlived every war alliance around it.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}}

PillowPet created the guild on 21 December 2014{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Dec 2014}}{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L925, composed 22 Mar 2018}}, the day before guild warfare itself arrived in [[the-guild-update|the Guild Update]] of 22 December — making it one of the very few guilds of that first cohort still being revived three years later. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] owned the guild from December 2015 to January 2018.

## The record

Almost everything known about the guild's internal history between 2015 and 2016 comes from one source: Drew1011's serialised first-person account, composed between 2018 and 2021, which he described as a mixture of fact and his own opinion. He is also the sole source for events in which he was an interested party, including the September 2015 transfer that made him leader.

## History

### 2015: the leadership crisis

PillowPet sold the guild to TartMango on 3 March 2015, and TartMango sold it to SSEEBBYZ on 23 April. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] joined on 25 May 2015 and the Troms meeting followed on 4 June.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Mar–Jun 2015}} By mid-2015 the guild was owned by SSEEBBYZ, who was largely inactive and had given day-to-day leadership to [[yosteric5]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L19–20}}. Drew1011, who joined in late May 2015 after being invited by the chief [[kuroi|Kuroi]], wrote that the guild's "reputation had never been lower" and that it had "gone through multiple scandals, including a duping ordeal that got many members banned"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L15–17}}.

About a week after joining, Drew1011 met three or four other members at the Troms throne room in what Drew1011 called the "Secret HoL Illuminati Society", a discussion of how to remove yosteric5 from the leadership{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L22–24}}. The request went to Kangronomicon in a forum post by Kuroi: "we wanted to ask you something about... yosteric5 … he's the stand-in leader of HoL, our guild … We're asking you to convince our guild leader, @SSEEBBYZ, to kick him out of the guild or demote him. Being leader of Fuq, we're pretty sure you can get SSEEBBYZ to do that"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|forum post by Kuroi reproduced as a screenshot at L25}}. [[spham|Spham]] agreed to intervene only if SSEEBBYZ logged in to the game, which he did not; Kuroi and Drew1011 instead put their grievances to yosteric5 directly and were both made "Head Chiefs"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L27–30}}.

![The forum post by Kuroi, guild HoL, asking Spham of Kangronomicon to intervene against yosteric5 — the message that ended the "Secret HoL Illuminati Society" plan. From Drew1011's account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/02-a64d84b0a8360b896c510f3abac7132c.webp)

### Kangronomicon, Validus and the fifty territories

Through the summer of 2015 the guild ran repeated skirmishes against [[nethers-ascent|Nether's Ascent]], taking and briefly holding six or seven territories at a time, which Drew1011 described as an audition for [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]]'s notice{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L31–33}}. In parallel it had been in contact with the guild [[validus|Validus]] since 5 July 2015, and it joined Validus's alliance [[concordia|Concordia]]{{cite:the-emperial-truth|Drew1011's Emperator application essay, mid-2017}}. On 14 August 2015 it became a Kangronomicon subguild instead, and the break with Validus followed the next day{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L96–100}}. The guild's own timeline dates the move to Kangronomicon to 15 August, has it back in Concordia from 24 August, and ends the Concordia membership on 22 September, the day [[spham|Spham]] took ownership and the guild became a full ally of Kangronomicon rather than a subguild.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Aug–Sep 2015}}

A glitch that prevented Kangronomicon from starting wars left its subguilds to recapture anything it lost. Between 15 and 24 August 2015 Holders of LE captured and held 50 territories before the same glitch reached it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L34–36, L100–101}}. In his mid-2017 application to lead the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]], Drew1011 put his own co-leadership at July to September 2015 and wrote that "the guild managed to capture and hold over 50 territories until the guild succumbed to the glitch that prevented a guild from starting a guild war"; only Wynn territories existed at the time{{cite:the-emperial-truth|Drew1011's Emperator application essay, mid-2017}}. He also claimed the guild reached fifth on the leaderboard at its height, when the board ranked guilds by level rather than territory{{cite:the-emperial-truth|Drew1011's Emperator application essay, mid-2017}}.

Drew1011 wrote that he was demoted to recruit and then kicked on 24 August 2015 after telling yosteric5 about the Troms meeting himself{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L40–45, L100–101}}, and that yosteric5 then realigned the guild from Kangronomicon to Validus; he attributed this to a personal feud between yosteric5 and Spham{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L102}}. He rejoined on an alternate account as co-leader on 13 September 2015{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L55}}.

### The coup of 22 September 2015

SSEEBBYZ told Drew1011 he wanted to sell the guild for "5 stacks"; Spham declined to lend the money but arranged for her partner unicorn67 to buy it{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L63–66}}. On 22 September 2015, at an announced guild meeting, SSEEBBYZ transferred the guild to an account he introduced as his cousin, AALLEEXX — which Drew1011 identifies as Spham's alternate account — after which yosteric5 was demoted to recruit and Drew1011 named leader in Spham's absence{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L67–71}}. yosteric5 left, followed by the "yosteric loyalists", "most of them" going to Validus "and then later to [[libertas|Libertas]] when Yos created it"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L74–76}}.

Under Dar_Krusos, who took over Kangronomicon within hours of the coup, Holders of LE was promoted from subguild to full ally and assigned nine territories around Nemract{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L111–114}}. In October 2015 it fought alongside Kangronomicon through a coordinated [[concordia|Concordia]] assault; Drew1011 wrote that he defended alone for roughly four hours because the rest of the guild was unavailable{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L119–129}}.

### Ordo Malleus and the alliance years

Late in 2015 Dar_Krusos required the guild to elect four officers — Diplomat, War Commander, Community Manager and Merchant — in preparation for a new alliance{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L148–151}}. Of the resulting elections Drew1011 later wrote that he "changed the results" of the Diplomat contest to install the chief coralialia{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L163–166}}.

The guild was approached to found [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] on 27 October 2015.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Oct 2015}} It was one of the alliance's seven founding guilds on 6 November 2015 and was assigned Nesaak and Mining Base under its territory system{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178, L197–199}}. Spham handed ownership to Drew1011 on 16 December 2015, six days after the creation of the [[vesta|Vesta]] alliance, which dissolved from inactivity on 10 January 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Dec 2015 and Jan 2016}} It appears in the alliance's February 2016 roster{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, 20 Feb 2016}}. Drew1011 withdrew the guild on 9 March 2016, the day the alliance collapsed{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L454}}. A member applying to rejoin in 2018 recalled: "I have joined HoL before Gavel was released, when HoL was in alliance with Toasted Pandas, HaHaUnited, Fuq etc … This was back when we were at war with [[vesta|Vesta]]"{{cite:thread-217600|post #15, PikaLegend, 2 Feb 2018}}.

It joined the [[astrafteri-affinity|Astrafteri Affinity]], created on 27 January 2016, for a short period after Ordo Malleus fell.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Jan 2016 and Mar 2016}} The guild then joined [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] at a ceremony in Llevigar on 18 March 2016 alongside [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom of Foxes]], HaHaUnited and [[imperial|Imperial]]{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L472–473}}, and left it on 5 June 2016 to found [[halcyon|Halcyon]] with ToastedPandas. Its leaving message records both the departure and the guild's artwork: "I don't really want to go down in history as the first (and probably only) guild to ever leave Valkyrie, but I am … I will remove the HoL art that Ari so graciously created for us"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|leaving message reproduced as a screenshot at L499}} — "Ari" being [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]]. A merger with The Sebbelonien Plebs [TsP] followed on 16 April 2016, and the idea of the Toasted Pandas alliance was raised on 4 June, the day before the guild left Valkyrie for it.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Apr 2016 and Jun 2016}} [[halcyon|Halcyon]] collapsed on 12 August 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Aug 2016}} It rejoined Valkyrie on 3 September 2016{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L554}}, and entered hibernation on 1 December 2016 to wait for guilds to be fixed in-game.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Dec 2016}}

### War doctrine

A captain's guide Drew1011 wrote for the guild's captains, and forbade them to share on pain of demotion, sets out how Holders of LE fought inside Ordo Malleus. Captains were to keep the territory map open at all times and never attack eight named allied guilds — Kangronomicon, Ha Ha United, ToastedPandas, Sinners, [[libertas|Libertas]], Death Reapers, Necronomicon and White Wolves — with a single exception for retaking one of the guild's own Nesaak territories. [[vesta|Vesta]]'s fourteen guilds were listed as "totally hostile".{{cite:gdoc-1sqfxhjwewtphua7|"Holders Of LE — A captain's guide", allies and enemies}}

Sixteen territories were the guild's own, all of them in Nesaak, Twain and Mining Base, and captains were told to retake any of them immediately. Three defensive compositions were prescribed. The first, for Nesaak territories only, was 300 level-1 and 300 level-18 mercenaries, 150 level-70 mercenaries, and 200 level-10 and 50 level-70 rangers, at about 1,650 emeralds. The second, known as "the 440 def", was used only when capturing a territory for an ally to take back. Against an opponent trying to drain the guild's treasury by attacking Nesaak with small forces, captains were to defend with 100 level-1 mercenaries and nothing else.{{cite:gdoc-1sqfxhjwewtphua7|"Holders Of LE — A captain's guide", designated territories and defences}}

### Revival and end

Drew1011 handed the guild to Thundderr on 31 January 2018, posting on its new thread the same day: "Make me proud."{{cite:thread-217600|post #2, Drew1011, 31 Jan 2018}} Revived inside the [[coalition|Coalition]], it was allotted 19 territories in the alliance's February 2018 division of the map{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}}, and its May 2018 thread lists Thundderr as leader with Kur0i and Pillowpet — the guild's creator — still among its chiefs{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}. Drew1011 established House Holderson as the guild's ruling house on 21 March 2018.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Mar 2018}} Thundderr told Drew1011 on 1 April 2018 that he was giving the guild up, and it went inactive again from that point{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1154–1155}}. Holders of LE resigned from Valkyrie on 9 June 2018; Drew1011 reclaimed ownership on the 13th, took the guild out of [[the-federation|the Federation]] on the 16th into a second hibernation, and on 25 June reopened its Discord to players already in other guilds, beginning what he called Operation: Unity the following day.{{cite:gdoc-1bbnalbfij8cjnog|Jun 2018}}

