## History
Horologium was formed on 1 Dec 2019 by [[DiamondDeities]], [[Titans Valor]] and [[The Simple Ones]] — three veterans of [[Terra]] and the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]], which had collapsed the week before.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

Horologium's end came from outside the war map: on 8 Jan 2020, [[Nitrogen2Oxygen]] disbanded DiamondDeities itself, and Horologium de facto dissolved with it.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Most of DiamondDeities' remaining members regrouped as Lux Nova the next day.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} No formal dissolution of the alliance was ever recorded.

## Membership
{{alliance:Horologium}}

## Legacy
Horologium closed the chain of ever-smaller successor blocs descending from Terra. Within the year its survivors resurfaced in the community alliances of 2020: Titans Valor (with Lux Nova) in [[Hestia]], and The Simple Ones in the [[Empire of Nemract]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

HungHung filed [[avicia|Avicia]]'s updates to [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] during 2021, including routine guild-level corrections in May of that year{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #130, 3 May 2021}}. On 7 July 2021 he posted the request that became the only public record of an entire alliance: "Can you also add Avicia [AVO], Blue Nations United [IBT], [[shadowfall|ShadowFall]] [Shy], and TheNoLifes [TNL] in the Niflheim community alliance? Don't replace valhalla, just add it as a second alliance please :)"{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}}

The post is doubly valuable. It names [[niflheim|Niflheim]]'s four member guilds, and its second sentence records that those same guilds simultaneously belonged to the war alliance [[valhalla|Valhalla]] — direct evidence that community and war alliances ran in parallel over the same membership rather than replacing one another{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}}. Sg_Voltage answered within the hour: "Should be set, let me know if you want anyone else added to the community!"{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #147, 7 Jul 2021}}

No other source lists Niflheim's membership, and HungHung's rank within Avicia is not stated anywhere in the record.

IceResistance founded [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] [ANO] on 2 July 2017 and opened its recruitment thread on 15 October 2017, where the guild's first hierarchy read "IceResistance | Leader of Titans Valor"{{cite:thread-206094|post #1 (OP), thread opened 15 Oct 2017; "Est. July 2nd, 2017"}}. Two weeks after founding he applied on the guild's behalf to the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]], describing a ten-member guild that was "Mostly community guild for the most part currently. Since we are still growing, we are not a War guild yet, although Titans Valor will always be partly community"{{cite:thread-188024-p06|p6 #102, 15 Jul 2017}}{{cite:thread-278112|post #11, 2 Dec 2020 (the same framing restated: "umm ANO community guild FIRST / war second")}}; the alliance's roster records "Titans Valor (ANO) - Owner: IceResistance"{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster, 7 May 2017}}.

Against [[sheepn|Sheepn]]'s moderation pamphlet of December 2020 he defended the staff: "Moderators will not ban players without reason. Mods should also be able to participate in guilds just like any other player without being accused of bias and other slander."{{cite:thread-279337|post #17, 19 Dec 2020}}

[[titan-times|Titan Times]] vol. 6 marked "the long term hiatus of ANO's founder, IceResistance"{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}; by vol. 9 he is "ANO founder and previous owner"{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}. The guild's later roster lists Calluum as Owner and IceResistance as Chief and Founder{{cite:thread-206094|post #1 (OP), as later revised}}. Interviewed in vol. 20, Calluum said he took the role because "No one else wanted it when pally was stepping down"{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol20|vol. 20, 23 Nov 2025}} — the only public statement touching the handover, and it identifies no one further.

Returning to the forums on 2 October 2025, IceResistance argued that public channels had displaced real diplomacy: "Once upon a time, guilds had their own channels, their own Discords, their own backrooms where actual conversations happened. Alliances were formed, enemies were negotiated with, all behind closed doors. And it worked."{{cite:thread-322643|post #1, 2 Oct 2025}}

Icey_Diamond co-led [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] [DDT] with [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]]. The [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]]'s thread names the pair as the guild's two representatives — the fullest leadership roster recorded for any 2018 sub-alliance.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} DiamondDeities was accepted into the pact on 18 July 2018.{{cite:thread-227373-p02|p2 #24, 18 Jul 2018}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s Federation tribute counts Nitrogen2Oxygen and Icey_Diamond among its most trusted friends.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

DiamondDeities went on through [[sol|SOL]], [[terra|Terra]], the [[council-of-canyon-kingdoms|Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] and [[horologium|Horologium]] before Nitrogen2Oxygen disbanded it on 8 January 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Idiot Co [ICo] is a Wynncraft guild created on 26 Nov 2017.{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-idiot-20co|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## History

### The quiet years (2017-2022)

Little of Idiot Co's first five years was recorded. In February 2021 it was among the guilds actively warring in the desert during the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]]; which side it fought on is not known.{{cite:thread-286375|post #4, 20 Feb 2021}}

### smtn elf (2023)

Idiot Co joined [[smtn elf]], the great super-alliance descended from [[Cucumber Company]], by late March 2023, when it held alliance territory.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}} It remained until the alliance quietly dissolved in mid-2023 after [[The Aquarium]] and [[Avicia]] walked out.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Aquarium war (2024-2025)

On 29 Apr 2024 Idiot Co ignited [[idiot-co-aquarium-war|the biggest war since 2021]] against The Aquarium, raging through mid-July with a peak of 5,045 territory exchanges in a single week, and returning for a second round from November 2024 into January 2025.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war spanned the Rekindled World map rework of 10 Aug 2024. As in all wars of [[private-diplomacy-era|the private-diplomacy era]], any wider coalitions involved went unrecorded; only the two principal guilds are known.

## Alliances

- [[smtn elf]] — by 25 Mar 2023 – Jun 2023 (the alliance's quiet end){{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}

No other alliance membership was ever recorded.

Imperial [Imp] is one of the oldest guilds in the warring record, created on 14 Jan 2015.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

## History

### Valkyrie and the Federation (2015-2018)

On 2 Jun 2015 Imperial co-founded [[Valkyrie]] with Kingdom of Foxes (today [[Kingdom Foxes]]).{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} It did not stay: Imperial was still among the member-guilds of the alliance's second relaunch thread of August 2016,{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, relaunch of 29 Aug 2016}} but by the third relaunch thread of 15 October 2016 it had gone — "tmw the alliance originally made by Imp and Fox has neither Imp nor Fox in it", one poster wrote,{{cite:thread-159734|post #2, 15 Oct 2016}} to which Ascended Kitten of Imperial replied, "Hey, we are pretty alive :3 Just not in the alliance anymore".{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, 15 Oct 2016}} Imperial's membership is next recorded in September 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The gap matters, because later accounts describe Valkyrie as a continuous four-guild bloc including Imperial.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}}

Imperial was a member of [[the-federation|the Federation]] from its founding in February 2018 through [[federation-era|the Federation era]];{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} during the November 2018 collapse its exit 'for independence... snowballed into a major attack on Fed together with the enemy alliance [Ent]', Ascended Kitten of Imperial wrote the following morning - part of the cascade that killed the alliance on 10 Nov 2018.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}}

### Luna and the wars of 2019

Imperial founded [[Luna]] on 14 Feb 2019 to counter [[SOL]],{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} and led its war on Kingdom Foxes, attacking Fox 660 times over five months.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} In March 2019 Imperial was the map's largest holder, at 85 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 3 Mar 2019}} On 29 Aug 2019 [[Emorians]] and [[Avicia]] left Luna and declared war on Imperial specifically;{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Luna collapsed that September in the Luna–[[Terra]] war, in which, [[arkada|Arkada]] wrote, Terra's guilds "focused on toppling one guild in particular, Imperial".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}}

### The Valkyrie join-date problem

Whether September 2019 marks a return to Valkyrie or only a first mention is unclear. Writing on 14 Sep 2019, [[arkada|Arkada]] of Titans Valor opened his account of the war with: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians, have existed for longer than I've played Wynncraft."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} He was a hostile observer describing an established bloc — yet Imperial and [[Paladins United]] are recorded entering Valkyrie only that September, weeks after Emorians had left it in the revolt of late August, so that on those dates his four guilds were never simultaneously members.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The September dates are probably first mentions rather than joins; when Imperial actually rejoined is not known.

### Artemis, Goose, and the quiet years (2019-2022)

Imperial co-founded [[Artemis]] on 30 Oct 2019 with Paladins United and Caeruleum Order.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} In March 2020 GoulartJJ, an Imperial player who by then led the guild ShadowFall, introduced himself on the forums as "the Shadow Fall leader and one of Artemis leaders" — see [[goulartjj|GoulartJJ]].{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} By December 2020 Imperial had drifted to the opposing coalition, appearing in the 18 Dec 2020 list of anti-Artemis guilds that became [[Goose]]{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}, and remained there until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} No war-bloc membership was recorded after 2021; Valkyrie, with Imperial a member, was last mentioned on 19 Sep 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Alliances

- [[Valkyrie]] — 2 Jun 2015 – Oct 2016 (co-founder),{{cite:thread-159734|posts #2 and #7, 15 Oct 2016}} and Sep 2019 – 19 Sep 2022 (end date is last mention; see the join-date problem above)
- [[the-federation|Federation]] — 16 Feb 2018 – 10 Nov 2018
- [[Luna]] — 14 Feb 2019 – 19 Sep 2019 (founder)
- [[Artemis]] — 30 Oct 2019 – ~Dec 2020 (co-founder; departure date approximate){{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}
- [[Goose]] — by 18 Dec 2020 – 11 May 2021{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}

## History

### Founding
On 11 May 2021 [[Goose]] and [[Artemis]] collapsed on the same day. While thirteen guilds formed [[Valhalla]], nine formed Khaos: [[Aequitas]], Wheres The Finish, Nerfuria, Tartarus Wrath, Ultra Violet, Fuzzy Spiders, ChinaNumberOne, Cyphrus Code and Eden — most of them the bloc that had joined Goose in its final spring.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Tartarus Wrath was created days after the founding and joined mid-May; Cyphrus Code's stint appears to have lasted only until late May.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

A megalist post of 25 May 2021 announced that “the two major alliances both disbanded and got new names… Valhalla and Kaos”.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|post #136, Dream, 25 May 2021}} No public Khaos roster was ever posted; by then alliance rosters lived in a private Google Sheet.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

### The war with Valhalla and Vanir
The [[valhalla-khaos-war|Valhalla-Khaos war]] began the day both blocs formed and outlasted Valhalla itself, with [[Vanir]] inheriting the opposing side.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} TheNoLifes — excluded from Vanir after turning on its Valhalla allies — joined Khaos around December 2021, becoming one of its leading guilds{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}} and erupting against the ex-Valhalla guilds that month.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war peaked in January 2022 at 500–800 territory exchanges per week{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} against an opposing coalition known as the Pineapple Pact{{cite:cameron-oral-history|oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}}, then faded through the spring.

### End
No dissolution was ever announced. Fighting faded to nothing by mid-July 2022{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}, and when the fourteen-guild [[Cucumber Company]] roster was posted to the megalist on 26 June 2022, replacing the old alliance listing, Khaos was gone, with several of its guilds, Aequitas among them, inside the new bloc.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Khaos}}

## Legacy
Khaos was the last opponent of the Valhalla line, and its fade set up the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]]: within months its guilds and their former enemies were trading territory as allies inside Cucumber Company.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

Kingdom Foxes [Fox] carries one of the longest continuous histories in Wynncraft guild warfare, spanning [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]] to the 2020s.

## History

### Foundation (2014)

The guild came out of two competing proposals of April 2014: Fibunny's United Federation of Animals and, in response, [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]]'s Animal Kingdom.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2014}} LoveLusting established the Kingdom of Foxes on 2 June 2014.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2014}}{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section IX: The Alliance}} A design of separate branches was abandoned in July for a linear hierarchy, and in August the United Federation of Animals was absorbed whole, its founder becoming the first Viceroy of the Foxes.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jul 2014 and Aug 2014}} The first Foxen Inquisition, a review of the membership, ran from 24 to 28 September 2014 in anticipation of the release of guilds.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2014}}

Guilds themselves arrived that winter. The Nether's Ascension merged into the Kingdom of Foxes in December 2014 as Her Majesty's Army and left after about fifteen days; the guild was incorporated in-game as Kingdom Foxes [Fox] on 22 December 2014, the day [[the-guild-update|the Wynnter Update]] implemented guilds, and CptShroom raised the Foxen Royal Navy [RFN] as a subordinate guild.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2014}} The Foxen Royal Navy was disowned on 24 April 2015.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2015}}

### Kingdom of Foxes and Valkyrie (2015-2016)

'Kingdom of Foxes' co-founded [[Valkyrie]] with [[Imperial]] on 2 June 2015 — an alliance 'not established for the purpose of war', governed by an Electorate of guild masters, that became the longest-lived in Wynncraft history.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} The alliance was relaunched twice, in August and October 2016.{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, relaunch of 29 Aug 2016}}{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, relaunch of 15 Oct 2016}} [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]], styled Queen of the Foxes, founded the guild{{cite:thread-89227|post #1, LoveLusting}} and the alliance.{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, LoveLusting}} The founding date was chosen for the guild's first anniversary.{{cite:gdoc-1iacdk2t_3tzwo_a|Part I (1.1) Our History}}

The year before it had passed through two confrontations. The Wynnter War of January 2015 was a month of tension between the Tetra Alliance and the Grand Entente, and comparable tensions with [[legio|Legio Praetoria]] followed in March.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2015 and Mar 2015}} [[spham|Spham]] was brought over from [[kangronomicon|Kangronomicon]] in April 2015 to help revive the guild and was voted out by its members shortly afterwards.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2015}} The merger that produced Valkyrie counted the Kingdom of Foxes as part of Legio Praetoria on a formality, and it left with [[imperial|Imperial]] and the Knights of Valor a few days later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2015}}

The guild then refused every offer made to it. Kangronomicon approached the Foxes and Imperial for an alliance in September 2015 under Dar_Krusos and was declined on isolationist grounds; [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]] invited both guilds that November and was refused too.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2015 and Nov 2015}} On 20 November 2015 the Kingdom of Foxes introduced guild awards in the form of orders, medals and decorations — the first guild to do so, by its own history — and held the first Foxen Award Ceremony in Troms eight days later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2015}} Ceremonies became the guild's fixed institution, held two to four times a year in Nesaak, Ragni, Cinfras, Troms and elsewhere for the next five years.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2015 – Apr 2021}}

Valkyrie ran a joint operation, Operation Old Glory, from 1 January 2016, and the Foxes and Imperial began a joint re-branding on Imperial's first anniversary a fortnight later.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2016}} Snowing was crowned Queen Consort at the Spring Ceremony in Cinfras on 5 March 2016. The Ordo Exodus — the departure of Holders of LE, [[libertas|Libertas]], Death Reapers and others from Ordo Malleus — ran from 22 February to 9 March 2016, and Ha Ha United and Holders of LE were announced into Valkyrie at Imperial's second award ceremony on 18 March.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb 2016 and Mar 2016}} LoveLusting handed the crown to Kurumi on 5 April 2016 and reclaimed it on the 26th, redistributing the guild's titles and offices on her return.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2016}} The Queen's Cross, the guild's highest decoration, was awarded for the first time on 2 June 2016, to Misty.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2016}}

### The disbandment, the re-registration and the revival (2016)

LoveLusting disbanded the Kingdom of Foxes on 2 July 2016 after a dispute. [[drew1011|Drew1011]] declined to relay the quarrel — "I was not part of it and have not heard the story from anyone without massive bias" — writing only that "it ended with Ari disbanding her guild".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 8, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The cause of the disbandment was never recorded. He wrote that "after Ari disbanded Fox, a few rogue Hax members recreated it with the same name and tag"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 9, composed 26 Feb 2018}}: the guild listed in the API today, created on 3 July 2016, one day after the disbandment — a hostile re-registration by outsiders, not a rename by the guild itself.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

LoveLusting proposed a revival on 21 November 2016, and the new guild was created on 24 November 2016: "So, on November 24th, we created Foxton Legacy [Eon]. Foxton Legacy because Ari's name in the guild lore was Arianna Foxton, and Eon to represent that her legacy would last an Eon."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 9, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The guild carried that name for roughly its first two and a half months, because the Fox name and tag were unavailable. Drew1011's forum profile records him as "King of the Foxes" from 1 December 2016{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-members-drew1011-2157|Drew1011 forum profile custom-title chain}} and the community guild timeline dates the revival to 3 December 2016{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} — both a week or so later than the creation date his narrative gives. The guild's own handbook accounts for all three dates: the new guild was created on 24 November 2016 and declared as [Eon] on the 25th, its thread was posted on 1 December, and on 3 December a deal returned the original Kingdom Foxes name and tag and the first State Council was formed.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section X: Historical Timeline, Nov–Dec 2016}} The Guild History instead dates the establishment of Foxton Legacy to 25 November 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2016}} LoveLusting left the guild again on 10 December 2016, giving up the office of Council Designer.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section X: Historical Timeline, Dec 2016}}

![Four Discord messages of 21 November 2016 in which Ari (LoveLusting) tells Drew1011 to "take my crown" and "reestablish the kingdom". Drew1011's account presents this exchange as the start of the Kingdom of Foxes revival; the screenshot comes from that account.](/images/chronicles/storytime/24-image.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|screenshot dated 11/21/2016, part 9}}

The guildless members of the disbanded guild were absorbed by a guild founded the same day: House of Sentinels [Snt], created on 2 July 2016 by Pyrias.{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}} The House of Sentinels, Drew1011 wrote, "was created to house the now guildless Fox members. Misty and Pretzule, two ex Fox members, were its leader and Co-Leader", and "Snt had taken Fox's place in Valkyrie"; the Misty of his narrative is Pyrias.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 8, composed 26 Feb 2018}} He names the same person as Queen of the revived guild from 24 November 2016 until she stepped down on 28 January 2017, LoveLusting being restored on 7 February 2017.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 10, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

### Government

The revived guild was governed by a State Council of seven portfolios — Secretary, Justiciar, Chancellor, Designer, War Commander, Treasurer and Advisor — whose holders alone carried the in-game rank of Chief, above Captain, Recruiter and Recruit.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Sections III and IV}} Councils were numbered afresh at every reshuffle, and nine of them sat between 3 December 2016 and 12 February 2017. The first was [[drew1011|Drew1011]] as Chancellor, Teumessi as Secretary, [[killerfish|Killerfish]] as Justiciar, 01100110111 as Advisor and LoveLusting as Designer.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section XI: State Council Timeline}}

Titles ran alongside the ranks and carried no power of their own: royalty, viceroyalty, five grades of nobility from duke to baron, and a minor nobility of lords, ladies, dames and knights, each with its own form of address.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section V: Titles and Addresses}} A Table of Honour set out fourteen awards in four classes, the highest being the Queen's Cross, for "Extreme loyalty and dedication to the State Council, or an act of never-ending valour and gallantry"; wearing a medal in a forum signature that had not been awarded meant immediate demotion.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Sections VI and VII}} An elected Prime Minister was added to represent the gentry in Parliament from 16 April 2017, when Whimsicality won the first election; the office ran through regular elections until at least April 2021.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017 – Apr 2021}}

The handbook named six priority territories — Temple of Legends, Ahmsord, Animal Bridge, Jungle Lake, Crater Descent and Desert East Lower — capped spending at 3,000 emeralds per territory, told warriors to move on after two failed attempts at the same target, and made attacking an allied territory a demotable offence.{{cite:gdoc-1b8e1nh_ate9h69n|Section VIII: Territory Priorities & War Policies}}

### The Emperium of Wynn (2017)

Kingdom Foxes was a member of the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]]. By 17 October 2017 it was one of the alliance's four remaining member guilds, listed as "Kingdom Foxes [ Fox ] - Owner LoveLusting/Drew1011".{{cite:thread-202724|post #1, OP as last revised 17 Oct 2017}}

Drew1011's account describes two separate memberships. The first began in about May 2017 on a 14–4 guild vote, with Fox holding three of the alliance's six judge seats, and ended thirteen days later after an argument between alliance officers and Fox members in the alliance Discord.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 11, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The second began in about September 2017, a decision he says he and LoveLusting took the day after he demoted four members of the guild's Parliament; he wrote that it "caused a significant amount of members to join and form their own guild, KingdomPhoenixes [Phx]".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}} The guild's own history dates that first membership to 22 April – 5 May 2017, a span of thirteen days, and gives its end as a dispute between the Foxes and many of the alliance's members; it dates the second to 23 September 2017, three weeks after Drew1011 was elected Shadow Advisor of the Emperium, an office open to candidates from outside the alliance.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2017, May 2017 and Sep 2017}} KingdomPhoenixes split from Kingdom Foxes in September 2017{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} and was established on 23 September 2017{{cite:thread-204381|post #1, 24 Sep 2017}}; the motive appears only in his account. He also attributed the guild's later turn to warring to the rivalry that followed, calling it "the single most important cause of Fox's transformation from a purely community guild to one of the top War guilds in the community".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 12, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

Drew1011 held the title "Viceroy of the Foxes" from 7 February 2017 to 7 February 2019, the title he was still carrying when he wrote the Federation Tribute.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} Other officers of the era included Goden, who rose from recruit to guild leader and was named among the Federation's foremost war leaders,{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} and Robturne.

### The Coalition (2017-2018)

In October 2017 Kingdom Foxes co-founded the [[Coalition]] with KingdomPhoenixes, Gilded Sparrows and House of Sentinels; the Coalition took the Wynn Province on 23 Nov 2017, wiped [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] on Christmas Day, and gained full map dominance.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Drew1011 places Fox and KingdomPhoenixes as the two co-founders, with Gilded Sparrows third and House of Sentinels fourth, and describes the alliance as built "with the sole purpose of bringing down War Syndicate".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 13, composed 4 Mar 2018}}

### The Federation era (2018)

When five guilds split off in February 2018, starting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]], Kingdom Foxes went with the Coalition remnant into the Federation and remained until [[the-federation-dies|its collapse on 10 Nov 2018]].{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} The territory allocation announced inside the Coalition on 16 Feb 2018 assigned Fox 36 territories, in North Canyon and Nesaak.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|allocation announcement of 16 Feb 2018, part 17}} In April 2018 Fox was the map's largest holder, at 82 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback leaderboard capture, 16 Apr 2018}} In the winter interregnum that followed, the community timeline records 'valk owning most of Gavel'.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

### Institutions and the Eternal War (2018)

Kingdom Foxes built standing military and civil institutions through 2018: the Royal Dragoons on 14 February, the Royal Academy on 2 May, the 1st Royal Fusiliers on 7 July and the 2nd on 4 August, the three warring regiments merging again that August and September.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb–Sep 2018}} A second Foxen Inquisition was held from 17 to 20 May 2018 after an information leak was discovered.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|May 2018}} The Royal Engineers were publicly acknowledged as a guild institution on 18 April 2020, when [[nitrogen2oxygen|Nitrogen2Oxygen]] was appointed their first representative to Parliament.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2020}}

BuildCraftia [BCr] attacked territories assigned to Kingdom Foxes on 24 March 2018 while both guilds were inside [[the-federation|the Federation]], and was voted out of the alliance on the 30th; the fighting that followed was called the Eternal War and ended on 19 September 2018 when BuildCraftia's leader was banned.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Mar 2018 and Sep 2018}} Within Valkyrie, the alliance split the Durum Isles between its members on 16 April 2018 and invited [[emorians|Emorians]] to join on 5 May.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Apr 2018 and May 2018}} Two long defensive actions of that summer were recorded by name: the seven-hour Battle of Nether's Gate on 17 June 2018, in which The Hive was the focus, and the sixteen-hour Siege of Ranol's Farm of 29–30 July, in which Kingdom Foxes was.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2018 and Jul 2018}}

### The wars of 2019

Kingdom Foxes left the Federation on 10 November 2018 and declared war on [[hackforums|HackForums]] on 13–14 November to check its expansion in Wynn. Further declarations followed: on 12 December 2018 against Achte Shadow, Wrath of Poseidon, Beyond the Scene, Spectral Cabbage and TheNoLifes, in defence of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] and Emorians territory, and on 26 December against [[diamonddeities|DiamondDeities]] and HackForums.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Nov 2018 and Dec 2018}}

[[Luna]] fought Kingdom Foxes across 300+ territories from 15 Feb 2019 — Imperial alone attacked Fox 660 times.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Peace came stepwise, and each settlement divided ground rather than awarding it. The DiamondDeities war ended on 10 January 2019 with Lava Lake declared free-for-all, the HackForums war on 8 February with Sky Islands split, and a second DiamondDeities war, declared on 17 February, on the 24th with Molten Heights split and Molten Reach declared free-for-all.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jan 2019 and Feb 2019}} The Treaty of Rodoroc with [[DiamondDeities]] took effect 2 Mar 2019, and the Treaty of Ternaves (6 Jul 2019) split the dissolved Celestial Tigers' land; Fox joined Luna on 8 Jul 2019. Kingdom Foxes declared war on [[fantasy|Fantasy]] on 7 June 2019 in what it called the Second Canyon War and claimed the Air Temple region on the 19th, and on 6 July it was attacked by more than fifteen guilds at once, including HackForums, DiamondDeities and BuildCraftia, in a day it called the Sunday War; two days later DiamondDeities and HackForums were wiped and Fox entered Luna.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Jun 2019 and Jul 2019}} Its departure on 18 Sep 2019 collapsed Luna. Three days earlier it had co-founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]], which it left on 2 Nov 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} [[Terra]] wiped Imperial, Paladins United and the rest of Luna from the map on 7 September 2019, and Kingdom Foxes, the last Luna guild still holding ground, declared a ceasefire the next day; it left the Council to take part in Imperial's Reconquista, which recovered the Imperial and Paladins United homelands on 3 November.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Sep 2019 and Nov 2019}} On 21 December 2019 it became the first guild to hold every Silent Expanse territory at once, and the following day it passed 50,000 recorded wars.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2019}}

### Artemis and after (2020-2022)

By March 2020 Kingdom Foxes was a member of [[Artemis]],{{cite:thread-263975|9 Mar 2020}} remaining through [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021. Three guilds left the alliance and attacked it on 18–19 December 2020, and on 16 January 2021 an attack by [[goose|Goose]] took Kingdom Foxes to zero territories for the first time since February 2018.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Dec 2020 and Jan 2021}} On 5 February 2021 the guild dropped all its territorial claims and announced a turn away from warring, after reassessing its direction in the wake of an overhaul of the guild system; it returned to warring on 3 April 2021.{{cite:gdoc-1kajulcrdc0cpf1j|Feb 2021 and Apr 2021}} It joined [[Cucumber Company]] in spring 2022, one of the alliance's fourteen guilds that June;{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} it appears to have left in early July 2022, after which it fought its former bloc.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Fox was still a Valkyrie member as late as 19 September 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

