## Origins

The thread's opening line, as last edited in October 2018, reads "Started by few descendants of another kingdom"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1, as last edited 9 Oct 2018}}. Drew1011 quoted the same sentence in a different form — "Started from a few descendants of crumbling Kingdom..." — and wrote that the word "crumbling" was what began the feud between the two guilds{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L826–830}}. The opening post was edited more than a year after it was written; which wording stood in September 2017 is not known.

Drew1011, then Fox's Viceroy, identified the "kingdom" as [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and attributed the split to Fox's decision to rejoin the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] — "It caused a significant amount of members to join and form their own guild, KingdomPhoenixes [Phx]"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L810–813}} — and wrote that the new guild copied Fox's structure{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L824–825}}.

The guild reached level 31, and its first star, four days after it was created, and level 41 on 5 November 2017.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entries of 9-27-17 and 11-5-17}} Iron was its first Viceroy; Alhecks was promoted in his absence on 9 October 2017, and on 15 October ElegantDeath briefly held the title of King while AurumKitsune spent half a day in Kingdom Foxes.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Oct 2017}}

An internal challenge came "after about a month": "the government officials decided that they wanted to try to take over the monarch... those that tried to start the coup got demoted"{{cite:thread-204381|post #1}}. Drew1011 described a different-looking episode in early October 2017, in which AurumKitsune handed the guild to ElegantDeath and briefly rejoined Kingdom Foxes before taking it back{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L853–863}}; the guild's own history dates that episode to 15 October.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Oct 2017}} Whether the two were the same event is not known.

### The November Exodus

At AurumKitsune's request, Drew1011 joined the guild on an alternate account on 2 November 2017 and became Viceroy in place of Alhecks.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}}{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-2-17}} The appointment split the guild, and the two Phoenix accounts of what followed differ. One dates the break to 3 November and has members leaving of their own accord after failing to force AurumKitsune's resignation, then banding together to create the Serpentem Empire [SNK].{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017}} The other dates it to 4 November, names [[elegantdeath|ElegantDeath]], Whimsicality and Alhecks, and records them as removed for high treason and "forever forbidden from coming back" after trying to have the queen hand the guild over to them.{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-4-17}}

AurumKitsune passed the crown to [[thundderr|Thundderr]] on 22 November 2017 and resumed it in January 2018 on her return.{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Nov 2017 and Jan 2018}}{{cite:gdoc-1m7ns_yvlupswxmr|entry of 11-22-17}}

## War Syndicate and the Coalition

KingdomPhoenixes joined [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] and left it over the leadership episode above{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L856–863}}. Weeks later, in mid-October 2017, the guild co-founded the [[coalition|Coalition]] with Kingdom Foxes; Gilded Sparrows joined third and House of Sentinels fourth{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L869}}{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Oct 2017 entry}}.

![Discord message from the KingdomPhoenixes parliament channel, author "King ElegantDeath": "Now I know you all hate Fox, but they are the enemy of our somewhat enemy, Tnt / I'm somewhat thinking about a temporary alliance with them purely for the sake of elimination of BCr".](/images/chronicles/storytime/41-image.webp)

The guild held mainland territory when the Coalition took the whole Wynn province on 23 November 2017, and was on the alliance's roster at the declaration of war on 21 December 2017{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L927–941}}. It left the alliance on 1 February 2018 and rejoined on the 8th, and Drew1011 was crowned King Consort on the 9th{{cite:gdoc-1v5kpnrdnydscdrz|Feb 2018}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1033}}, and the division of Wynn announced on 16 February 2018 assigned it "Mid canyon"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|screenshot of the announcement of 16 Feb 2018}}, 24 territories{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}}.

KingdomPhoenixes was a member of the [[the-federation|Federation]] through that alliance's collapse in November 2018, when Drew1011 credited AurumKitsune with "setting up the discord and coming up with things such as the 2/3 majority voting rule"{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}.

## Structure

The guild's ranks were a copy of the Kingdom of Foxes' arrangement of titles over in-game ranks. Its leaders were a King or Queen holding the owner rank and the power to override any decision, a Prince or Princess as heir, a Viceroy or Vicereine as second-in-command, and an elected Prime Minister who carried the gentry's concerns to parliament. Beneath them ran a nobility of dukes, marquises, earls, viscounts and barons — the last three serving as head, senior and junior regional managers — and a gentry of baronets, knights, squires and pages.{{cite:gdoc-1q2iebjuyn91dxov|Structure of Phx}}

Lego_DW answered [[drew1011|Drew1011]]'s tribute on 13 November 2018 asking recognition for "the absolute gods of war this alliance created" — himself, 21(n), [[goden|Goden]], _Antho74_, InnerJoker, 0x7cf and snowy — who "along with too many others to credit, were the ones that really held the alliance together in terms of war power".{{cite:thread-237070|post #18, Lego_DW, 13 Nov 2018}} It is the only list of [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s war leaders anywhere in the record.

In April 2020 he gave the alliance's genealogy differently from the accounts around it: "Coa never technically 'beat' WS rather when AA split from coa, Coa and WS merged to wipe a common enemy, this was a creation of fed."{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, 4 Apr 2020}} His conclusion — that the Federation was a [[coalition|Coalition]]–[[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] merger — matches the rest of the record; his premise that no wipe of War Syndicate occurred does not.

His forum profile records guild offices between October 2017 and July 2020: chief of The Mage Legacy and of Sins of Seedia, and owner of ZephraShredders.{{cite:wynncraft-forum-profiles|Lego_DW, member 88629}}

Lev98bug was a chief of [[eden|Eden]] during [[artemis-goose-era|the Artemis–Goose era]].{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #72, 19 Jan 2021}}

On 19 January 2021 [[99loulou999]] of The Dark Phoenix wrote the name [[goose|Goose]] on [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] for the first time anywhere in the record; Lev98bug confirmed his own guild's membership half an hour later, asking the maintainer to add it: "Eden is in Goose if you could add that:))".{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #71-73, 19 Jan 2021}} The two posts are the earliest written evidence that the anti-[[artemis|Artemis]] coalition had taken a name.

Eden had been among the anti-Artemis guilds listed in [[sheepn|Sheepn]]'s "Guild Moderators" thread of December 2020, a month before the name appeared.{{cite:thread-279337|posts #1–#20, 18–19 Dec 2020}}

lotuss led Sins of Seedia, one of the three guilds that created the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] inside [[the-federation|the Federation]] on 25 March 2018.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

He posted the pact's public thread on 5 June 2018, describing Aesir as "an alliance, or if you will sister-ship pact, between 4 warring and growing community guilds".{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}} The thread gives the pact's own origin story — [[fantasy|Fantasy]] and Sins of Seedia became friends during the [[war-syndicate|War Syndicate]] era, were separated when Fantasy entered the [[coalition|Coalition]] and Sins of Seedia warred against it, and were reunited inside the Federation — and names two leaders for each member guild.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018, last revised 21 Jul 2018}}

His guild's co-leader [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]] is credited by [[drew1011|Drew1011]] as the first to accept the merger proposal that created the Federation.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}

## History

### Formation
Luna was formed on 14 Feb 2019 by [[Imperial]], [[Emorians]], Blacklisted, BuildCraftia and others, explicitly to counter [[SOL]], the bloc left standing after [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s fall.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The community timeline lists [[Kingdom Foxes]] among the founders, but Luna was at war with Fox from its second day.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### The war on Kingdom Foxes
From 15 Feb 2019 Luna fought Kingdom Foxes across more than 300 territories; Imperial alone attacked Fox 660 times.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war ended when Fox joined Luna on 8 Jul 2019 — the day after the Treaty of Ternaves, in which Fox, [[The Simple Ones]] and ThisIsMurica divided the territory of the dissolved Celestial Tigers.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

### Full map control
After fending off an attack on Kingdom Foxes in July 2019, Luna wiped every guild on the map except [[Avicia]]; Avicia joined on 17 Jul 2019, and Luna held the entire map.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

{{map:2019-07-17|Luna at full map control}}

### Luna as the Valkyrie bloc
[[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]], writing on the opposing side in September 2019, described not a new alliance but a renaming: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians" broke a summer raid on Kingdom Foxes, took the map in under two days, and thereafter appears in his account as "the Valkyrie alliance, now calling themselves the Luna alliance".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” to “ASSAULTS ON BCR”, 14 Sep 2019}} He blames the raid's failure on Valkyrie's "controversial use of sub guilds", by which main-guild members "could defend land more quickly by branching into sub guilds", and names Blacklisted and BuildCraftia as the first defectors, followed by Avicia and The Simple Ones.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” and “THE FORMATION OF LUNA”, 14 Sep 2019}}

The renaming account matches Luna's role as the public war-fighting face of the [[Valkyrie]] network{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, but not the recorded dates: Luna formed in February 2019 against SOL, while Arkada places the bloc's emergence after the midsummer raid and counts Imperial and [[Paladins United]] as long-standing Valkyrie members, though their Valkyrie membership is first recorded in September 2019.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} The discrepancy is set out on the [[imperial|Imperial]] and Paladins United pages.

### Revolt and collapse
On 29 Aug 2019, after a leadership dispute, Emorians and Avicia left Luna and declared war on Imperial, spiralling into a large war over Gavel; ThisIsMurica was kicked the next day for sending fighters, and [[Terra]] formed in the chaos on 30 Aug.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} Arkada adds a cause for the Emorians' turn from neutral exile to belligerent: Luna "seized all of its lands" after the departure, which he judged "a large mistake", since it made the Emorians sympathetic to the resistance.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“A RAY OF HOPE”, 14 Sep 2019}} In the Luna–Terra war of 7–19 Sep 2019, The Simple Ones defected to Terra on 8 Sep and Terra took map control the same day{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} — over 2,000 exchanges swept across 322 territories in ten days.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} A week of Luna counter-raids failed, and on 14 Sep 2019 Luna mounted an organised counter-raid that Terra had been warned of by a spy. Arkada wrote the same day: "In the morning, Luna struck, but we struck harder. In the late afternoon, Luna struck again, but we struck even harder."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“LUNA'S RETALIATION”, 14 Sep 2019}} Kingdom Foxes left on the 18th, and Luna collapsed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

