## Legacy
Luna's fall handed the map to Terra, whose core went on to found the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]]. Luna itself was the war-fighting face of the much older [[Valkyrie]] community network.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Lux Imperius was announced in the guild subforum on 16 September 2016 by valvoid, posting under the name xMC_Master11x{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Lux Imperius! Community Alliance!, valvoid, 16 Sep 2016}}, as an alliance "founded by @xMC_Master11x, @motoki1, @BlackbirdMC, @Loxotus, and @Arkam initially for war and community purposes. Lux Imperius is now a community alliance that values honor, prestige, and respect."{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} It sits among the cluster of non-war alliances that formed in [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]] alongside [[halcyon|Halcyon]], [[seraphim|Seraphim]] and [[aurelion|Aurelion]], while [[hackforums|HackForums]] and its partners held most of the territory map.

## History

The member guilds, with their leaders and founding dates, were: Dragon's Arise [DsA], "founded in July of 2016 by @xMC_Master11x"; UltimateXeons [UXs] under motoki1, "a Community Guild (Also Semi-War)"; Eternal Legacy [ETL], led by Commer after nicedoge509 and dated to 27 February 2015; WarLords [War] under Arkam; GrimNation [GrN] under MagicGum; and Beasts [BST] under Beastovrlrd.{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} Beasts was announced as a new member on 12 October 2016.{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #29, 12 Oct 2016}}

Membership was closed and deliberately kept small. "As lux imperius prefers to invite guilds without them asking we will look in about Forum Ninjas", Loxotus told one applicant{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #31, 12 Oct 2016}}; valvoid told another that "generally we don't let many guilds in as it is much harder to do events, it is less prestigious, etc."{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #37, 13 Oct 2016}} Both requests were refused on 15 October, because "the alliance would become too large".{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #48, 15 Oct 2016}} Asked why an alliance that admitted nobody kept a public thread at all, Yuno F Gasai answered for it: "So they could posts announcements and so that everybody will know they exist."{{cite:thread-153722-p03|posts #54 and #55, 16–17 Oct 2016}}

The thread nonetheless drew a response from the bloc that held the map. TheHipster posted a mock-declaration signed "BLACKLISTED" — "I see, so you plan to build an army of weaker powers to gain a foot against us... when you hear the drums of war, the only light to pass under the shadows of our steeds will be the fires of our guns"{{cite:thread-153722|post #16, 17 Sep 2016}} — which Yuno F Gasai read as confirmation of who felt threatened: "That short paragraph you wrote is what members of a powerhouse write when an alliance is made against them. The only current powerhouse is hax."{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #21, 18 Sep 2016}} A month later TheHipster disclaimed it as a joke{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #50, 16 Oct 2016}}, and the argument that followed set out [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]]'s place in that bloc.{{cite:thread-153722-p03|posts #49 and #52, 16 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p04|post #62, 20 Oct 2016}}

## Membership

As of 25 October 2016 the roster named six guilds: Dragon's Arise [DsA], UltimateXeons [UXs], Eternal Legacy [ETL], WarLords [War], GrimNation [GrN] and Beasts [BST].{{cite:thread-153722|post #1, opened 16 Sep 2016, last revised 25 Oct 2016}} Earlier that month it also included a seventh, Aquafinity [Aqu], "created by @Loxotus and @Wynncraftian on 9/2/16"; Loxotus described it as "allied since creation".{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #30, quoting the opening post, 12 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p02|post #38, 13 Oct 2016}} No departure was announced, and UltimateXeons' own recruitment thread still listed Aquafinity a year later, so whether the omission was a removal or an editing slip is unrecorded.{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, "Old alliances" list, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} The alliance predates machine-recorded alliance data, which begins in January 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

Membership of one alliance did not preclude membership of another in this period. Dragon's Arise appears earlier in the year among the guilds of the Astrafteri Affinity, a bloc formed around January 2016 that [[hackforums|HackForums]] also joined.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L352–358, composed 26 Feb 2018}}{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} Lux Imperius itself appears to have taken no part in the territory war.

## The Ordo Malleus misattribution

UltimateXeons' recruitment thread carries an "Old alliances" section headed "(Lux Imperius)" and listing six tags — DsA, ETL, War, Aqu, GrN, BST.{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, "Old alliances" list, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} The list has been misread as the membership of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]], because motoki1 announced joining Ordo Malleus in the same thread in February 2016.{{cite:thread-109350|post #7, motoki1, 20 Feb 2016}} The two rosters are unrelated: Ordo Malleus' only recorded roster is the twelve-guild list in the same thread's opening post, headed by the rule "Don't attack the territories that ally guilds own".{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} The six tags belong to Lux Imperius, not [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]].

## Legacy

No dissolution was ever recorded; the alliance's last recorded business, on 19 October 2016, is an Aquafinity event planned for December 2016, to which "All leaders of a guild in Lux Inperius is invited and is allowed to bring 1 friend."{{cite:thread-153722-p03|post #60, 19 Oct 2016}}{{cite:thread-153722-p04|post #61, 19 Oct 2016}} By 30 November 2017 [[ultimatexeons|UltimateXeons]] had moved it to an "Old alliances" list and its own live alliance section read "None at the moment!"{{cite:thread-109350|post #1, as last revised 30 Nov 2017}} Two members reappear later: Dragons Arise in [[aurelion|Aurelion]]{{cite:thread-135191|post #1}}, and Beasts under Beastovrlrd in the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]] of 2017.{{cite:thread-188024|post #1, member-guild roster}}

**Mr_Robin_Hood** opened the thread that created [[the-banhammer|The Banhammer]] on 8 June 2016, the first of two anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] alliances posted that month.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: The Banhammer (anti-hax), Mr_Robin_Hood, 8 Jun 2016}} His opening post gives the earliest hard territory count on record for [[hackforums|HackForums]] — "its that Hax currently owns 94 territories" — and the proposal it justified: "the only way for us to be able to beat them / is if all of the guilds unite!... we create one big alliance / where none of the guilds in the alliance attack eachother so that / even weaker guilds can hold territories."{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}}

He ran the alliance from a forum conversation, asking guild owners to message him directly{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}}, renamed the thread on the evening it was posted{{cite:thread-130386|post #16, 8 Jun 2016}}, and spent most of his subsequent posts defending it against the charge that it was a hate thread. "It was never intended to hate on HAX i know they are a hard working and honourfull guild," he wrote on 9 June. "its just that i think the smaller guilds could really benifit from an alliance because of how strong hax is right now."{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #26, 9 Jun 2016}} Asked why he singled out one guild, he answered with a comparison of holdings: "a bunch of guilds that have a lot of territories...... like who? TTZ with about 12% of what hax has? or WTh with a nice 3%?"{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #29, 9 Jun 2016}} His last recorded post, thanking a poster who had spoken up for the alliance, reads: "I was about to give up on this whole thing and you really saved my day."{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #40, 9 Jun 2016}}

His guild membership was never recorded, and nothing else about him is known.

**Naraka00** led [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] [BLA] with [[neonrider|NeonRider]] from the guild's creation on 19 January 2016, and kept its recruitment thread through 2016 and 2017.{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} Under the heading "ALLIANCES AND ALLIES", the thread stated from the inside the arrangement of the bloc that held the 2016 territory map: "We are allied with Libertas (Lir) and Hackforums (Hax)."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} No other member guild of the bloc wrote the alliance down.

The guild styled itself as pirates — "Yo-ho-ho. We are Blacklisted, a guild of friends who aim to claim ultimate victory!" — with its capital at Selchar, territory "composed by the great ocean islands", and Treasure Thursday, a weekly war night whose prize was five unidentified legendaries "for the person who gets more territories".{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} He handled the guild's applications himself through 2016.{{cite:thread-131893|posts #7 and #9, 22 Jun 2016}}

He was again among Blacklisted's leaders in 2018{{cite:thread-219617|post #1, as last revised 29 Aug 2019}}, and he remained active on the Wynncraft forums long after: in August 2022 he replied to a guild recruitment thread with a moderation notice, "Hi, avoid bumping your thread so much, you can only bump it twice per day."{{cite:thread-301804|post #10, 3 Aug 2022}} As of September 2026 his forum account carries the Staff Member, Mod Manager and Moderator banners and gives his guild as Blacklisted.{{cite:thread-131893|forum profile banners and guild field in the page markup, captured 3 Sep 2026}}

**NeonRider** led [[blacklisted|Blacklisted]] [BLA] from its creation on 19 January 2016, jointly with [[naraka00|Naraka00]]: "Our guild was founded on 19/01/16 and the leaders are @NeonRider and @Naraka00."{{cite:thread-131893|post #1, as revised 15 Sep 2017}} In the guild's successor thread of 2018, milo890 wrote "the leaders are @NeonRider, @Naraka00, and I".{{cite:thread-219617|post #1, as last revised 29 Aug 2019}}

He entered the era's public argument over territory once. On 2 March 2017, in a thread demanding that [[hackforums|HackForums]] be capped and in which Blacklisted had just been named among the bloc's holders, he answered the premise directly: "It's cute that you guys think that my guild is super op but in reality it's only me doing wars and we're down to 1.7mil emeralds."{{cite:thread-179383|post #18, 2 Mar 2017}}{{cite:thread-179383|post #7, 1 Mar 2017}} No other statement by a Blacklisted leader about the guild's warring capacity survives from the period.

He was still posting in the guild's second recruitment thread in September 2018{{cite:thread-219617|posts #15 and #16, 20 and 25 Sep 2018}}, and his forum profile still gave his guild as Blacklisted as of September 2026.{{cite:thread-179383|forum profile guild field in the page markup, captured 3 Sep 2026}} Nothing else about him is recorded: no founding account, no war record, and no departure.

Niflheim's four members were simultaneously war-alliance guilds, and it dissolved on 18 December 2021, the same day [[Vanir]] collapsed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

## History
Niflheim's formation was never documented; the earliest recorded event in its history is [[ShadowFall]]'s join on 27 December 2020.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} By 7 July 2021 the alliance comprised [[Avicia]], Blue Nations United [IBT] (the guild known today as IceBlue Team), ShadowFall and TheNoLifes; when the three guilds other than ShadowFall joined is not known.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #146, HungHung, 7 Jul 2021}}

All four members belonged to war alliances at the same time: all were in [[Goose]] by February 2021, and three of the four went on to found [[Valhalla]] in May.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Niflheim itself took no recorded part in any war.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

Niflheim was officially dissolved on 18 December 2021 — the same day Vanir collapsed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}

