## Legacy
Alongside [[Hestia]] and the [[Empire of Nemract]], Niflheim was one of the few community alliances of the era whose membership is known{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}; beneath the war-alliance churn of 2020–2021 ran a quieter, more stable social layer.

Ordo Malleus was created on 6 November 2015 and fell on 9 March 2016.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "-= Ordo Malleus =-", Paladin A'renos, Nov 6, 2015}}

## The record

The alliance's own thread — "**-= Ordo Malleus =-**", opened by Paladin A'renos on 6 November 2015, 15 pages and 296 replies, locked, last post by Ha_Ha_Redstone on 10 March 2016 — carries its opening post in the state it stood in on 9 March 2016, the day the collapse began{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}}, an earlier state of that post quoted back within the thread in November 2015{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #25, Tapu_Fini, 10 Nov 2015, quoting the opening post}}, and the replies of its first three weeks.{{cite:thread-93754-p03|p3 #60, 23 Nov 2015}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}} [[drew1011|Drew1011]], a founding member, wrote in 2018 that the thread had been deleted and was restored on request in early 2017, and that he had used it to recover dates: "many of the dates and minor events during the Ordo parts of this story would have been educated guesses without it."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L692–695, composed 26 Feb 2018}} For the alliance's internal politics the principal witness is still that retrospective account of 2018, which is partisan, was written by a party to the disputes it describes, and is in most particulars the only witness for what it reports. A separate chronology, compiled afterwards, tracks admissions, refusals, expulsions and the collapse to the minute; it dates the alliance's creation to 8 November 2015, two days after the thread's own first replies.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|chronology, 27 Oct 2015 – 11 Mar 2016}}

## History

### Founding, 6 November 2015

The alliance was founded on 6 November 2015 by seven guilds: Kangronomicon [Fuq] led by Dar_Krusos ("Kru"); Holders of LE [HoL] led by Drew1011; Ha Ha United [HHU] led by Ha_Ha_Redstone ("Red"); End of Everything [EoE] led by "Shadow"; Hack Forums [Hax] led by TheDarkSoul; ToastedPandas [TnP] led by Yamipanda and [[killerfish|Killerfish]]; and Sinners [Snr] led by Rani.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L169–178, composed 22 Feb 2018}} Drew1011 gave the purpose in one sentence: "Ordo Malleus was created for the sole purpose of defeating Concordia."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L179, composed 22 Feb 2018}} Glitchedslayer likewise put the alliance at seven guilds{{cite:thread-143392|post #13, Glitchedslayer, 9 Aug 2016}}; the twelve-guild roster below dates from February 2016, after five further admissions.

The opening post named Kangronomicon as the founder and gave a guild count of eight — the seven guilds and the Wynn Wide Merchants Organisation [WWMO], a trading body "led by The Three Members of Four" that was carried on the roster to the end as an unofficial member.{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #25, Tapu_Fini, 10 Nov 2015, quoting the opening post}}{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}} Paladin A'renos, styled High Grand Master of the Ordo Malleus, claimed it for himself on the thread: what mattered was not how long a thing lasted but "the experiences, the relations you acquire and the friends you make ... That is why i have created this alliance."{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #22, Paladin A'renos, 9 Nov 2015}}

The alliance was assembled by **Paladin A'renos**, then a chief of Kangronomicon, who recruited the member guilds and created the leader chat, while Dar_Krusos held the senior authority; the requirement that each member guild elect a council of four officers — a Diplomat, a War Commander, a Community Manager and a Merchant — came from Kangronomicon shortly before the alliance was announced.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L148–162, composed 22 Feb 2018}}

### Governance

The alliance ran on four tiers of coordination. Above the guild councils sat a **leader chat**; a superseded earlier chat was renamed "**The Board**" and "quickly became very inactive and was almost never used"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L190, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. The rename followed a manoeuvre Drew1011 described carrying out himself within weeks of the founding: he canvassed the other member-guild leaders, secured a majority, and had alliance business moved to a new leader chat that excluded Paladin A'renos, citing A'renos's manner toward the other leaders{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L186–190, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. Above the leader chat, Dar_Krusos later created a top tier called the "**Shadow Government**", described as "the highest leadership tier within the alliance", whose members were Drew1011, Killerfish, Yamipanda, Ha_Ha_Redstone and Rani{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L248–257, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. The opening post set out what those councils were for. War Commanders led attacks and defence and coordinated with their counterparts in the other guilds; Diplomats were "the voice of the guilds", responsible for inter-guild relations and for resolving disputes; Community Managers ran events and kept the alliance's public reputation; and Merchants kept emeralds flowing into the guild banks. Councils could be elected by members or appointed by the guild leader, and merchant and community guilds were excused the War Commander requirement.{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #25, Tapu_Fini, 10 Nov 2015, quoting the opening post}} Five alliance rules ran alongside them, of which the third was "Refrain from attacking allies' territories."{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}} General business ran through a hundred-person Skype chat{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L344, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, and new members of member guilds were asked to join "the Ordo Malleus skype chats".{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} Voting was by guild rather than by person: when Killerfish was added to the leader chat, Drew1011 checked "to make sure that TnP still only had one vote when it came time to vote on things", and was assured they did.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L253–254, composed 22 Feb 2018}} Admissions and expulsions were decided by votes of the leaders.

The mechanism by which the alliance won the territory war was a system of assigned territories. "Each guild was designated certain territories to focus, and as long as we actually succeeded in defeating Concordia, we would get to keep them… We attacked those territories and defended them religiously, and before long Concordia gave up on touching those territories," Drew1011 wrote; Holders of LE held Nesaak and Mining Base, End of Everything was given the desert, and ToastedPandas held Ternaves.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L197–202, composed 22 Feb 2018}} The opening post's own allocation, published in November 2015, differs in its details and covers the whole map: Kangronomicon took Lusuco, Ragni, the City of Troms and Rymek; Holders of LE the Savannah and Nemract; Ha Ha United Nesaak and Ternaves; End of Everything Almuj and the desert; ToastedPandas the Ocean Islands and the Nether Portal; Sinners Nivla Forest and Time Valley; and HackForums the Jungle and Detlas.{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #25, Tapu_Fini, 10 Nov 2015, quoting the opening post}} The blocks were reassigned as membership changed: by the winter Holders of LE was holding sixteen named Nesaak and Mining Base territories, Ha Ha United's original allocation.{{cite:gdoc-1sqfxhjwewtphua7|"Holders Of LE — A captain's guide", designated territories}} An associated tactic governed how allied territory was recovered: a guild retaking a territory for an ally left "minuscule defenses" so the owner could take it straight back, a rule whose breach later became a grievance against HackForums.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L336–338, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

![A territory map from Drew1011's account showing Ordo Malleus at its height, with every guild holding its designated block: ToastedPandas around Detlas and Ternaves, HaHaUnited around Nemract and the savannah, Sinners in Nivla Forest, Holders of LE at Nesaak Transition and HackForums at Elkurn.](/images/chronicles/storytime/12-image.webp)

### The Concordia war and the forum campaign against Ordo

The alliance's target, [[early-guild-era|Concordia]], was effectively finished within weeks. Drew1011 recruited Historical [UEZ] out of it, and its leader 3zPz posted a thread titled "Concordia Disbanded" — dated 8 November 2015, two days after Ordo's founding rather than the three Drew1011 recalled — after which, he wrote, "most people began to consider the alliance dead", although Ezura of Validus denied it in the thread itself.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L203–204, composed 22 Feb 2018}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "Concordia Disbanded", 3zPz, Nov 8, 2015, 27 replies, locked}}

The alliance's dominance produced a public reaction on the forums. On 28 November 2015 tangler, a chief of Validus, opened "Come Join! The Odeus Anti-Validus Pact"{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}}, a thread in which, Drew1011 wrote, it "was revealed that Arenos had tried to bribe guilds in to joining Ordo Malleus"; he qualified the allegation — "I cannot entirely recall if this was true, but I believe I remember a discussion with Arenos where he admitted to it" — and said the thread devolved into A'renos and Ezura posting screenshots of each other before a moderator closed it.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L215–226, composed 22 Feb 2018}} The moderator Mekyr made the thread's last post the following day.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "Come Join! The Odeus Anti- Validus Pact", tangler, Nov 28, 2015, last post Mekyr, Nov 29, 2015}}

The same day a thread appeared under a new account called **TheOrdoSpies**, announcing that members of the alliance were passing information to Validus. Its text was never preserved. The account was banned and the thread locked the same day, and no moderator ever disclosed whose alt it was.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L227–232, composed 22 Feb 2018}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1: "Ordo Spies", TheOrdoSpies, Nov 28, 2015, locked}} Drew1011 speculated that the account belonged either to tangler or to 3zPz.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L231, composed 22 Feb 2018}} "All this talk of spies within Ordo made many of us paranoid," he wrote, with no evidence to act on.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L232, composed 22 Feb 2018}}

![The thread posted by the account "TheOrdoSpies" on 28 November 2015, claiming that Ordo Malleus members were leaking to Validus. The account was banned and the thread locked the same day.](/images/chronicles/storytime/09-image.webp)

### Admissions, expulsions and the February 2016 roster

Historical [UEZ] was welcomed into the alliance on the thread on 12 November 2015{{cite:thread-93754-p03|p3 #42, Paladin A'renos, 12 Nov 2015}}{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entry of 11/12/15}} and left on 1 December; on that same day End of Everything was expelled by vote for failing to hold the desert it had been assigned, its territories passing to HackForums, a boss-killing service called the **Demon Hunters** was founded, and [[libertas|Libertas]] was admitted{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L234–247, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. Death Reapers were rejected on a first application and admitted on a second days later{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L233, L255–256, composed 22 Feb 2018}}; grimmcat's White Wolves were revived to join{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L258–260, composed 22 Feb 2018}}; Necronomicon [Feq] was promoted from Kangronomicon subguild to full member and complained about having no assigned territories until ToastedPandas and Holders of LE donated three each{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L261–268, composed 22 Feb 2018}}. Megitsune [Bri], under Amaranthe, joined about a week after Gavel's release and left on 1 February 2016, its leader disbanding the guild rather than passing it on{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L326, L362–364, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. Applications were closed after Gavel because wars had stopped working, and reopened in late January{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L329, L361, composed 26 Feb 2018}}; the dated chronology puts the closure on 28 December 2015, with Megitsune's admission, and the reopening on 29 January 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entries of 12/28/15 and 1/29/16}} It also fixes the intake of that winter: Death Reapers refused on 29 November and admitted on 7 December, Papa Johns [PPJ] refused on 4 December, Libertas admitted on 8 December, White Wolves on 13 December, and Heroes of Wynn still applying as late as 26 February 2016. On 16 December 2015 Holders of LE and ToastedPandas each gave up three territories for Necronomicon.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entries of 11/29/15 – 2/26/16}} The alliance ran a fortnightly Nether games with Lightly Toasted Heroes from 10 February 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entry of 2/10/16}} WynnTheory [WTh], bought by Paladin A'renos after he left Kangronomicon, was admitted on 3 February 2016 over Drew1011's objection{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L366–370, composed 26 Feb 2018}}, and The No Lifes and Ultimate Xeons followed within days{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L375–376, composed 26 Feb 2018}}.

On 20 February 2016 the UltimateXeons owner motoki1 posted "Update: Joined the Alliance Ordo Malleus!"{{cite:thread-109350|post #7, motoki1, 20 Feb 2016}}, and the guild's recruitment thread carried an alliance section headed by a single rule, "Don't attack the territories that ally guilds own", above twelve guilds:{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}

| Guild | Tag |
|---|---|
| Kangronomicon | Fuq |
| Ha Ha United | HHU |
| ToastedPandas | TnP |
| TheNoLifes | TNL |
| Holders of LE | HoL |
| Wynn Theory | WTh |
| Sinners | Snr |
| White Wolves | WWA |
| Necronomicon | Feq |
| [[libertas|Libertas]] | Lir |
| Death Reapers | DxR |
| UltimateXeons | UXs |

End of Everything, Historical, Megitsune and [[hackforums|HackForums]] are absent from the list, all having left or been expelled by then.

### The expulsion of HackForums

[[hackforums|HackForums]] was expelled and later readmitted. "I think you're forgetting that Hax was actually kicked out of Ordo", Drew1011 wrote in August 2016{{cite:thread-143392|post #7, Drew1011, 9 Aug 2016}}, and earlier that summer: "Hax was one of the original guilds, although we kicked them out, and then for some reason, let them back in"{{cite:thread-133666|post #6, Drew1011, 27 Jun 2016}}. Neither remark gave a date or a reason. The expulsion fell on 7 January 2016.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entry of 1/7/16}} Immediately after TheDarkSoul was banned from the forums, Drew1011 raised the ban in the Shadow Government chat as reflecting badly on the alliance, Yamipanda moved a vote, and the vote to expel was unanimous or nearly so. The stated grievances were repeated accidental attacks on allied guilds and the practice of defending recaptured allied territory with full mob defences instead of the light defences the alliance's recapture tactic required.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L333–342, composed 26 Feb 2018}} HackForums is absent from the 20 February 2016 roster{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}, and its own recruitment thread listed a different alliance — "Astrafterí-affinity" — on 11 February 2016{{cite:thread-109319|post #13, ThePastryMaster, 11 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}}. Paladin A'renos re-invited the guild around late February 2016.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L435–436, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

### The collapse, February–March 2016

Drew1011 called his account of the collapse the most partisan part of his story: "in no part of this story will this be made more apparent than in the collapse of Ordo. Parts of it will contain my biased perspective. If you ask others who were here, they might give a completely different perspective."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L393–397, composed 26 Feb 2018}} He described the leadership as having drifted into two informal factions — one around Paladin A'renos with Dar_Krusos and Rani, one around himself with the ToastedPandas leaders and Ha_Ha_Redstone — and said nobody acknowledged the split at the time.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L404–410, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

ToastedPandas left on 22 February 2016, after which Dar_Krusos left the Shadow Government{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L381–385, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. On 25 February a row broke out over A'renos having invited another guild, Sleeping Knights, into a "sub-alliance" without the other leaders' approval; Drew1011 created a chat excluding him and moved to expel WynnTheory, and the motion failed, with most leaders abstaining or declining{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L414–431, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. Ha Ha United left about 3 March{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L438–439, composed 26 Feb 2018}}. Drew1011 withdrew Holders of LE on 9 March 2016 at approximately 5:27 PM EST, and the alliance ended the same day: "The alliance would crumble a mere 16 days after TnP left."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L390, L454, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

In his withdrawal message he wrote that "instead of this alliance being a balance between all the guilds, it become more of a dictatorship between Kru and Arenos", and gave as his ground that Ha Ha United and ToastedPandas had been Holders of LE's closest allies and that their departure had left his guild alone on one side of an unnamed dispute.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L454–455 and the accompanying screenshot, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

![Drew1011's message withdrawing Holders of LE from Ordo Malleus on 9 March 2016, the departure that ended the alliance.](/images/chronicles/storytime/15-image.webp)

The community timeline dates the collapse two days later: "11th Mar, Ordo Malleus collapses after a chain of leaves started by Holders Of LE [HoL] approximately 2 days before."{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}} The alliance thread's last post is dated 10 March 2016, by Ha_Ha_Redstone.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|complete census of Alliance-prefixed threads, page 1}} A chronology kept to the minute gives the whole sequence and sides with the timeline. Holders of LE left at 5:27 PM EST on 9 March, Death Reapers at 5:31, Libertas and HackForums at 5:55. WynnTheory went the next afternoon at 3:46, and with it, in the chronology's words, "the only few people who could successfully lead the alliance give up, and the alliance is dead". Necronomicon left at 6:50 AM on 11 March, White Wolves at 7:34, Kangronomicon at 7:39 and Sinners at 12:20 PM.{{cite:gdoc-1csqnkuglsisvsvx|entries of 3/9/16 – 3/11/16}} Drew1011 wrote that afterwards "many people began naming me as its destroyer. Did I truly deserve that title? To this day I'm still not sure."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L457, composed 26 Feb 2018}} Both Paladin A'renos and Dar_Krusos left Wynncraft shortly afterwards; A'renos returned about a year later, while Kru "has never returned, except to pass down leadership of Kangronomicon."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L462–463, composed 26 Feb 2018}} Holders of LE and Ha Ha United joined [[Valkyrie]] on 18 March 2016.{{cite:community-guild-timeline|Mar 2016 entry}}{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L472–473, composed 26 Feb 2018}}

## Membership

Three rosters survive. The opening post of November 2015 gives eight names — Kangronomicon, Holders of LE, Ha Ha United, End of Everything, HackForums, ToastedPandas, Sinners and the Wynn Wide Merchants Organisation.{{cite:thread-93754-p02|p2 #25, Tapu_Fini, 10 Nov 2015, quoting the opening post}} The February 2016 roster above gives twelve.{{cite:thread-109350|post #11, Drew1011, 20 Feb 2016, quoting the opening post}} The opening post as it stood on 9 March 2016, hours before the collapse, lists eleven guilds beneath a stated count of ten, plus the merchants' organisation: Death Reapers under jjaayyddoonn, Wynn Theory under PaladinArenos, Holders Of LE under Drew1011, Kangronomicon under Dar_krusos, Libertas under yosteric5, Necronomicon under LordMuttonChops, White Wolves under Grimmcat, Sinners under Rani, The No Lifes under chownick, UltimateXeons under motoki1, and HackForums under TheDarkSoul — readmitted after its January expulsion.{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}} Machine-recorded membership data begins in January 2018, after the alliance's end.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Culture

The alliance ran a public programme alongside the war. Its thread advertised a Cross-Province Race, a Thanksgiving Ball and a Valentine's Ball, and a demon-hunting and exploration service called the Pandemonic Paragons; it carried banner art credited to Sparklepopz, coralialia and KompriZe, two versions of an alliance forum signature, and a nine-question guild application form.{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}} Two alliance poems were printed on it: "The Passage of Kinship" by Paladin A'renos and "The Blacksmiths of Peace", a twenty-line verse by Dar_Krusos ending "Our shields together, under The Hammer / United en masse 'til the final year."{{cite:thread-93754|post #1, opening post as last edited 9 Mar 2016}}

## Legacy

Ordo Malleus became the yardstick veterans reached for whenever a later power looked too large. When Glitchedslayer compared [[hackforums|HackForums]] to it in August 2016 — "both were known as the king of guild territories and stopped everyone from getting and holding land"{{cite:thread-143392|post #10, Glitchedslayer, 9 Aug 2016}} — Drew1011 objected to the comparison itself: "if you're going to try to compare your guild to the greatest alliance to inhabit Wynn, at least spell it right. It's Ordo Malleus. (Order of the Hammer)"{{cite:thread-143392|post #7, Drew1011, 9 Aug 2016}}, adding "I was just trying to defend the memory of the alliance that my friends and I developed."{{cite:thread-143392|post #9, Drew1011, 9 Aug 2016}}

Glitchedslayer wrote that Ordo "collapsed from the inside because of guilds fighting and was much slower because they had the split the land together" — a structural contrast with Hax, a single guild that "gets much more land for itself so it lvls faster and is much harder to die because of inner fighting".{{cite:thread-143392|post #10, Glitchedslayer, 9 Aug 2016}} Drew1011's gloss on the difference was about the era rather than the structure: "people cared a lot more about guilds then and there were a lot more active guilds fighting for territories".{{cite:thread-143392|post #11, Drew1011, 9 Aug 2016}} He also credited Ordo with the first guild ball, the community-event format later alliances copied: "First guild ball was hosted by Ordo. Legio never hosted events."{{cite:thread-188024-p04|post #61, Drew1011, 22 May 2017}}

The alliance kept a social afterlife. A reunion Discord server was created in early 2017; Paladin A'renos joined it, the deleted alliance thread was recovered through it, and it was where A'renos began planning the alliance that became the [[emperium-of-wynn|Emperium of Wynn]].{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L691–700, composed 26 Feb 2018}} Members still identified with it years later — "Once an Ordo brother always an Ordo brother", written on the 2018 Federation tribute thread.{{cite:thread-237070|post #6, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

Paladins United [PUN], created on 2 Jun 2017 by EHTYSCYTHE,{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}{{cite:thread-246617|post #1, opened 5 Apr 2019, last edited 19 Sep 2022}} belonged to more alliances than nearly any other guild. Its forum thread was opened in April 2019 by Carrie, one of the guild's leading figures through the 2019–2020 alliance wars; Vholtz_ owned the guild at that date, and by 2022 ownership had passed to Auxiliary_ — when is not recorded.{{cite:thread-246617|post #1, opened 5 Apr 2019, last edited 19 Sep 2022}}

## History

### The Coalition and the Federation (2017-2018)

By late 2017 Paladins United was in the [[Coalition]]. On 17 Feb 2018 it left with four other guilds to co-found [[Alliance Alliance]], starting the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]]; when the war ended on 20 Mar 2018 the AA guilds were absorbed into [[the-federation|the Federation]], where PUN served two stints (to June, and from August until [[the-federation-dies|the collapse of 10 Nov 2018]]).{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

### 2019: Terra to Artemis

In the [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|alliance wars of 2019]] Paladins United appears to have fought with [[Terra]] against [[Luna]], staying until 30 Oct 2019 — the day it co-founded [[Artemis]] with [[Imperial]] and Caeruleum Order.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} It was in [[Valkyrie]] by 14 Sep 2019,{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} and in the community alliance [[Hestia]] from around mid-2020;{{cite:thread-278112|post #10, 2 Dec 2020}} its thread listed both until 19 Sep 2022.{{cite:thread-246617|post #1, opened 5 Apr 2019, last edited 19 Sep 2022}}

### The Valkyrie join-date problem

Whether 14 September 2019 marks a join or only a first mention is unclear. [[arkada|Arkada]], writing that day, opens: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians, have existed for longer than I've played Wynncraft."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|Leonhart_Arkada, 14 Sep 2019}} He wrote as a hostile observer describing an established, long-standing bloc of four guilds — yet Paladins United and Imperial are recorded entering Valkyrie only in September 2019, after [[Emorians]] had left it in the revolt of late August 2019, so that on those dates the four guilds were never simultaneously members.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} The dates probably mark first mentions rather than joins: Valkyrie's threads had gone quiet after 2017 and no membership list was published between then and the 2020s.{{cite:thread-159734|posts #2 and #7, 15 Oct 2016}} Carrie, writing in March 2020 as "the leader of PUN", placed the guild "in Valk, in a large alliance".{{cite:thread-263975-p03|p3 #41, 9 Mar 2020}}

### Side-switch and the blocs (2020-2023)

By December 2020 PUN had drifted from Artemis to the opposing coalition — it appears in the 18 Dec 2020 anti-Artemis list that became [[Goose]]{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} — and stayed until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, then joined [[Valhalla]] at its founding and followed it into [[Vanir]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} At the start of Season 8 (autumn 2022) it joined the renamed 'Smtn else' — later [[smtn elf]] — alongside [[The Simple Ones]] and TerraLune, remaining until the alliance's quiet end in mid-2023.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}

