Seraphim was formed in the middle of [[hackforums|HackForums]]' map dominance and defined itself by refusing to fight, and its thread became the venue for the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]]'s most substantive argument about that dominance.

## History

The thread opened on 8 August 2016 with an unusually candid statement of purpose. "Do you like guild wars? Do you like dominating the territory map and controlling the entire province of Wynn...? Well get the fuck out then," the opening post began, before setting out the terms: "The Seraphim alliance is a 100% community based alliance... There's no intention of actively providing support for guild wars."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}} What it offered instead was a way around the guild-slot cap of the period — "an opportunity to grown their communities beyond the bugged-out, limited guild slots" — plus shared art and thread graphics, and the founder was frank about his motive: "80% of the reason I set this up is because I want an excuse to make new graphics." Membership was deliberately non-exclusive: "any guild can join the alliance, regardless of if they are already in another alliance."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Within a day the thread was taken over by an argument between veterans about whether HackForums' position resembled [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]]' earlier control of the map. That exchange — Glitchedslayer against [[drew1011|Drew1011]], LeoDiesAlot and Yuno F Gasai — preserved much of what is known about Ordo Malleus, Hax's ejection from it, and the composition of the bloc holding territory in 2016{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}. LeoDiesAlot, a chief of [[libertas|Libertas]] and so describing his own guild's arrangement, said that Hax "work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories".{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, LeoDiesAlot, 9 Aug 2016}}{{cite:thread-119596-p09|post #171, yosteric5 naming LeoDiesAlot a chief, 11 Aug 2016}} The founder's own verdict on his thread: "Thanks for hijacking my thread gais. Appreciate it."{{cite:thread-143392|post #16, 9 Aug 2016}}

## Membership

Seraphim had four recorded member guilds: Saltiest, [[libertas|Libertas]], FOX and Holders Of LE.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening-post roster graphics}} In September 2016 Libertas held 60 territories, second only to HackForums' 146{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback Machine capture of the api.wynncraft.com guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016 (pre-2018 territory snapshots)}}, so a declared community alliance with no war function counted among its members the map's second-largest warring power. Holders Of LE was simultaneously a member of [[halcyon|Halcyon]]{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, opening post (Halcyon founded 5 Jun 2016 between ToastedPandas and Holders of LE)}} and joined [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] that October{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}}, which the alliance's own rules expressly permitted.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Seraphim predates the machine-recorded alliance logs, which begin in January 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No activity after the founding was ever recorded, and neither was the alliance's end. Its legacy is the argument it hosted: much of what is known about Ordo Malleus, and the clearest contemporaneous statement that HackForums was not acting alone, were written on the thread of an alliance set up as a joke about not warring.{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}

ShadowFall [Shy] was created on 21 Aug 2017.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} Its first years went unrecorded; its warring history begins in 2020.

## History

### An Artemis leader (2020)

In March 2020 ShadowFall's GoulartJJ posted on the forums as a leader of [[Artemis]], the map-holding alliance of the day.{{cite:thread-263975-p02|p2 #36, 9 Mar 2020}} The guild joined the community alliance [[Niflheim]] on 27 Dec 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The side-switch (2021)

On 1 Feb 2021, mid-way through the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]], the [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] recorded that 'BNU(IBT), SHY and TNL are all goose now' — a defection from the Artemis camp to [[Goose]].{{cite:thread-278112-p04|p4 #76, 1 Feb 2021}} ShadowFall fought with Goose until [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, then became a founding member of [[Valhalla]] and followed it into [[Vanir]], while retaining its Niflheim membership{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #146, 7 Jul 2021}} until that alliance dissolved on 18 Dec 2021, the day Vanir collapsed.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Into The Aquarium's orbit (2023)

By August 2023 ShadowFall was a subguild of [[The Aquarium]], part of the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact's shared infrastructure alongside Avoquarium [HQs] and Avicia's the Avos.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} How and when it passed into TAq's orbit is not known.

