On 18 December 2020 Sheepn, then of Diablo [DXI], opened thread 279337, "Guild Moderators" — the best-documented political flashpoint between the ignition of the war against [[artemis|Artemis]] and the naming of [[goose|Goose]] a month later. Its opening sentence supplies the era's clearest framing of the conflict: "there is currently an ongoing large-scale conflict between Artemis, the map-holder alliance, and a currently unnamed group of anti-Artemis guilds."{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}

The complaint was that "a moderator affiliated with a major Artemis guild" had banned two prominent members of the leading anti-Artemis guild for macro use, when the numpad spamming they described was "publicly known to be NOT bannable and allowed by moderation"{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}. The thread's thesis was structural rather than personal: "The root of the problem boils down to the moderation team failing to adapt to the modern way guilds operate even though many Moderators come from guilds, and a lack of set-in-stone rules for guilds related issues."{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}} Sheepn closed with a request not to "name drop or harass the moderator involved"{{cite:thread-279337|post #1, 18 Dec 2020}}.

The replies made the thread a record in itself. [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] answered that "Moderators will not ban players without reason"{{cite:thread-279337|post #17, 19 Dec 2020}}; Carrie of [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] located the real fault in the team's "lack of communication, being on the same page"{{cite:thread-279337|post #18, 19 Dec 2020}}; Miles_ questioned a rule enforceable only when players incriminate themselves{{cite:thread-279337|post #20, 19 Dec 2020}}. Read together with the guild tags of its participants, the thread also preserves the membership of the then-unnamed coalition — Diablo, Eden, [[avicia|Avicia]], HICH, Bovemists, Lily Pad, Ultra Violet, [[emorians|Emorians]], The Dark Phoenix, Paladins United and [[imperial|Imperial]] — and places [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] and Titans Valor in Artemis{{cite:thread-279337|posts #1–#20, 18–19 Dec 2020, read with the participants’ forum guild badges (badge markup, not post text)}}.

Sins of Seedia (SDU) was founded on 6 May 2017, per the official guild API.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} It spans nearly the whole recorded history of alliance warfare, from the Federation era to the present.

## History

### Federation era

Sins of Seedia enters the record as a founding-era member of [[The Federation]] in February 2018.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}} On 25 Mar 2018 it co-founded the [[Aesir Pact]] with [[Fantasy]] and IceBlue Team — a pact of sister guilds "especially dedicated to Gavel, and the birth place of Aesir, the canyon" — with its leader simplyinfinity_ named among the pact's creators.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opened 5 Jun 2018}} The Aesir guilds were the Federation's last defenders: as [[the-federation-dies|the alliance fell]] on 10–11 Nov 2018, they quit only after fourteen hours of constant warring, and Aesir died with the Federation.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, 11 Nov 2018}}

### Later blocs

The alliance record then goes quiet for over two years. Sins of Seedia reappears in [[Artemis]] from March 2021, staying until [[the-great-collapse|the alliance collapsed]] on 11 May 2021.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In the 2022 realignment it joined [[Cucumber Company]]; the alliance's full fourteen-guild roster — the last public alliance roster ever posted — was submitted to the forum megalist on 26 Jun 2022 by SDU's own TherapueticLiz.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} The guild carried through the rename into [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]] and stayed until the alliance's quiet end in June 2023.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

As of September 2026 the guild remains active — level 90, around 75 members, led by TherapueticLiz — holding no territories.{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}

