## Legacy
smtn elf was the last of the public super-alliances, and its unannounced death is the [[private-diplomacy-era|private-diplomacy era]] in miniature: no roster, no dissolution notice, just silence between two season posts. Its collapse set up the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact and the wars that followed.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## History

### Creation
SOL was created in the post-collapse chaos following [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s fall of 10 Nov 2018{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, around December 2018.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The war with [[Luna]]
On 14 Feb 2019, Luna was formed "as an alliance to counter SOL," and the two blocs fought through the spring as part of [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the Alliance Wars of 2019]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} SOL was still a current bloc in June 2019 — "the current SOL and Luna guilds"{{cite:thread-251543|post #1, Pikacal, 26 Jun 2019}} — and then disappeared as Luna consolidated the map in July. No dissolution was ever recorded.

### Roster
No member list of SOL was ever published. Its six guilds appear to have been [[DiamondDeities]], Achte Shadow, Wrath Of Poseidon, Beyond the Scene, Spectral Cabbage and, from January 2019, Ecliptic Awakening: all fought Luna's founders from Luna's founding onward — Beyond the Scene alone accounting for nearly 4,000 territory exchanges — while showing near-zero fighting among themselves.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} DiamondDeities' membership is consistent with the Treaty of Rodoroc — its peace with [[Kingdom Foxes]], effective 2 Mar 2019{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} — and with a late-2018 arrangement to share Molten Heights with Fox.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

## Membership
{{alliance:SOL}}

## Legacy
SOL bridged the Federation's fall and the alliance wars that consumed 2019: it inherited the map's chaos, provoked Luna into existence, and dissolved into obscurity without a recorded ending. Several of its members resurfaced in the autumn blocs — DiamondDeities and Achte Shadow both appear in [[Terra]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

**Tapu_Fini** founded [[the-separatists|The Separatists]] on 26 June 2016, the second of the two anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] alliances of that month.{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: The Separatists, Tapu_Fini, 26 Jun 2016}} At the time he posted under the name Supermariowifi and led The Anarchy, the alliance's founding guild; his forum profile still lists The Anarchy as his guild.{{cite:thread-133666|post #12, Drew1011, 27 Jun 2016, quoting post #11}}{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}{{cite:thread-133666|forum profile guild field in the page markup, captured 3 Sep 2026}}

His opening post is the earliest surviving written description of the bloc that held the 2016 map, and casts it as a duumvirate: "This enemy, known only has 'Hack Forums' quickly established their rule through military might... Soon after, another guild, [[libertas|Libertas]], joined the surge. The two guilds crushed all opposition and still rule with an iron fist."{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} The whole thread is written in Star Wars references, which he confirmed when a reader objected that separatists forming an alliance made no sense: "Ever seen Star Wars? In star wars the separatists were an alliance of systems that wanted to leave the republic."{{cite:thread-133666|post #11, 27 Jun 2016}}

He was candid about the odds — "Luck will definitely be needed to take down hax lol"{{cite:thread-133666|post #4, 26 Jun 2016}} and "even if we don't beat them, at least we can be an annoyance"{{cite:thread-133666|post #11, 27 Jun 2016}} — and, challenged on whether he had ever attacked the bloc at all, gave the only account of the alliance in action: "I mean lir and hax. And we have. Usually around Ragni. Katoa ranch we tend to attack a lot."{{cite:thread-133666-p02|post #23, 28 Jun 2016}} His last recorded posts, on 1 July 2016, argue for the guild-repair update over new content: "I'd rather have usable content then lots of content."{{cite:thread-133666-p02|post #34, 1 Jul 2016}}

## History

### Formation
Terra formed on 30 Aug 2019 in opposition to [[Luna]], amid the Emorians–Avicia revolt that had broken out the day before{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}; several of its guilds were already fighting Luna from 25 Aug.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

Terra was a merger rather than a fresh founding. After Luna took the map, [[arkada|Arkada]]'s guild [[Titans Valor]] joined **The Ascendancy**, "a small and weak band of guilds that resisted Luna through unsuccessful attacks"; as more guilds tired of Luna's reign, "small alliances similar to The Ascendancy merged together, forming a larger and more organized counter-alliance called Terra", Arkada wrote.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“ASSAULTS ON BCR” and “A RAY OF HOPE”, 14 Sep 2019}} By the time of the decisive raid the merged bloc fielded "nearly 15 guilds"{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}, more than the twelve otherwise recorded{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}; the roster was never published. The Ascendancy outlived Terra as a distinct grouping: its departure collapsed the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] on 23 Nov 2019.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Luna–Terra war
The war for the map ran 7–19 Sep 2019: over 2,000 attacks across 322 territories in ten days — a genuine full-map war, with only 37% of the fighting on the usual free-for-all hotspots.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} [[The Simple Ones]] defected from Luna to Terra on 8 Sep, and Terra took map control the same day; [[Kingdom Foxes]] left Luna on the 18th and Luna collapsed.{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} The decisive action was a weekend raid intended only to take [[Imperial]]'s land, which instead "ended in nearly six hours and resulted in the complete wipe of all Luna guilds except Kingdom Foxes", Arkada wrote{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}, followed on 14 Sep by a Luna counter-raid that Terra repelled.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“LUNA'S RETALIATION”, 14 Sep 2019}}

{{map:2019-09-08|The map as Terra took control}}

### Dispersal and fall
A week after victory, on 15 Sep 2019, Terra's core — Kingdom Foxes, [[DiamondDeities]], Titans Valor, The Simple Ones, [[Fantasy]], Phantom Hearts and Empire of Sindria — founded the Council of Canyon Kingdoms.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} [[Paladins United]] departed at [[Artemis]]'s founding on 30 Oct.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Terra itself fell on 2 Nov 2019, seven weeks after taking the map; on 10 Nov its fragments launched one final raid on the newborn Artemis.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

## Membership
Terra's founding roster was never recorded{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}; only The Simple Ones' membership is directly documented — it joined hours after leaving Luna. The other recorded members each mounted 100 or more attacks on Luna during the decisive September war.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

{{alliance:Terra}}

## Legacy
Terra ended the last period of single-alliance map control in 2019 and seeded what came next: its core formed the Council of Canyon Kingdoms, and Paladins United left it to co-found Artemis, the alliance that would anchor the following era.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

The Aquarium [TAq] is a Wynncraft guild created on 22 Mar 2020,{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-the-20aquarium|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} in the middle of the [[goose-artemis-war|Goose-Artemis war]]; its first territory exchange came the following day.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Its earliest alignment was never written down; it appears to have first fought on the anti-[[Artemis]] side of that war.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

## History

### The Valhalla years (2021)

On 11 May 2021, the day of [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]], The Aquarium was one of the thirteen guilds that founded [[Valhalla]], which took map control within days. When Valhalla reorganized as [[Vanir]] on 28 Nov 2021, The Aquarium was among the ten founding guilds; Vanir collapsed twenty days later.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Through the following winter it fought in the [[valhalla-khaos-war|war against Khaos]], which peaked in January 2022 and faded by mid-July — the run-up to [[the-realignment-era|the realignment]].{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### Cucumber Company to the Avocado split (2022-2024)

For guild Season 5 (spring 2022) The Aquarium joined [[Cucumber Company]],{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} appearing in the 14-guild roster posted to the [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] on 26 Jun 2022 — the last public alliance roster ever —{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}} and carried through the alliance's renames into [[smtn elf]].{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}} In June 2023 it and [[Avicia]] walked out, rejecting pressure to shrink their claims,{{cite:thread-308780|Avicia guild season post, 10 Jun 2023}} and as the two-guild [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact — Avicia called TAq "our unwavering ally" —{{cite:thread-310286|Avicia guild season post, 19 Aug 2023}} the pair waged [[the-avocado-split|a sniping and claim-taking campaign]] against their former allies into early 2024,{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} running shared infrastructure including the joint subguild Avoquarium [HQs] and the subguild [[ShadowFall]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Idiot Co war (2024-2025)

From 29 Apr 2024 The Aquarium fought [[Idiot Co]] in [[idiot-co-aquarium-war|the biggest war since 2021]] — a weekly peak of 5,045 territory exchanges — through mid-July 2024, with a second round from November 2024 into January 2025, spanning the Rekindled World map rework of 10 Aug 2024.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

