**The Banhammer** was a Wynncraft alliance of June 2016, the first of two anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] blocs opened within three weeks of each other. Its thread — carrying the guild subforum's Alliance prefix and titled "The Banhammer (anti-hax)" — was posted on 8 June 2016 by Mr_Robin_Hood{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Mr_Robin_Hood, 8 Jun 2016}}, and proposed one universal non-aggression pact so that smaller guilds could hold land against a guild then holding 94 territories.{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}} It belongs to [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]].

## History

The opening post set out both the grievance and the mechanism: Hax held 94 territories and was too strong for any single guild, so the guilds should unite in one alliance whose members would not attack each other, letting weaker guilds hold land.{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}} Guild owners were asked to open a forum conversation with Mr_Robin_Hood and would then be "added to a special alliance conversation" — the alliance's only recorded organ.{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}} An attached poll ran from "yes hax is ruining the guild experience for me" to "no you are just salty and mad"; its results were visible only to voters and were never published.{{cite:thread-130386|thread poll options, from the page markup}} The thread was also renamed on the evening it was posted; its earlier title is not known.{{cite:thread-130386|post #16, 8 Jun 2016}}

The response from the [[hackforums|HackForums]] side was immediate. "Wtf is this NATO you cant take down mother russia," Shawarma replied the same afternoon. "I will not stop till every inch of wynncraft is mine or my allies, my allies will attack you or be attacked if they revolt."{{cite:thread-130386|post #5, 8 Jun 2016}} Defenders argued the thread was simple resentment: "viva hax and screw all the haters. If you cant get and hold land, dont hate on those who can", wrote qqcora, who described the rival Astrafterí Affinity alliance as "the alliance i created" and said it "has over 10 guilds, and every single one of them would back hax up".{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #23, qqcora, 8 Jun 2016; and post #30, quoting qqcora, 9 Jun 2016}}{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Astrafterí Affinity, LordMuttonChops, 3 Apr 2016}} Mr_Robin_Hood answered that the alliance was not aimed at the guild's members: "it was never intended to hate on HAX i know they are a hard working and honourfull guild. its just that i think the smaller guilds could really benifit from an alliance because of how strong hax is right now."{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #26, 9 Jun 2016}} Cybersoap707, who had founded the Morsus Mihi alliance a month earlier{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: Morsus Mihi, Cybersoap707, 3 May 2016}}, offered the only coordination scheme anyone proposed: "If we get big enough, I think I might calculate and distribute territory areas equally to each guild in which they target any Hax Territories."{{cite:thread-130386|post #17, 8 Jun 2016}}

### The mid-June reversal

Within ten days the thread's participants were reporting that HackForums had collapsed on the map. "As of now Hax has ONE territory," wrote WhettoWen, a member of the Hax-allied guild UltimateXeons, on 16 June{{cite:thread-130386-p03|post #60, 16 Jun 2016}}, and on 18 June: "Hax is dead. They own no territory."{{cite:thread-130386-p04|post #77, 18 Jun 2016}} Buttless, a chief of World of Crafters, congratulated "everyone who participated in the alliance".{{cite:thread-130386-p04|post #63, 16 Jun 2016}}

The cause was disputed at the time. Cybersoap707 credited two member guilds — "All the Credit goes to Mythic Zodiac and The Crafters, when my guild was ready to attack we encountered a glitch that prevented us from attacking, it was fixed recently when Hax was already destroyed" — then narrowed the claim next day: "When I said destroyed i meant that Hax was basically put out of power. They're still a very powerful guild and in the top 5, but don't have over 90 territories anymore."{{cite:thread-130386-p04|post #78, 18 Jun 2016}}{{cite:thread-130386-p05|post #81, 19 Jun 2016}} Goden credited a guild outside the alliance: "Nether's Ascent took over Hax recently... and they've been able to hold the map decently well."{{cite:thread-130386-p05|post #94, 21 Jun 2016}} Yuno F Gasai of [[imperial|Imperial]] dismissed the episode: "So you took over for a couple of days, try to hold it forever now."{{cite:thread-130386-p04|post #79, 19 Jun 2016}} By 23 September 2016 HackForums held 146 of the map's roughly 332 territories, more than at any point in June.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}

## Membership

The opening post listed three member guilds — World of Crafters [WoC], The Wynn Guard [TwG] and MythicZodiac [MZS]{{cite:thread-130386|post #1, opened 8 Jun 2016, last revised 11 Jun 2016}} — of which only WoC and TwG appear in the version of the post quoted on 8 June, so MythicZodiac joined during the thread's first days; the same early version carried a line, later removed, asking Hax members not to reply.{{cite:thread-130386-p02|post #18, quoting the opening post, 8 Jun 2016}} On 20 June a poster added the tag "DragonSlayers [WkD]" beneath a quotation of the roster, but the opening post was never revised to include it.{{cite:thread-130386-p05|post #92, 20 Jun 2016}} No further roster was published, and no leader other than Mr_Robin_Hood was ever named. Territory exchanges were not recorded until January 2018, long after the alliance's time.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

The thread went quiet after 29 June 2016, and no dissolution was ever announced.{{cite:thread-130386-p06|post #101, 29 Jun 2016}} The next day a [[hackforums|HackForums]] chief remarked in a different thread that "right now there is 2 anti hax alliances"{{cite:thread-134638|post #13, 30 Jun 2016}}; the Banhammer and [[the-separatists|The Separatists]], posted eighteen days apart, appear to be the two. The community's verdict on such efforts was already settled before either began: "It didn't work, all those guilds no longer have any territory", an UltimateXeons member wrote of the previous attempts.{{cite:thread-133666|post #10, 27 Jun 2016}}

The **Federation** (tag **Fed**) was the dominant war alliance of 2018 on Wynncraft — the largest alliance the game had yet seen, holding the entire territory map for eight months and twenty-five days before collapsing in a single day on 10 Nov 2018. Founded and unofficially led by [[Drew1011]], it grew to 37–40 member guilds and gave its name to the [[federation-era|Federation era]].{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

## History

### Formation
The Federation was born from the fracture of the [[Coalition]]. On 16 Feb 2018 the Coalition published a guild-by-guild division of the province of Wynn; within an hour five guilds left and formed [[Alliance Alliance]] with two others, and held the map by nightfall{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}. The Coalition remnant merged with the remains of War Syndicate — the power the Coalition had wiped the previous Christmas — into a new alliance, founded and led by Drew1011.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

![The Discord @everyone announcement of 16 February 2018 setting out the Coalition's guild-by-guild division of Wynn, from HackForums' allocation down to Immortalish's single region. Its publication triggered the split that produced the Federation.](/images/chronicles/storytime/58-52bb6b02a8a9f0906e04907a12ab07bd.webp){{cite:drew1011-storytime|announcement of 16 Feb 2018, part 17}}

Drew1011 wrote that the merger was his own proposal, that he first messaged BuildCraftia's co-leader without response, and that [[simplyinfinity|simplyinfinity_]] of Sins of Seedia was the first to accept{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 11 Jul 2018}}{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}. He gives the name a mundane origin: "The name 'Federation' began as a joke, considering Coalition had also been named just by being a synonym for alliance, I joked we should do it again with the name Federation, but people liked it and it became our name", and says the bloc "copied the exact same structure that Coalition had"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}.

Even its genealogy was disputed among participants: Lego_DW described the Coa–WS merger in 2020 as "a creation of fed"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, Lego_DW, 4 Apr 2020}}, while Slayne posted a rival claim on the tribute thread on 14 Nov 2018 — "In a way, you could say that I created Fed because I (along with some others) created Double AA. Take that drew! Owait. Im also drew."{{cite:thread-237070-p03|post #45, Slayne, 14 Nov 2018}} The claim is causal rather than direct: "Double AA" is Alliance Alliance, whose split from the Coalition triggered the merger that produced the Federation.

### Governance
The alliance ran on a Discord server built by AurumKitsune of KingdomPhoenixes, thanked in Drew1011's tribute "for setting up the discord and coming up with things such as the 2/3 majority voting rule that contributed greatly to its success".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} That two-thirds majority is the bloc's only known decision rule; how it was applied in practice, and to what class of decisions, was never written down.

### The first battle, 17-19 February 2018
The war opened with an attack by Snowythewolf, a chief of Hall of Fame, on [[emorians|Emorians]]' Llevigar territories, chosen because she had heard the guild's leaders discussing a low bank. Drew1011 joined the attack on the night of the 17th and stopped at about 3 AM on the 18th with Llevigar still held; Emorians was defending at the full 1,000-mob cost of roughly 2,500 emeralds a defence despite being near bankruptcy. By noon on the 18th Llevigar had flipped and Emorians was, in Drew1011's words, "almost totally bankrupt".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}

Drew1011 wrote that he then coordinated the alliance's war effort personally for about fifteen hours, and that the Federation had "ballooned into at LEAST 22 guilds, fighting 7 of the strongest guilds Wynncraft had to offer". [[viaire|Viaire]] of [[fantasy|Fantasy]] defected from Alliance Alliance mid-battle on 18 February in exchange for keeping his canyon territories, after which "Fantasy immediately began targeting Hax".{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}} Fantasy's Alliance Alliance stint ran until 19–20 Mar 2018{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}; the defection and the stint's end were different events. Drew1011 credited [[iceblue-team|IceBlue Team]] with holding the night shift of 18–19 February and taking the Light Forest and Aldorei while the rest of the alliance slept.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}

### The wipe of HackForums
On 19 Feb 2018, three days after forming, the Federation attacked [[HackForums]]' 111 territories and [[the-wipe-of-hackforums|wiped them to zero]] in under 12 hours{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} — the end of Hax as a territorial power, a year after its 2017 peak of roughly 350 territories.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

After the Federation had taken Llevigar, the swamp, the Dark Forest and the Light Forest, "at the very latest hours of the 19th, Snowy announced it was time to attack Hax. At the time they held 111 territoires. Less than 10 hours later, they had none."{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}} Accounts differ on the duration — under ten hours or under twelve. A leaderboard of 22 Feb 2018 shows the map's largest holder with only 43 territories{{cite:thread-219744|post #1, 22 Feb 2018}}: guilds such as Blacklisted "managed to rise to the top of the leaderboards out of pure chance. They were not Fed so AA did not attack them, and they were not AA so Fed did not attack them", and so topped the table for about a day{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}}.

### When the map was won
The Federation took the map on 21 February 2018, four days into the war, holding 356 of 383 territories, or 93%, against Alliance Alliance's 24{{cite:territory-exchanges|daily ownership reconstruction, 5 Feb – 10 Apr 2018}}{{cite:territory-exchanges|356 of 383 territories, 21 Feb 2018}}. Drew1011's account agrees — "Three days after the Civil War had begun, Federation had won the map"{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}} — as does the arithmetic of his tribute, whose "8 months and 25 days" of map control counts back from the collapse of 10 November 2018 to mid-February 2018{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}.

Map control broke once. Federation holdings fell to 164 territories on 2 March and to 43, or 11%, on 3 March, with Alliance Alliance back at 308, recovering to 114 on 4 March and to roughly 300 from 6 March{{cite:territory-exchanges|Federation 43 of 383 territories, 3 Mar 2018}} — the interruption the tribute describes as "aside from ~3 days in March"{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}.

The community timeline instead dates the Federation's map control to 19–20 March{{cite:community-guild-timeline}}. Those are the days Alliance Alliance fell from 72 territories to one and the Federation reached 380 of 383 territories, or 99%{{cite:territory-exchanges|Alliance Alliance from 72 territories to one, 19–20 Mar 2018}} — the elimination of the opposing bloc and the end of the war, a month after the map changed hands.

### Map dominance
The Federation took full map control on 21 Feb 2018{{cite:territory-exchanges|356 of 383 territories, 21 Feb 2018}} and eliminated the Alliance Alliance guilds as a territorial force on 19–20 Mar 2018, ending the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]] and absorbing them.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} It held the entire map for 8 months and 25 days, with a roughly three-day interruption in March.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} On 16 Apr 2018 all fifteen territory holders on the map were Federation guilds, together holding 384 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|Wayback Machine guild-leaderboard API capture, 16 Apr 2018 (pre-2018 territory snapshots)}}

{{map:2018-04-16|The Federation's map at its height}}

The March interruption began with a game update. Drew1011 writes that "beginning almost as soon as the clock struck midnight and March 1st began, Hax & Co. began attacking Gavel. We quickly discovered that there had been a mob update and that they were using broken defenses that the vast majority of players were unable to overcome". Tntdestroyd coordinated the first two days of the counter-effort, concentrating it on House of Sentinels alone, and handed coordination to Drew1011 on 3 March; "by the 5th, the entire map once again belonged to Federation". [[paladins-united|Paladins United]] was admitted at [[slayne|Slayne]]'s request on 7 March, and House of Sentinels left Alliance Alliance on 12 March and returned to neutrality, at which point Drew1011 considered the war over.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 17, composed 30 Aug 2018}} His tribute thanks "@Tntdestroyd, for fighting hard to reclaim the map back in March".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} The trough of the relapse fell on 3 March, and the Federation was back near 300 territories from 6 March — a day later than the "by the 5th" of his account{{cite:territory-exchanges|Federation holdings, 2–6 Mar 2018}}.

Replying to the tribute on 13 Nov 2018, the member Lego_DW asked recognition for "the absolute gods of war this alliance created" — himself, 21(n), Goden, _Antho74_, InnerJoker, 0x7cf and snowy — who "along with too many others to credit, were the ones that really held the alliance together in terms of war power".{{cite:thread-237070|post #18, Lego_DW, 13 Nov 2018}} Of the seven, only Goden, a [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] officer, is otherwise known.

Membership churned heavily — [[Titans Valor]] alone served three separate stints.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Within the bloc, [[Fantasy]], Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team formed the [[Aesir Pact]] on 25 Mar 2018{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}, a pact of sister guilds dedicated to Gavel.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opening post (lotuss/simplyinfinity_)}} Fantasy itself left the Federation in late May 2018 — the departure was never recorded in writing, and sustained fighting began in the week of 28 May — and fought the bloc across more than 220 territories all summer before rejoining on 29 Oct 2018.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### Internal conflict, spring 2018
Drew1011 records an unstable spring: BuildCraftia's seizure of Serpentem Empire's share of the swamp without penalty; a dispute over the Sky Islands; an attack by BuildCraftia on Kingdom Foxes territories while a vote on their status was still open, and a retaliation by Fox, Imperial, Paladins United and The Hive that he says he called off himself the following morning; and a **vote to expel BuildCraftia opened on 30 March 2018**, which its leader pre-empted by leaving.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 18, composed 20 Jun 2019}} He also names an alliance that guild's leader attempted to build from inside the Federation, "Centurion"; a thread post of 25 April 2018 has Tntdestroyd writing "We have already began forming what it is your looking to do now, join us if you like"{{cite:thread-224905|post #3, 25 Apr 2018}}. Whether that guild was expelled or left of its own accord remained a live dispute between the two men into 2019.

### Collapse
At around 3 AM EST on 10 Nov 2018, one guild left the Federation — and the alliance cascaded apart within a day.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} In the sequence of [[the-federation-dies|the Federation's death]], The Hive had left a month earlier, then Odysseia; [[Imperial]]'s exit for independence "snowballed into a major attack on Fed together with the enemy alliance [Ent]"; Arisen followed, and after 14 hours of constant warring the Aesir Pact guilds quit, ending it.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, Ascended Kitten, 11 Nov 2018}} The tag **[Ent]** is the only identifier ever given for the opposing bloc, which is otherwise unrecorded. "What killed Federation was... internal affairs", wrote Drew1011 in his tribute, posted three days later with the full member roster.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

## Membership
The founder's tribute names 37 member guilds — one of them, "Death Reapers", is otherwise unknown — and with renames and re-joins the alliance counted 37–40 guilds.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} Three roster guilds renamed during the alliance's life: LE Flowers → [[DiamondDeities]], DogsAmongUs → White Lotus, As Darkness Falls → Constellations.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

{{alliance:Federation}}

## Legacy
The Federation's fall ended 2018's era of single-bloc dominance and opened a winter interregnum in which, per the community timeline, "all guilds keep to themselves with valk owning most of Gavel" — the territorial peak of the [[Valkyrie]] network.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} [[SOL]] was created in the post-collapse chaos{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, and [[Luna]] was formed to counter it in February 2019, beginning [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the Alliance Wars of 2019]].{{cite:community-guild-timeline}} No later alliance matched the Federation's duration of total map control.

[[tapu-fini|Tapu_Fini]] opened the alliance's thread on 26 June 2016{{cite:forums-wynncraft-com-forums-guilds-72-prefix-id-82-order-post-date-direction-asc|thread listing: The Separatists, Tapu_Fini, 26 Jun 2016}}, three weeks after [[the-banhammer|The Banhammer]] — the second of the two anti-[[hackforums|HackForums]] blocs of [[early-guild-era|the early guild era]] to open that month.

## History

Its opening post gave the earliest written description of the bloc that held the territory map, framing it as a duumvirate: "a deadly enemy rose from the defeated corpse of [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]]. This enemy, known only has 'Hack Forums' quickly established their rule through military might. Young aspiring guilds were crushed under the might of the tryhards... Soon after, another guild, [[libertas|Libertas]], joined the surge... Many distinguished scholars compare this rule of two to the ancient guilds of 'The Nether's Ascent' and 'Kangronomicon'."{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}

Enrolment was deliberately loose. A player could join The Anarchy directly "regardless of level or class", or "pledge your guild to The Separatists, and you way withdraw that allegiance whenever you feel the need. No guild is too small or too low level, heck, we are level 13! Strength in numbers!"{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} The Anarchy is described as the founding guild, a "Combat Guild" led by supermariowifi with the chiefs comrade_doge and superACE.{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}} The post closed with a disclaimer: "this is all for fun, no real hate to the Hack Forums and Libertas players, just to their 'Own everything' policy."{{cite:thread-133666|post #1, 26 Jun 2016}}

The reception was uniformly sceptical. WhettoWen of UltimateXeons pointed to earlier attempts — "To make a long story short: It didn't work, all those guilds no longer have any territory"{{cite:thread-133666|post #10, 27 Jun 2016}} — and a fellow member, valvoid, spelled out his own guild's position: "our alliance with Hax and Lir (we are UXs) is gonna let the three guilds keep their territory (we are like the only three guilds with any real territory) without anybody really taking it unless one of the guilds leaves or breaks the alliance."{{cite:thread-133666|post #13, 27 Jun 2016}} qqcora corrected the terminology — "ur alliance with hax and lir is a mutual land agreement" — and directed readers to the Astrafterí Affinity thread as "the actual alliance".{{cite:thread-133666|post #16, 28 Jun 2016}} [[drew1011|Drew1011]] wrote of HackForums' readmission to [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]]: "Hax was one of the original guilds, although we kicked them out, and then for some reason, let them back in."{{cite:thread-133666|post #6, 27 Jun 2016}}

The founder's own expectations were modest: "Luck will definitely be needed to take down hax lol"{{cite:thread-133666|post #4, 26 Jun 2016}} and "even if we don't beat them, at least we can be an annoyance."{{cite:thread-133666|post #11, 27 Jun 2016}} Challenged on 28 June to say whether the alliance had ever attacked the bloc, Tapu_Fini answered: "I mean lir and hax. And we have. Usually around Ragni. Katoa ranch we tend to attack a lot."{{cite:thread-133666-p02|post #23, 28 Jun 2016}} Tomix, replying for the bloc, disputed it — "I've never seen your guild try to take territory from us,weird heh"{{cite:thread-133666-p02|post #22, 28 Jun 2016}} — and WhettoWen's comment on the state of affairs was "it should stay that way", which Tapu_Fini accepted: "Fine by me. You guys seem nice enough anyways."{{cite:thread-133666-p02|posts #21 and #23, 28 Jun 2016}}

## Membership

No guild other than The Anarchy was ever named as a member, and none was recorded as pledging.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No dissolution or outcome was ever recorded; the alliance was last mentioned on 1 July 2016.{{cite:thread-133666-p02|post #36, 1 Jul 2016}} It was one of the two blocs behind the [[hackforums|HackForums]] chief Mrussell75's remark on 30 June 2016 that "right now there is 2 anti hax alliances", the other being [[the-banhammer|The Banhammer]].{{cite:thread-134638|post #13, 30 Jun 2016}} Neither bloc changed the map: in September 2016 HackForums still held 146 of roughly 332 territories.{{cite:pre2018-territory-snapshots|pre2018-territory-snapshots.json — Wayback Machine capture of the Wynncraft v1 API guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016}}

The Simple Ones [ILQ] was created on 5 Feb 2019 by Goatylicious, Saethar, GrandAdmiralAce_ and _Infected_gaming, "as a way to find more people to play and have fun with"{{cite:thread-255067|post #1 (OP as last edited 16 Sep 2020)}}{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3/guild, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} — nine days before [[Luna]] formed. It joined Luna around the alliance's founding, though only its departure was documented.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## History

### Founding and the Aetherius merger (2019)

Three days after it was founded, on 8 February 2019, the guild merged with XeraAndromeda's [Aeu] The Aetherius{{cite:thread-255067|post #1 (OP as last edited 16 Sep 2020)}}. XeraAndromeda held the guild thereafter: the thread's roster of September 2020 gives her as owner under the title "Empress", GrandAdmiralAce_ as "Crown Prince" and chief, and four more officers as a "Parliament" of barons and baronesses{{cite:thread-255067|post #1 (OP as last edited 16 Sep 2020)}}. The same roster claims membership of a "Wynnic Union community alliance"{{cite:thread-255067|post #1 (OP as last edited 16 Sep 2020); the alliance appears in no other archived source}}.

### The defection that decided a war (2019)

The Simple Ones signed the Treaty of Ternaves on 6 Jul 2019 with [[Kingdom Foxes]] and ThisIsMurica, splitting the territory of the dissolved Celestial Tigers.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Two months later came its decisive act in [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the alliance wars of 2019]]: on 8 Sep 2019, mid-war, it defected from Luna to [[Terra]] — and Terra took control of the map the same day.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} It then co-founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] on 15 Sep 2019, staying to its 23 Nov collapse, and co-founded [[Horologium]] on 1 Dec 2019, which died with [[DiamondDeities]]' disbandment on 8 Jan 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Empire of Nemract (2020-2021)

On 17 Aug 2020 The Simple Ones formed the [[Empire of Nemract]], a political union with Mystic Woods later branded 'The Empire of Nemract | ILQ + Aeu', whose empress held court titles ('Empress of Nemract, Queen of Aphelion').{{cite:thread-278123|Wynncraft forums thread 278123, Empire of Nemract branding}} The union was last mentioned in August 2021; the two guilds never fought each other, and the union may have persisted quietly.{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} On 21 May 2021 ILQ signed the Treaty of Damask, under which Nefarious Ravens declared independence.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The blocs (2021-2023)

The Simple Ones was a founding member of [[Valhalla]] on 11 May 2021 and followed it into [[Vanir]].{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} At the start of Season 8 (autumn 2022) it joined the renamed 'Smtn else' — later [[smtn elf]] — remaining until the alliance's quiet end in mid-2023.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}

