TherapueticLiz — the in-game name carries the transposed spelling "Therapuetic" — appears in the record with [[sins-of-seedia|Sins of Seedia]] from 2018, posting in the [[aesir-pact|Aesir Pact]] thread that June{{cite:thread-227373|posts #9, #12 and #17, 5 Jun 2018}} and writing in the Federation Tribute of 13 November 2018: "Glad I was apart of it for the entire ride. Kind of sad to see it end but nothing ever truly lasts."{{cite:thread-237070|post #4, 13 Nov 2018}}

On 26 June 2022 came the post that closed the public record. Correcting [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] — "Don't mean to necro, but a majority of the alliance info is incorrect. here's a list in case you want to update it" — the post set out [[cucumber-company|Cucumber Company]]'s fourteen guilds: [[aequitas|Aequitas]], [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]], [[avicia|Avicia]], Blacklisted, KongoBoys, Empire of Sindria, Gang of Fools, [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]], The Clowns, Nefarious Ravens, Sins of Seedia, [[the-aquarium|The Aquarium]], Wynn Legacy and [[profession-heaven|Profession Heaven]]{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}. Less than two weeks later [[sg-voltage|Sg_Voltage]] deleted the thread's alliance section{{cite:thread-278112-p09|p9 #161, 7 Jul 2022}}, and no alliance roster has been published publicly since. The same post recorded the retreat from the forums in miniature: "my guild has ceased recruiting through forums. We have an application process within our discord as many other guilds now do."{{cite:thread-278112-p08|p8 #160, 26 Jun 2022}}

She is also credited with the video "SMTN ELSE SLANDER" of 3 October 2022, made after the bloc renamed itself [[smtn-elf|smtn elf]]{{cite:youtube-com-watch-v-tfcs3b6emlq|"SMTN ELSE SLANDER", TherapueticLiz, uploaded 3 Oct 2022}} — leaving her chronicler of both the roster and its successor's mockery. As of September 2026 the Wynncraft API records her as Sins of Seedia's owner{{cite:wynncraft-api|Wynncraft API v3, guild/Sins of Seedia, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}}.

Thundderr was one of the two chiefs of [[kingdomphoenixes|KingdomPhoenixes]] under [[aurumkitsune|AurumKitsune]], styled "Prince of the Phoenixes" in the guild's monarchy-themed rank scheme, alongside "Princess Whimsy".{{cite:thread-204381|post #1 (OP), 24 Sep 2017}} The guild was established on 23 September 2017 and co-founded the [[Coalition]] with [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] weeks later.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L869}}

[[drew1011|Drew1011]] handed him [[holders-of-le|Holders of LE]] on 31 January 2018, posting on its new thread the same day: "Make me proud."{{cite:thread-217600|post #2, Drew1011, 31 Jan 2018}} Revived inside the Coalition, the guild was allotted 19 territories in the alliance's February 2018 division of the map,{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1044–1056}} and its May 2018 thread lists Thundderr as leader with [[kuroi|Kur0i]] and [[pillowpet|PillowPet]] — the guild's creator — still among its chiefs.{{cite:thread-217600|post #1, Thundderr, 10 May 2018}}

He told Drew1011 on 1 April 2018 that he was giving the guild up, and it went inactive from that point.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|L1154–1155}} Drew1011's Federation tribute thanks him "for allowing HoL to shine once more and for being there for us in the crucial beginning months".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

Writing in May 2018, Drew1011 credited him with "probably somewhere between 100-150 territories" across several guilds — an estimate offered before the rule against warring on multiple accounts existed.{{cite:drew1011-storytime|part 15, composed 20 May 2018}}

Titans Valor [ANO], created on 2 Jul 2017,{{cite:api-wynncraft-com-v3-guild-titans-20valor|creation date, retrieved 2 Sep 2026}} belonged to more alliances than almost any other guild - and documented much of that history itself through its newsletter, the [[titan-times|Titan Times]].

## History

### A community guild that took up warring (2017–18)

The guild described itself in December 2017 as one that "began as a community guild, although we have gotten more into warring, although Titans Valor will always be part community", valuing "loyalty, courage and respect"{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}. Its published rules bound members to the guild's diplomacy — "do not attack any guild in the alliance we are affiliated with, or if we have a pact of good terms" — and removed anyone inactive for more than two weeks{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}. The hierarchy then ran [[iceresistance|IceResistance]] as leader with KnixFice and AnDr3i_FTW as chiefs and advisers; by February 2018 the same three were styled Emperor and Consuls{{cite:thread-206094-p02|#34, 11 Dec 2017, quoting the opening post}}{{cite:thread-206094-p04|#73, 24 Feb 2018, quoting the opening post}}.

### Federation and the wars of 2019

Titans Valor cycled through [[the-federation|the Federation]] three times in 2018 (February-May, June-July, and September to the collapse).{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, 13 Nov 2018}}{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} In 2019 it appears to have fought with [[Terra]] against [[Luna]],{{cite:territory-exchanges|territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} co-founded the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]] on 15 Sep 2019, left on 21 Nov - two days before the alliance collapsed - and co-founded [[Horologium]] on 1 Dec 2019 with [[DiamondDeities]] and [[The Simple Ones]], which died with DiamondDeities' disbandment on 8 Jan 2020.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Hestia, Artemis, and the blocs of 2020-2021

From around mid-2020 Titans Valor belonged to the community alliance [[Hestia]]. By 2 Dec 2020 it was in [[Artemis]]: its own member [[paladinsorcerer|Pally]] wrote on [[the-forum-megalist|the megalist]] that 'ANO is apart of the alliances Hestia (a community alliance between ANO, ESI, LXA, and PUN) and Artemis (war alliance) made up of all the current massive land holding guilds on the map'.{{cite:thread-278112|post #10, 2 Dec 2020}} The guild stayed through [[the-great-collapse|the Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021 into [[Valhalla]] and [[Vanir]], and fought the ex-Valhalla side of [[valhalla-khaos-war|the Khaos war]] into 2022.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}} Pally restated the Hestia roster on the megalist on 6 Jun 2021.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|p7 #140, 6 Jun 2021}}

### The realignment and Adonis (2022-2024)

Titans Valor joined [[Cucumber Company]] for Season 5, which ran from 3 Mar to 2 May 2022 - its newsletter's first volume (8 May 2022) records 'our first season being a part of the new Cucumber Company war alliance'{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} - and carried into [[smtn elf]] until that alliance's quiet death in mid-2023.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}} Around May 2022 its leaders and Empire of Sindria's founded [[Adonis]] as Hestia declined, 'a space for those of us who are still active to hang together';{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol1|vol. 1, 8 May 2022}} Adonis was still active in March 2024.{{cite:chronicle-records|Chronicle alliance and event records}}

![Territory-map excerpt from Titan Times vol. 13 (22 March 2024) marking out Titans Valor's 'Jungle FFA' course through nine numbered ANO-held territories in Season 17; neighbouring holdings tagged TAq, AVO and DFS are visible around them.](/images/chronicles/media/titans-valor-1c6832fa.webp){{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol13|vol. 13, 22 Mar 2024}}

### Ownership

[[iceresistance|IceResistance]] founded the guild and opened its recruitment thread on 15 Oct 2017,{{cite:thread-206094|post #1, opened 15 Oct 2017}} and was still speaking for it politically in December 2020. By October 2022 he was on hiatus,{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}} and by March 2023 he was the guild's founder and previous owner{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}} - ownership changed hands at some point between those dates, and the successor was not named at the time.

In a November 2025 interview with Lamplesspost, the guild's leader Calluum - a Sage Council member back in vol. 1 - described his succession: 'No one else wanted it when pally was stepping down, so I realised I'd need to step up and take on the mantle.'{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol20|vol. 20, 23 Nov 2025}} Pally - apparently ANO's [[paladinsorcerer|PaladinSorcerer]] - led the guild before Calluum, who led it by November 2025. Whether Pally took over directly from IceResistance, and when either handover happened, was never recorded.

IceResistance remained a public voice for the guild long after leaving the ownership: his October 2025 forum remark that real diplomacy 'happens in private alliance chats' names the defining fact of [[private-diplomacy-era|the private-diplomacy era]].{{cite:thread-322643|post #1, 2 Oct 2025}}

### Later years (2024-2026)

Titan Times ran to vol. 21 on 18 May 2026,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol21|vol. 21, 18 May 2026}} but from vol. 14 onward it names no alliance at all, reporting only guild-internal affairs: the guild reached level 105 in mid-2024,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol15|vol. 15, 5 Aug 2024}} placed fifth on the Season 21 leaderboard and sixth in Season 22,{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol17|vol. 17}}{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol18|vol. 18}} and continued its internal Ocean Trials war rankings through Season 29.{{cite:titansvalor-org-news-vol21|vol. 21, 18 May 2026}}

